[{"sha":"23b83ad50f63d241d0069a3dc426d43b211adf2e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDIzYjgzYWQ1MGY2M2QyNDFkMDA2OWEzZGM0MjZkNDNiMjExYWRmMmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T21:14:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T21:14:50Z"},"message":"feat(code): add `editable` trace metadata (#5737)\n\nDeep Agents Code traces now expose whether the client is an editable\ninstall as a filterable boolean.\n\n---\n\nTrace consumers currently must parse `lc_versions[\"deepagents-code\"]`\nfor a `+editable` suffix. `build_stream_config` now emits an\nalways-present `editable` boolean derived from the same cached PEP 610\nlookup, keeping both values consistent.\n\nTests: focused metadata contract and stream-config tests; `make\nformat_diff`; `make lint_diff`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6e666be6-44be-5afd-abb0-945fac4d7912)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac5089a522457731e576e63b5562d120f3b74c40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ac5089a522457731e576e63b5562d120f3b74c40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/23b83ad50f63d241d0069a3dc426d43b211adf2e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiL/KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzpEQAANjbhkcXIoJFqH39o1oWT9g\nRzOpCNzI1NGoWtVtf8hPcbOR7djgjWgTSwaPyRG6G0C6d8wTze63CTMBZCvG8iv3\nsgVhCUykr48wVSwrbpQO+J7Gk1t2UHykbTLqxrLHUlrQP662weuzrzvq93k2gBo/\n/INN8QVAfKiJvmibmjv3gL412pVeR2/1uE+aPTjwiecYO/Dpl6exEmIesRLewJDV\nxfCqBnK9pNfo6LwFbs4e3G9Reha4gMHeDEMXsRt+t8Ik1e+6yLTWEi/nD8BKSrcK\nxcM3IesSDvLk//iuIUvIWn73R7yRk54QaKrl7+bn9ndMrBfV8KrmmL4zSQpgLICG\nqmEzJWUIJu2j2ePrfQuAY86nEpaGadbQC+A3qRJNwixkTencXX/fJ99BZyJvIozP\nDWnWCKxSZAGPdyX6xkOEuxB90jSVRrRilDfi6H4bOGStybUZ8+HuwjkBe8vgfhs5\nZEpFHqd23TPbSfmBYnW77Dk5gNgEy3zsv5iHbkYuKIzaAYQ4I1kndRwl79lWx6+T\nNeiz0MTuMIFH1bz5uyksRoxpRcv6W4PXMEWGPIhax8MGobqdxRiTPbCcV6vBjGeQ\nelMul2D55NKhi65bSRACwUfo5+QJjSVWZvh+4uLl9Ifyc2K7A/W7GDuYbacrbA+J\nZ11ApXpdiERvtNhHqkcA\n=9kHQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ac5089a522457731e576e63b5562d120f3b74c40\nparent e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787346890 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787346890 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add `editable` trace metadata (#5737)\n\nDeep Agents Code traces now expose whether the client is an editable\ninstall as a filterable boolean.\n\n---\n\nTrace consumers currently must parse `lc_versions[\"deepagents-code\"]`\nfor a `+editable` suffix. `build_stream_config` now emits an\nalways-present `editable` boolean derived from the same cached PEP 610\nlookup, keeping both values consistent.\n\nTests: focused metadata contract and stream-config tests; `make\nformat_diff`; `make lint_diff`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6e666be6-44be-5afd-abb0-945fac4d7912)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T21:14:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/23b83ad50f63d241d0069a3dc426d43b211adf2e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/23b83ad50f63d241d0069a3dc426d43b211adf2e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/23b83ad50f63d241d0069a3dc426d43b211adf2e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686"}]},{"sha":"e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUwNTkzMWIzMDE2ZWQzZDE1MDBkZjBjNWI3NzQwMmY0NTdlZTU2ODY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T21:01:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T21:01:09Z"},"message":"fix(code): extend text selection with `Shift` + `click` (#5732)\n\n<kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>click</kbd> now extends an existing text\nselection from its original anchor.\n\n**Known limitation:** this only works when the terminal delivers the\nmodified click to the app. Ghostty binds <kbd>Shift</kbd> +\n<kbd>click</kbd> to its own selection and never forwards the event while\nmouse reporting is active, so it's a no-op there (users can `keybind =\nshift+click=unbind` to opt out). Verified working in iTerm2; kitty and\nWezTerm also forward the shift modifier bit.\n\n---\n\nTextual resets selection state on every mouse press. This preserves the\nprior selection anchor for modified clicks while retaining stock\nbehavior when no selection exists or the target is not selectable.\nRegression tests cover forward, backward, and multi-widget ranges.\n\nThe rebuilt selection state can field-match the finished drag selection,\nwhich Textual reactives treat as unchanged — so the patch invokes the\n(patched, now-async) select-state watcher directly to repaint the\nhighlight. The module docstring documents the terminal-delivery\nlimitation for maintainers.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4d90066c-60b9-51ed-b7a3-cce83ee4fd0b)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6db4e6cfb092d9bc4f0375bf916a0cd0833c27bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6db4e6cfb092d9bc4f0375bf916a0cd0833c27bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiLyVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIiYQAH+w70NUy9XYIjqm/UOJUtXh\n+baKzAH6T4GfC+v4EETgJao5x4xTXgfUj2KM1hk7LoV+B1qo0sN8FVaq0IxqsTGa\nUcpBdUH2WlqgtxzeH5uBZ9lqOTa00dldyYIFelS6PJTmhWLju+ImWpaGBR4Ot75q\nbvzjfGMbJXLQ95UIkrD44q9uhaQ6Pb3aYMKFCbRPpwBYfdAngtIi5WbI9hxoMGBo\nlQvKUSwpaOxfA2E72yW+Xtrrw62BQ6CN+2D2Xaf3pLNd9f17yElFH0Zo18xQxIfE\npVo1Zvhp5eX2iJ2RB5hn8B7BUmR8JJJTb5awCd+cHQLC+uke5XblA1OSAOqiiqWv\nahmi5ey4sGpo+TbAQRZhZ0zAHqETFn6GqePe1J8NvOUTROwTQbRFfG4hMrJ/aQBe\nu40Uwkp3Xonv+PIMmiysnfPfdMQeiRyGtjjPewnGBJlFqyhgnzQfXj1+twZRdjYF\n6rziqEL3oWFhKObVjIQoPws4yVr1jNZfoJziaHTJQEXmbqKpJAUhvRu/h/TobObi\nIECuzugcak9G3WqNIYp4mEyoKADnLZ+yZlw+bDdJvTN9nObJIp/Gh69L15kAmdZy\nhlSpjFVwcOPwVb0rDFUDe72oB8w4oviWr38kVqd6gXrHnDzS+lVUAcM1oI14HVie\nJnMx5l6EpiCPx8FP2OSS\n=gNLt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6db4e6cfb092d9bc4f0375bf916a0cd0833c27bc\nparent 5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787346069 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787346069 -0400\n\nfix(code): extend text selection with `Shift` + `click` (#5732)\n\n<kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>click</kbd> now extends an existing text\nselection from its original anchor.\n\n**Known limitation:** this only works when the terminal delivers the\nmodified click to the app. Ghostty binds <kbd>Shift</kbd> +\n<kbd>click</kbd> to its own selection and never forwards the event while\nmouse reporting is active, so it's a no-op there (users can `keybind =\nshift+click=unbind` to opt out). Verified working in iTerm2; kitty and\nWezTerm also forward the shift modifier bit.\n\n---\n\nTextual resets selection state on every mouse press. This preserves the\nprior selection anchor for modified clicks while retaining stock\nbehavior when no selection exists or the target is not selectable.\nRegression tests cover forward, backward, and multi-widget ranges.\n\nThe rebuilt selection state can field-match the finished drag selection,\nwhich Textual reactives treat as unchanged — so the patch invokes the\n(patched, now-async) select-state watcher directly to repaint the\nhighlight. The module docstring documents the terminal-delivery\nlimitation for maintainers.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4d90066c-60b9-51ed-b7a3-cce83ee4fd0b)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T21:01:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e05931b3016ed3d1500df0c5b77402f457ee5686/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f"}]},{"sha":"5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDUzOTc4MTJhZDVmMjE3Y2Q4NGY4NzFmMTIxY2Y5ZWE4ZjNkNjNmNGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T20:52:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T20:52:22Z"},"message":"fix(code): remove notification settings expand flicker and trailing disclosure glyph (#5734)\n\nPressing Enter on \"Notification settings\" no longer opens the pane with\na beat of unselected content and a late-arriving footer hint, and the\ntrailing triangle no longer flips between glyphs as the section opens\nand closes — the leading cursor now carries the disclosure state.\n\n---\n\nTwo papercuts from #5698:\n\n**Lag before the footer hints update.** The app constructs the center\nwithout the suppressed-keys snapshot, so the first expand read\n`config.toml` (four `asyncio.to_thread` calls) before mounting any\ncheckboxes, focusing the first one, or refreshing the footer. The pane\nwas visibly open but nothing was selected, and only then did the hint\nswitch to \"Space/Enter toggle\" — a one-frame flicker. The screen now\npreloads the suppressed keys in a background worker when it mounts, and\n`_expand_settings` flips the expanded state, disclosure glyph, and\nfooter hint synchronously before its first await, so the expanded hints\nrender in the same frame the pane opens. A rapid Esc during an in-flight\nread both collapses the section and stops the expand worker from\nreopening it.\n\n**Trailing disclosure triangle.** The `▸`/`▾` after \"Notification\nsettings\" is removed. The leading glyph carries the state instead: `›`\nwhen the row is selected and collapsed (Enter opens), `▾` whenever the\nsection is expanded (Esc collapses).","tree":{"sha":"d8e0193d838e791febf5b526a23e21284842c4e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d8e0193d838e791febf5b526a23e21284842c4e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiLqGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEPEQAEGpej0qWbTZmzHPyL/8svA4\nxZ5mWXY0sWMWzgun/hgJdVosgJFOXVg9iAb0gAcgugtVh1V9jzKHSGo5QzgtTfrA\n8DsYu0atnGi37GKlly+Ft0ZQrOPcSdmI1URf0qeAeiFXzhAZK/9WDbhOmPLsaYzT\nDV37X3c91QG5PcT1Sb5E8Pvueh5Kz5cFZb/D2SmD4ElwsJlrvWQ+QhDRQ8kdo+jB\nUCqjR19EjYSB1cBB2PRYuLSeOuSE7UkUhQt5ovsY76PIL9gKHXU9MLTZdji30R7I\nzvbFm1hVSgDG0rAzDn0lmAKoiwtrdQDC63Kdx0izn5LDvTi6qld2W3CjfZ4ESxa/\nZHAJjrvrRGs8j57oN372aUh3NKbyxzDptB84yXRKsDt32uCAguZkb4cOnOq1D4Ky\n8JDkyFpgFcjlTK74Ih5ZdbG9IVUJeRevDn0VKgwHWk3ErS6lBlDUxM086f0nUYsc\nMaiPfHvabVeXGggoMNF6G201Ro1FioVVkzNJR087iJCGS6wNqF1hnFHdGpFFb0Hb\n+5Wyy6vBz9JzRoz6tr5Hh4a8wJwjtWT6iEfv0X3LzgUQSJZ0aHOiYB5sYf/N4/VN\n4uZ8tbkVAGrS+/9g1Rij393+ZBGbraDrJjBRMRU8mBU6BIwGB7tdFWfi2vBmm4hp\nsBaI1WjWTx9lfr2YulSJ\n=TRnj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d8e0193d838e791febf5b526a23e21284842c4e0\nparent 85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787345542 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787345542 -0400\n\nfix(code): remove notification settings expand flicker and trailing disclosure glyph (#5734)\n\nPressing Enter on \"Notification settings\" no longer opens the pane with\na beat of unselected content and a late-arriving footer hint, and the\ntrailing triangle no longer flips between glyphs as the section opens\nand closes — the leading cursor now carries the disclosure state.\n\n---\n\nTwo papercuts from #5698:\n\n**Lag before the footer hints update.** The app constructs the center\nwithout the suppressed-keys snapshot, so the first expand read\n`config.toml` (four `asyncio.to_thread` calls) before mounting any\ncheckboxes, focusing the first one, or refreshing the footer. The pane\nwas visibly open but nothing was selected, and only then did the hint\nswitch to \"Space/Enter toggle\" — a one-frame flicker. The screen now\npreloads the suppressed keys in a background worker when it mounts, and\n`_expand_settings` flips the expanded state, disclosure glyph, and\nfooter hint synchronously before its first await, so the expanded hints\nrender in the same frame the pane opens. A rapid Esc during an in-flight\nread both collapses the section and stops the expand worker from\nreopening it.\n\n**Trailing disclosure triangle.** The `▸`/`▾` after \"Notification\nsettings\" is removed. The leading glyph carries the state instead: `›`\nwhen the row is selected and collapsed (Enter opens), `▾` whenever the\nsection is expanded (Esc collapses).","verified_at":"2026-08-21T20:52:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5397812ad5f217cd84f871f121cf9ea8f3d63f4f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430"}]},{"sha":"85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg1YzY4MzM3MzRhNTQ3ZTk2ODIyMWMxMTk5YTc2OWQ3YWFjNjk0MzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T20:25:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T20:25:05Z"},"message":"fix(code): standardize modal navigation hints (#5699)\n\nModal footers now consistently advertise forward and reverse Tab\nnavigation, with specialized hints where Tab autocompletes, jumps\nservers, or switches tabs.\n\n---\n\nCentralizes the standard copy, fixes app-level Shift+Tab routing for the\neffort and launch preference selectors, and keeps the MCP footer compact\nenough to preserve list navigation at standard terminal sizes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1e0aca0d-8819-5754-acdc-4a08b1b2ac0c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"883a98f1164832105103356fd1b6ca68fe586080","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/883a98f1164832105103356fd1b6ca68fe586080"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiLQhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArQoQAJ0buxVWYC+3aSMdPur3MEFk\nL1wAwGiagC9ISZ5ZHS0gyrw5vWjUaGAHH66OOXgkqc8BTgvfe+z89ClkdGMdW9eh\na5WdfA0OCaw87LvCW3cxV+oMyJRHGYA2YqcAYlul7go2b1EU7DJxoq3ZoC0gyGHC\niY3Ie+oCDAvYMeVFuG/9y+uZ1X0wseGXDDbi1HUNtkFhRTVv+Pe/No+rOsnyhPpI\nE2+OlAl22Qf3U45m1hgEoguDx1uaGDrPKhLQpJhvbb10CuQ1SXPdEfPm+HEWPUjo\neMMLyDTR3HG2fwG2STqdhEd2lzIOvqi5CYovLT/f4DAD1u3BUuVN8PfJ81SIqN15\ncSNsJqUBA9ZeTsmb87PhkiH9XcLY2MRJx1QtXfZKDA9E+2+intSKDqS+cIqX/3fp\n2Sxxfmc0vUjNxS2hr5XnqmtvDqEK8iBCxf+mZ4BV9eKCzSeu3LF2Gm5mwdDHNWaO\nrdqrQHpagupHxDkZiuw3yvkE/0WrIQbhOTEjmS6tQ++Z9jkx0io1jpH2GEigjC+g\nRnCpJ1cDGP7RoXBS9rvgBL6HR/9mGn7iqqhrhWHEIPIhPl4FtWHYFOQLZeWjRdCj\n8Vx6AqwEXRstM/NLeB1GMQgzdASp9StAkTJID9MCBjp71kNwSrEesoYWUfbwl2lg\n4xO2+yyVYG/hOwz0MOrB\n=Rqi0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 883a98f1164832105103356fd1b6ca68fe586080\nparent 3ac059e1574963fe216692642aa1b1a4044daaa9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787343905 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787343905 -0400\n\nfix(code): standardize modal navigation hints (#5699)\n\nModal footers now consistently advertise forward and reverse Tab\nnavigation, with specialized hints where Tab autocompletes, jumps\nservers, or switches tabs.\n\n---\n\nCentralizes the standard copy, fixes app-level Shift+Tab routing for the\neffort and launch preference selectors, and keeps the MCP footer compact\nenough to preserve list navigation at standard terminal sizes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1e0aca0d-8819-5754-acdc-4a08b1b2ac0c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T20:25:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/85c6833734a547e968221c1199a769d7aac69430/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"co