nchanged.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9670a6fbc8bd29e45649f3dabe89583a9572c9db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9670a6fbc8bd29e45649f3dabe89583a9572c9db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9767f420c622a31a7511c4601739534ddc6062a7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiKWECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATI0QAJ7LSoBdHOhTToLVtTXgVQFF\n8apEiuXMLZCGvZHRnWY9Fqt3bZdw0UueyinZx7FWubLEzZc/V7ntSU8n8rMQwTm1\n68duq4OoV2YjUx7ffqqV7W6aZjOTvQvZa0vN2OLueZ8oxNXvP2pWY0aC07C3aDNV\n0yDZPCHQVroVtNPxdcLs4suBfdvJL1TXv9Ope9ryZG4143NHt0xUMT6eh+UiyGub\nhXwm90iy00Jt4k3BoX8os9Rtfkx5lb+Cc1yObFEK7EedWshfrM/SWxe42vvBv1bw\nVzNpZrgYlxcGRIYDCJl0nD1lknvVdxBQLKPLU4+Oof8bwhGMF0voYyIwoXEXpNkN\nMFiEQn5WsOcsnVcx22ZErK/hfZ5NR8OU035ABs+9H5gl4CpoWUOpHmo4R/qt49C4\nY7rJjsy8LHlyju9PMKqOiNSc4XPFEycYaxIiTsHayHdSEaDuYjJ0/JaZydtQt1KF\nUPdWTAnvKB5wj6mQrMojPJXv5IzVB3sVjw62uRMZEesmCeCPUJcQDMvOqOunOTnf\nvOx47yxkQywr7++aFgEIX6kIyGN9oDkqxa/3mLhNs2mbo+U3nm3VF+VjZsbGYRBq\nmh7V/XaH9heQo2bfncz9MqY2S2wh7ve27zxsmd9e2ojNLedsAKKbY/e6EpUqcIYH\nBxoFW++AuhiJNdMRVNXA\n=mKQI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9670a6fbc8bd29e45649f3dabe89583a9572c9db\nparent 074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787340164 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787340164 -0400\n\nfeat(code): unify notification center and settings (#5698)\n\n`Ctrl+N` and `/notifications` now open one notification hub where\nwarning settings expand inline under a \"Notification settings\"\ndisclosure row, alongside pending notices — including when the inbox is\nempty.\n\n---\n\nThis removes the separate warning-preferences modal. Toggling the\nsettings row mounts the warning checkboxes directly inside the hub, so\npreferences never leave the notices list and closing them just collapses\nthe section. Existing notification detail, suppression, and in-place\naction flows are unchanged.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T19:22:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9767f420c622a31a7511c4601739534ddc6062a7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9767f420c622a31a7511c4601739534ddc6062a7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9767f420c622a31a7511c4601739534ddc6062a7/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1"}]},{"sha":"074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA3NGE1MDE5ZTFmM2VkZmQ1ODk2MTQ3NzQ5NTg0MDBkMDUxZTVmZTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T19:03:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T19:03:56Z"},"message":"fix(code): show contextual auth footer actions (#5690)\n\nThe `/auth` manager footer now names the action for the highlighted row\ninstead of listing every action the screen supports.\n\nBefore, one line had to cover every row:\n\n```\n↑/↓ or Tab/Shift+Tab navigate • Enter add/replace/delete/install • Esc close\n```\n\nNow the action follows the cursor:\n\n| Highlighted row | Footer |\n| --- | --- |\n| `anthropic  [env set: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY]` | `Enter replace` |\n| `openai  [stored]` | `Enter replace/delete` |\n| `tavily` | `Enter add` |\n| `groq  [not installed]` | `Enter install` |\n| `OpenAI Codex (ChatGPT login)  [chatgpt: plus]` | `Enter manage` |\n\n---\n\n**An expired ChatGPT access token counts as signed in.** Expiry is the\nnormal state for a returning user: the saved refresh token renews the\naccess token when a model is constructed, which is why\n`_get_codex_auth_status` reports the row as `CONFIGURED` and badges it\n`[chatgpt]`. The footer reads that same status, so the badge, the\nfooter, and Enter agree. Treating expiry as signed-out would have told\nthe user to re-authorize a session that never lapsed, and would have\nhidden sign-out — which only the signed-in overlay offers — behind that\nunnecessary OAuth round trip.\n\nReading the cached status also means highlighting a row never touches\nthe token file. Arrowing over the ChatGPT row used to read\n`chatgpt-auth.json` on every keypress.\n\n**A stored key with no known env var offers replace/delete.** The set of\nproviders with a credential in `auth.json` is snapshotted when the\noption list is built. Without it, a provider whose env var is absent\nfrom `PROVIDER_API_KEY_ENV` — a custom `class_path` provider, or a\nwell-known one renamed across an upgrade — resolved to `UNKNOWN` and the\nfooter said `add`, while the prompt behind Enter offered `Ctrl+D delete`\nfor the key it had just denied existed.\n\n**The footer follows the row, not the cursor index.** `_refresh_options`\npreserves the highlighted index while configured rows float to the top,\nso saving or deleting a key changes which provider sits under an unmoved\ncursor. The rebuild recomputes the footer from the row that ended up\nthere.\n\nBoth footer writers share one helper that tolerates a dismissed manager.\nA queued `OptionHighlighted` can arrive after the screen is gone, where\nan unguarded `query_one` raises `NoMatches` and Textual escalates it\ninto a callback error that tears down the REPL.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d9dd1ec2-f3c6-5ff0-aaa2-da82e97fcbc7)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab81c373d68dd916d953a779d87f1a5cfd08f54e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ab81c373d68dd916d953a779d87f1a5cfd08f54e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiKEcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArYsQACPy8FhMuAOK0ObJviktiM3x\nNvLdy1XztBbhvbCRZg077krkcic+/++/1Sbx0YYacleJHAfx+8ZQGw2wcvBjTlMu\nmLcJbcg+ydID48cTs1/iae//94FrJhnKfsxlvXOuFkdxEjj+Ot7j4pLS4m+7GgPR\nQA6WkNcfnCNW9vKmezHV1RSWYquFKtm0SLsIMbBYrrr4fnlxzzZJ3Fxau+hW0DV2\nx4lDseLfndDJ5pxLDC/bSHYzgpEtcEvZ5DVEmRxLGF/2XNS1wmOBLKEqMicBfWyw\n4hDb3u2fNZwAIJrPoTLMyOjCOFQB19twXUW/g0q0iuv0zEPROebl6SuiW7B720b0\n6GVlcY4ExqA5CIEEtl4yygBOUfBZ2pW3hYhvmYLtS0quub85Vc5VMithSgYsPOcC\nuiq5FJk5wpTOH4+Noi8NEKAneqBw5p/KHgwuGTKXXmW+UVE0Re0gRQAjlMN0hlz+\nsRVxYJdjclSVeUhPhprTpb7oOVq+xdiM4WROegNuV7Qgsn6pPo8ZGAqlCpJoz9hO\nm7wWP3zC0Hk3U9yAvLfM+JFFlwiSG+aBfzB7kKhrlqnObxq9sced05FpqhGdFhTb\nV2BqwNsgNK4lRqJkKZ4XGGQhXeutHagthL/+mYaa7nfZZnykpMZrju42HJRbBeTx\n4qtgpGUTx9YZKwH4W/o/\n=hWTJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ab81c373d68dd916d953a779d87f1a5cfd08f54e\nparent 1f7495949232fe2e3e3328b6ff9054c202002f95\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787339036 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787339036 -0400\n\nfix(code): show contextual auth footer actions (#5690)\n\nThe `/auth` manager footer now names the action for the highlighted row\ninstead of listing every action the screen supports.\n\nBefore, one line had to cover every row:\n\n```\n↑/↓ or Tab/Shift+Tab navigate • Enter add/replace/delete/install • Esc close\n```\n\nNow the action follows the cursor:\n\n| Highlighted row | Footer |\n| --- | --- |\n| `anthropic  [env set: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY]` | `Enter replace` |\n| `openai  [stored]` | `Enter replace/delete` |\n| `tavily` | `Enter add` |\n| `groq  [not installed]` | `Enter install` |\n| `OpenAI Codex (ChatGPT login)  [chatgpt: plus]` | `Enter manage` |\n\n---\n\n**An expired ChatGPT access token counts as signed in.** Expiry is the\nnormal state for a returning user: the saved refresh token renews the\naccess token when a model is constructed, which is why\n`_get_codex_auth_status` reports the row as `CONFIGURED` and badges it\n`[chatgpt]`. The footer reads that same status, so the badge, the\nfooter, and Enter agree. Treating expiry as signed-out would have told\nthe user to re-authorize a session that never lapsed, and would have\nhidden sign-out — which only the signed-in overlay offers — behind that\nunnecessary OAuth round trip.\n\nReading the cached status also means highlighting a row never touches\nthe token file. Arrowing over the ChatGPT row used to read\n`chatgpt-auth.json` on every keypress.\n\n**A stored key with no known env var offers replace/delete.** The set of\nproviders with a credential in `auth.json` is snapshotted when the\noption list is built. Without it, a provider whose env var is absent\nfrom `PROVIDER_API_KEY_ENV` — a custom `class_path` provider, or a\nwell-known one renamed across an upgrade — resolved to `UNKNOWN` and the\nfooter said `add`, while the prompt behind Enter offered `Ctrl+D delete`\nfor the key it had just denied existed.\n\n**The footer follows the row, not the cursor index.** `_refresh_options`\npreserves the highlighted index while configured rows float to the top,\nso saving or deleting a key changes which provider sits under an unmoved\ncursor. The rebuild recomputes the footer from the row that ended up\nthere.\n\nBoth footer writers share one helper that tolerates a dismissed manager.\nA queued `OptionHighlighted` can arrive after the screen is gone, where\nan unguarded `query_one` raises `NoMatches` and Textual escalates it\ninto a callback error that tears down the REPL.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d9dd1ec2-f3c6-5ff0-aaa2-da82e97fcbc7)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T19:03:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/074a5019e1f3edfd589614774958400d051e5fe1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1f749594923