ctHc0twrBslOF5UxzRYUtC6\n/h4kV3DKvOW3dQVYzmqmGm8ovYPV2gUEgcGjv5RrMEUAy5I+gGfEJg82N2Q+9klY\ndT9z8/v/xzkjwX13QpvTg48oQPpytVoaq+BxEVhm+4MuWjRLAKZlv85CLfd7RgoA\nuFPN94HRneL72GMlQv8ViGwO4wx4HzXXAeVyLX52Qg5R0eoCtssLbZUoKpW0gv9Z\nsxNyYNWTXRWGc88fSaBk\n=RSdm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 250de771a9f1b96c5115693e2ea5c088c364f085\nparent c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787338991 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787338991 -0400\n\nfix(code): align wrapped debug snapshot values (#5727)\n\nWrapped Debug Console snapshot values now align with the start of their\nvalue column.\n\n---\n\nLong snapshot values previously wrapped at the modal's left edge, making\nlabels hard to scan. The snapshot view now applies a hanging indent\nwhile preserving copy and link spans.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/88a043f9-b5fc-5cea-9ade-548ea4d3c0dc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T19:03:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1f7495949232fe2e3e3328b6ff9054c202002f95","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1f7495949232fe2e3e3328b6ff9054c202002f95","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1f7495949232fe2e3e3328b6ff9054c202002f95/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2"}]},{"sha":"c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM3MmFjYzI4M2IxN2JjOTRmYzI2MTJhZGZhZTM1NzY3ZjM4MTBjYzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T18:37:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T18:37:04Z"},"message":"style(code): update resize handle after theme changes (#5664)\n\nThe chat input's draggable top bar now follows the active theme whenever\n`/theme` changes it.\n\n---\n\nThe resize handle uses an inline color so hover feedback survives\ncaptured drags, but that color was only refreshed for mode and hover\nchanges. Watching Textual's app theme keeps the existing mode-aware\nstyling synchronized without changing resize behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/23698746-0a5b-561b-8353-5799c952bbe7)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c075daffe333adc0a3a92d41daf9752b2bf8625","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6c075daffe333adc0a3a92d41daf9752b2bf8625"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiJrQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdd8QAJCpdicCz2rLra+l07nQit9d\nWW5arlbZcr5WtYTGFgpaMVEeh0s9N/t9PJhz6XAFYgjfiImxZQ0KRMM5Yemq5ulS\n66tEHyzF6VCD/QE5hzJ2K/BNO5qb3sq2LCjizBt3ozYNrKhLlL08IJpBku5yT4W3\nsqT0CBIt5RsgSwg2ObRU8qxPhhIVGczeX9JzOkb9/jQNVJE9hxau/M+0eEDR1yiY\nVoDCUZ0hgfRLB0N8/ksrohtBG37sYYVcwl6PIsOde3RtgcF18PHruinfuSMUYel2\nvMjTPvvzS/BhQc72SfVLmgcAz6wqdgaEe/DLH2Q8b0T3nMHQz1J4mn4UO5BmjrpP\nA0PqxBjfccz1ldcoXO7+ng2JVOwVGzvlxa10dMMFdBEkGk8+kJHXm1IDfCzCoAg5\npt8yyg4k2FtSy4PnQrNOvrEwGcQRh4JUxoVa8+8d9owAE0eT0PlSJPc/M1XAb9o8\np1ns7EcwzthWw4a8I3JXrYrrEP7A285OeF82PrfEz9eiu4FGMM8hNWGgStVGdVmb\nR0vIkexVRUgjcbd96qSAHN0qaWXXc18UPlT1D+Apf1/44suPL5IMe++mFFqJ1TB5\nzSZKeNCQ8lQwGVpd2YhkfGi0Jb3zc84TwK+wh4qoPCL8ro/Adps2SlhCg3NiGNdm\nbKnBEtbk6qTdY8Zqchp8\n=1wAj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6c075daffe333adc0a3a92d41daf9752b2bf8625\nparent d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787337424 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787337424 -0400\n\nstyle(code): update resize handle after theme changes (#5664)\n\nThe chat input's draggable top bar now follows the active theme whenever\n`/theme` changes it.\n\n---\n\nThe resize handle uses an inline color so hover feedback survives\ncaptured drags, but that color was only refreshed for mode and hover\nchanges. Watching Textual's app theme keeps the existing mode-aware\nstyling synchronized without changing resize behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/23698746-0a5b-561b-8353-5799c952bbe7)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T18:37:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c72acc283b17bc94fc2612adfae35767f3810cc2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425"}]},{"sha":"d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ3MTFiYzYxMzAwMDkwMTgxZGM4OWUzZTExNmU4YjM0M2ZiNjU0MjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T18:35:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T18:35:43Z"},"message":"feat(code): highlight shell commands in the chat input (#5675)\n\nShell command modes now highlight Bash syntax as users type, including\nincognito mode.\n\n---\n\nInspired by Toad’s shell-mode UX, this is independently implemented with\nTextual’s public highlighter API.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e838fab2-9289-5b71-92ca-85585bcbbe0b)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"966801520e5f25fb547fc092bd4acd6b5d42df2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/966801520e5f25fb547fc092bd4acd6b5d42df2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiJp/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIrQQAFJvYC+v8j+ZIgJgR9ZUVu/O\nPbb8lyEItpGqUyu/IgO6d+s8Uk08tLUibloPQSENzBPhKo/TXh9ZYG67UOM5yuxk\nUvG36PtYtgvuGGVMvHp/uR8iuuoD+CQf0qYSLZ4imrkkVJ78BFoZt7TbQv/zK3YL\nZQaM1AesMBfViXndqkN5phwK0pVE44uujy54NlACBzAT36goz5CnMMJGOOrOX4BL\n2JJUvQlbLqZJoc99ENM/SYEYEnXiOSv+9qJ7BbJClR2FDwbJ/EkezLMamZfJDkV5\nTlT8fzcwMz4nwT7OHXiJyJYl/jjvkkG4u55oq9uwM8XgjpnXKRyvg2DaP9/6W8hp\nRmEKdGLX1aeodVUhXYn3WuAwHUn1hHhadBsMS/SeS5U682/e9nMJNRFaHf+fcrXB\nZ5FiAKZnjAtkmLwJcPI/UnEmEhuci8A2sGFhovItEtXG6Vra23GLbN1S0f5LshpY\ni4lZ7U4k0Y13Ft3hIythOVUKga4FhOdGNZ/52r2X6aHP+RRGEvcMJ5fr+WmzVCfi\ngN9v/kGneIktGJbVTQV/P2Gsn/IhgqyRmSxXbQqYoBEHwxt3UitSc9UZ9sIgkMFi\nZXKHT8wSGNpzQuB/HLkGeAsFu/509vV5MLbodohe9FaDrEDSMBjN2bf/dX4rvDWM\n6vYCB2moM0r5MgRycRji\n=b6B9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 966801520e5f25fb547fc092bd4acd6b5d42df2f\nparent d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787337343 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787337343 -0400\n\nfeat(code): highlight shell commands in the chat input (#5675)\n\nShell command modes now highlight Bash syntax as users type, including\nincognito mode.\n\n---\n\nInspired by Toad’s shell-mode UX, this is independently implemented with\nTextual’s public highlighter API.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e838fab2-9289-5b71-92ca-85585bcbbe0b)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T18:35:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d711bc61300090181dc89e3e116e8b343fb65425/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc"}]},{"sha":"d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ1MDA1ZDNjYzllNTczNWI4OGViNzc3NzkyMDU5NzZlMTI1M2YwYmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T18:34:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T18:34:36Z"},"message":"refactor(code): validate `ask_user` args with pydantic instead of a custom error (#5682)\n\nA malformed `ask_user` call still surfaces to the model as a retryable\nerror `ToolMessage`. The validation now lives on the tool's pydantic\nschema. The hand-rolled validation function, the `ToolErrorMiddleware`,\nthe `ToolArgumentError` type, the `on_error` handler, and the scope list\nare all deleted.\n\n## The rules on the schema\n\nPer-field, on `Question`:\n\n- `question` has an `AfterValidator` that rejects blank and\nwhitespace-only text. The field keeps `min_length=1`, but that\nconstrains only the JSON schema the model reads. The validator is the\ninner annotation, so it runs first and is the only runtime gate.\n- `type` stays a `Literal`. `required` stays a strict bool.\n- Each `Choice` has an `AfterValidator` that rejects a blank `value`. A\nblank value renders as an unlabelled option whose answer reads as \"no\nanswer\".\n\nCross-field, on the `ValidatedQuestion` alias and the `questions`\nparameter:\n\n- A choice question must have a non-empty `choices` list.\n- A non-choice question must not have `choices`.\n- `questions` must not be empty.\n\n`AskUserRequest.questions` is `list[ValidatedQuestion]` too. The\ncross-field rules then also apply where `tui.textual_adapter`\nre-validates the interrupt payload with `TypeAdapter(AskUserRequest)`.\nBefore this, a choice question with no `choices` reached the client and\ndegraded to a text box.\n\n## The tool wires no error handling\n\nA rejection is a pydantic `ValidationError` raised during argument\nparsing. `ToolNode` converts it to an error `ToolMessage`. The tool sets\nneither `handle_validation_error` nor `handle_tool_error`, and that is\ndeliberate.\n\nAn earlier revision of this PR set `handle_validation_error` to get a\nshorter message. That field is not part of the documented LangChain v1\nsurface, and the v1 migration guide lists schema mismatches under \"do\nNOT handle — already auto-handled by the framework\". It also intercepts\ninside `BaseTool.run`, which costs three things:\n\n**Harness faults reach the model.** `tool_call_id` and `runtime` are on\nthe same `args_schema` as `questions`, so pydantic reports them the same\nway. LangGraph strips them in `_filter_validation_errors`; a handler on\nthe tool runs earlier and bypasses that. The model cannot rewrite those\nfields, so it retries until the recursion limit.\n\n**Tracing records a success.** A handled error leaves `error_to_raise`\nunset, so `BaseTool.run` calls `on_tool_end`. With no handler the\nexception escapes, `on_tool_error` fires, and a rejected call traces as\nan error.\n\n**The model corrects one rule per retry.** The formatter named only the\nfirst error. `ToolNode` lists all of them.\n\nMeasured on one call that breaks two rules:\n\n```\nwith handle_validation_error:\n  callbacks: on_tool_end\n  content:   `ask_user` failed: questions.0.question: Value error, question text\n             must not be blank. Fix the input and retry.\n\nwithout (this PR):\n  callbacks: on_tool_error(ValidationError)\n  content:   Error invoking tool 'ask_user' with kwargs {'questions': [...]} with error:\n              questions.0.question: Value error, question text must not be blank\n             questions.1: Value error, multiple_choice question 'Pick' requires a\n             non-empty 'choices' list\n              Please fix the error and try again.\n```\n\nThe message is longer and echoes the model's own arguments. That is the\ncost of the framework default, and it buys correct tracing,\ninjected-argument filtering, and one retry instead of two.\n\n## Known limitation\n\nA `ValidationError` raised by the tool body after parsing succeeds is\nstill reported to the model as bad input. `BaseTool.run` and `ToolNode`\nboth wrap the body in the same `try` as argument parsing, so this is\nframework behavior, not specific to `ask_user`. Nothing in the body\nraises one today: `_parse_answers` raises plain `ValueError`, which\nstays fatal.\n\n## Unchanged\n\nThe raw-payload backstop in `auto_mode` (`_ask_user_question_count`\nre-reading unvalidated tool-call args off message history) does not\ndepend on how the tool validates. It still guards the same-turn\nauthorization path.","tree":{"sha":"57571de198b944a6c7052ec8ff5db0fb8a99e764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/57571de198b944a6c7052ec8ff5db0fb8a99e764"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiJo8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/5cQACK4FifEObxBA40eJMhBBZvi\nY8HEqB658RTQSIY4GYPcnazOglOGdszrB/9pbnmhZN+moAfn5bx9Mi2pMvQ24spI\nYNZsaOSnJnP5yL1E4+XnUvGOqlwktVuY+dLjEka3cToqY6s41ScWUChlKflw2E1P\nYK1VOSpdND5e6tKWE/slkmBt7JhntKW9pchJSdzcJWsU6uh0BG06ZwzCXeshd9Yg\nA88E8jcI/fTxTbxzvxY04MsiG/h0LQ83+DjQrtcLucfnFxXV7R0ST2uL73S6jwB5\nwY5rGsEI2Kd65BF0fimjblQ1AjAYuXygiTAPGpK7UKoMuw1zxl7E76inD+pMo8Gu\n6Xgld0NueHJ45ZnQByqrz47LFyRP+8zW8QCTV2ibmFqv/FIiD39/96/rHI+C81P8\nSPkmGToFkd4Mn28VVKkFuA8SH1oQ7ebU4LdGwHCUK8+OOp3FepAaX31O1pshljSA\nuW67Mf2Jm/YTyBG+D9wbdKEEXvVbg8UxjIyHHqsXj85qJ6UsyImqXCNZJl6tbZZo\nf13fqHfM0rUAggRYegl0vRfkPj57tadgLmCJMAcR0iv+yidXvX9IuImcp1vtA42r\nRGVY+9SP4v53zvBgUIi7DPh/ujbC3O3CeAN5ODs+S5RtA7iwgwi4oJDKdjboxy4y\nHqbSA14sV72E2n6/s3Nx\n=9pP+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 57571de198b944a6c7052ec8ff5db0fb8a99e764\nparent f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787337276 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787337276 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): validate `ask_user` args with pydantic instead of a custom error (#5682)\n\nA malformed `ask_user` call still surfaces to the model as a retryable\nerror `ToolMessage`. The validation now lives on the tool's pydantic\nschema. The hand-rolled validation function, the `ToolErrorMiddleware`,\nthe `ToolArgumentError` type, the `on_error` handler, and the scope list\nare all deleted.\n\n## The rules on the schema\n\nPer-field, on `Question`:\n\n- `question` has an `AfterValidator` that rejects blank and\nwhitespace-only text. The field keeps `min_length=1`, but that\nconstrains only the JSON schema the model reads. The validator is the\ninner annotation, so it runs first and is the only runtime gate.\n- `type` stays a `Literal`. `required` stays a strict bool.\n- Each `Choice` has an `AfterValidator` that rejects a blank `value`. A\nblank value renders as an unlabelled option whose answer reads as \"no\nanswer\".\n\nCross-field, on the `ValidatedQuestion` alias and the `questions`\nparameter:\n\n- A choice question must have a non-empty `choices` list.\n- A non-choice question must not have `choices`.\n- `questions` must not be empty.\n\n`AskUserRequest.questions` is `list[ValidatedQuestion]` too. The\ncross-field rules then also apply where `tui.textual_adapter`\nre-validates the interrupt payload with `TypeAdapter(AskUserRequest)`.\nBefore this, a choice question with no `choices` reached the client and\ndegraded to a text box.\n\n## The tool wires no error handling\n\nA rejection is a pydantic `ValidationError` raised during argument\nparsing. `ToolNode` converts it to an error `ToolMessage`. The tool sets\nneither `handle_validation_error` nor `handle_tool_error`, and that is\ndeliberate.\n\nAn earlier revision of this PR set `handle_validation_error` to get a\nshorter message. That field is not part of the documented LangChain v1\nsurface, and the v1 migration guide lists schema mismatches under \"do\nNOT handle — already auto-handled by the framework\". It also intercepts\ninside `BaseTool.run`, which costs three things:\n\n**Harness faults reach the model.** `tool_call_id` and `runtime` are on\nthe same `args_schema` as `questions`, so pydantic reports them the same\nway. LangGraph strips them in `_filter_validation_errors`; a handler on\nthe tool runs earlier and bypasses that. The model cannot rewrite those\nfields, so it retries until the recursion limit.\n\n**Tracing records a success.** A handled error leaves `error_to_raise`\nunset, so `BaseTool.run` calls `on_tool_end`. With no handler the\nexception escapes, `on_tool_error` fires, and a rejected call traces as\nan error.\n\n**The model corrects one rule per retry.** The formatter named only the\nfirst error. `ToolNode` lists all of them.\n\nMeasured on one call that breaks two rules:\n\n```\nwith handle_validation_error:\n  callbacks: on_tool_end\n  content:   `ask_user` failed: questions.0.question: Value error, question text\n             must not be blank. Fix the input and retry.\n\nwithout (this PR):\n  callbacks: on_tool_error(ValidationError)\n  content:   Error invoking tool 'ask_user' with kwargs {'questions': [...]} with error:\n              questions.0.question: Value error, question text must not be blank\n             questions.1: Value error, multiple_choice question 'Pick' requires a\n             non-empty 'choices' list\n              Please fix the error and try again.\n```\n\nThe message is longer and echoes the model's own arguments. That is the\ncost of the framework default, and it buys correct tracing,\ninjected-argument filtering, and one retry instead of two.\n\n## Known limitation\n\nA `ValidationError` raised by the tool body after parsing succeeds is\nstill reported to the model as bad input. `BaseTool.run` and `ToolNode`\nboth wrap the body in the same `try` as argument parsing, so this is\nframework behavior, not specific to `ask_user`. Nothing in the body\nraises one today: `_parse_answers` raises plain `ValueError`, which\nstays fatal.\n\n## Unchanged\n\nThe raw-payload backstop in `auto_mode` (`_ask_user_question_count`\nre-reading unvalidated tool-call args off message history) does not\ndepend on how the tool validates. It still guards the same-turn\nauthorization path.","verified_at":"2026-08-21T18:34:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d5005d3cc9e5735b88eb77779205976e1253f0bc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82"}]},{"sha":"f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY5NTRjZGUzN2YxMTcxYWRjMmVjM2YxNTE2YTAzOTNiZGVkNDdlODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T18:03:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T18:03:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): increase warm limit to 800 (#5728)\n\nResumed threads now warm more recent messages before scrollback reaches\ncold history.\n\n---\n\nThe transcript still mounts 100 rows initially, then warms to 800 while\nretaining opposite-edge pruning so all history remains reachable.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/61ba3072-607c-5a9f-bc03-aa370ac641ca)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Johannes <johannes117@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1d51172d1d401db273328371081bd546d53eec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e1d51172d1d401db273328371081bd546d53eec6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiJLkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEmQQAJ6Bn1/mhYeekwxG7zad2JqL\njcLCgUYKYGJiDSGJljSTCfnh5UaoW6VhDfNX/eD6kMDC1Wwac1udXufewSjaXRlv\ns4zPcZBUeGm/xrJFAwtLmeTA1WjWKlDZX5YTQS80Mv4Dw1bur1YUaCxQZ034+ynC\ntPkE+Eni/6ol0sSqsSJPJ/Q4nBde3v5PtiLtQitBVAWmqZQ0rTqptsddpPD77ePT\nzBZ/4mR5y0tZ0wgHEIWAnIBgSC6FJGiUrB6fa9WxsEihS5EeYfbnswjzaFDBnEpo\ndugMprJDz/PNZ8PbhAISzUueWws6DOufAUAlrie9/HuivZPD0uaFbnuVRP6RNKP9\nzL+pMp+R8EJ+jQ0zxay36rFItOGSqyN8s+zGk+7xcgEP+ivQYrVsxiZPvmmRgUMF\ni+aPr2er1BIoV8EIuMvSq0ijrUiFvUtw5tIcm3WaDmvUCnmB7QZRemCJjBTXYIDX\nEXfbZ/c7Bfq6vJVgJTPuMVSP9cfLL5q6GvU4XeULA5tsnGKYUiE7z3ZMdljsya8w\n5MUDPJ+713RX4B2ZDAz6/jOfiQGL1AFQmMD1QS7ubCK5HQYrpakMK+brIIWA3MuV\nUM/iLvk9jyl5VzedAt7481kEmIVJ6TC8Jwo6kpOcWxHe/tvB8x1mbf9Ua1h9P8DE\nMQuVja5xWTjwaFu8HwHG\n=qa8b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e1d51172d1d401db273328371081bd546d53eec6\nparent 995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1787335396 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787335396 -0400\n\nfix(code): increase warm limit to 800 (#5728)\n\nResumed threads now warm more recent messages before scrollback reaches\ncold history.\n\n---\n\nThe transcript still mounts 100 rows initially, then warms to 800 while\nretaining opposite-edge pruning so all history remains reachable.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/61ba3072-607c-5a9f-bc03-aa370ac641ca)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Johannes <johannes117@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T18:03:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f954cde37f1171adc2ec3f1516a0393bded47e82/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88"}]},{"sha":"995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk5NWNhZDY3NTE5YWYyOTQ4NTEyODIxMzNmOGM0MGY2NDM4MDdjODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T16:51:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T16:51:49Z"},"message":"feat(code): make project `.env` loading configurable (#5726)\n\n`dcode` can now be told not to read the *project* `.env` file. A new\n`startup.read_project_dotenv` option (default `true`, preserving current\nbehavior) controls whether the nearest `.env` discovered walking up from\nthe working directory is applied to the process environment. Set\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_READ_PROJECT_DOTENV=0`/`false`, or\n`[startup].read_project_dotenv = false` in `~/.deepagents/config.toml`,\nto skip the project file. The global `~/.deepagents/.env` still loads\neither way.\n\n---\n\nLoading the project `.env` is the trust boundary tracked as T12 in\n`libs/code/THREAT_MODEL.md`: the file travels with a cloned repo, so its\nvalues are attacker-controlled input that lands in `os.environ` and\nreaches every subprocess `dcode` spawns (including the startup `git`\ndetection that runs before any approval prompt). The denylist from #4288\nand the git keys from #5723 are best-effort enumerations of known\nexecution hooks — this option gives a user (or an org's managed config)\na way to close the boundary entirely when working in untrusted trees,\nrather than waiting for the next unlisted hook to be reported.\n\nDesign points:\n\n- **Default-on** so existing workflows (API keys, `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*`\nsettings carried in a project `.env`) keep working; this is strictly an\nopt-out.\n- **Scoped to the project file only.** The user's own global\n`~/.deepagents/.env` is trusted and unaffected.\n- **Cannot self-veto.** The option resolves from managed config →\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_READ_PROJECT_DOTENV` → user `~/.deepagents/config.toml`\n→ default. All of those are read *before* any project `.env` is applied,\nand the env var lives in the user-controlled process env (not a repo\nfile), so a project `.env` cannot turn the toggle off (or back on) for\nitself.\n- Wired as a first-class manifest option (`startup.read_project_dotenv`,\nBOOL, default `True`) so `dcode config get startup.read_project_dotenv`\nreports the resolved value and source like any other option. Resolution\nis a thin `resolve_read_project_dotenv` over the standard ranked engine;\n`_load_dotenv` consults it before the project-file branch and skips to\nthe global file when false. The dry-run `_preview_dotenv_environ` is\nunchanged — it reports what a real reload would load, and a real reload\nnow loads nothing from the project file when the option is off.","tree":{"sha":"22eb94dd97587bf4e56f6c539671870dcb037cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/22eb94dd97587bf4e56f6c539671870dcb037cb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiIIlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIAAQADxn8HP1GEnp2Gux3LIq7px9\nw1xmatZQdr8SdYitS94DwTzNH+ysFuxwQD3VKiA9axXOwewG/zsnDa3snhhvlAE0\nZplKA/oPBtfdFWW8WRvPXjz86zjx0DerSS8JZ0A5x/pJ3SHzZEOtcev8AvMjdqzx\n8M0gp8iLD4xj3Q1NVVLpt8ydHZxUeF6PLxVapDNyR/+5dQ8hMcmPMNYfuQNTbe/H\nHGG+h1EWwsEyc7ArsfLtcvqPH3MuSP/9UA4RA1JBENW/QXIQ8Ws+qDcnH8gl9ZBV\n1AAm6HANGrXe6S8tZ99m0hHPqUHKHq1LrJ1vWyTt2J7U3BXyU811E5QFfiOzMbRR\npl6xXMydS0Dl5Uu9qziwvhS7gCuPmKngTzg4npEJia3Cz3JZSWEni+T917OTSKtZ\nJU5sbnd1KbdDgWLC14vben9wC9PSewEvw70H3if6QqZ8ttVizZemIHn5IPbEyQ7/\nZPm1f7k1c68gElOZYpkt8wF5TmsN2Pjctl0iv4cqnbYX1PI6UC8F+Y30jeeF2qNA\nm+HZUrLfoEK3HYAWEQfvGC9AXdU3UOcpDwHVtyjNNEMmC3H73FjX4hLOStafKpPB\nVWL0rBs8XiUPD0sfHMXE9qm7zbbceLIDpZgq8l300oENLaOQrP5M1rRGupS/GA9K\nEPICNvSTRgQYOSqNnlZ5\n=Mr/Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 22eb94dd97587bf4e56f6c539671870dcb037cb5\nparent 42afcded97029070f393232778c84aaf3b69fb1c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787331109 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787331109 -0400\n\nfeat(code): make project `.env` loading configurable (#5726)\n\n`dcode` can now be told not to read the *project* `.env` file. A new\n`startup.read_project_dotenv` option (default `true`, preserving current\nbehavior) controls whether the nearest `.env` discovered walking up from\nthe working directory is applied to the process environment. Set\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_READ_PROJECT_DOTENV=0`/`false`, or\n`[startup].read_project_dotenv = false` in `~/.deepagents/config.toml`,\nto skip the project file. The global `~/.deepagents/.env` still loads\neither way.\n\n---\n\nLoading the project `.env` is the trust boundary tracked as T12 in\n`libs/code/THREAT_MODEL.md`: the file travels with a cloned repo, so its\nvalues are attacker-controlled input that lands in `os.environ` and\nreaches every subprocess `dcode` spawns (including the startup `git`\ndetection that runs before any approval prompt). The denylist from #4288\nand the git keys from #5723 are best-effort enumerations of known\nexecution hooks — this option gives a user (or an org's managed config)\na way to close the boundary entirely when working in untrusted trees,\nrather than waiting for the next unlisted hook to be reported.\n\nDesign points:\n\n- **Default-on** so existing workflows (API keys, `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*`\nsettings carried in a project `.env`) keep working; this is strictly an\nopt-out.\n- **Scoped to the project file only.** The user's own global\n`~/.deepagents/.env` is trusted and unaffected.\n- **Cannot self-veto.** The option resolves from managed config →\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_READ_PROJECT_DOTENV` → user `~/.deepagents/config.toml`\n→ default. All of those are read *before* any project `.env` is applied,\nand the env var lives in the user-controlled process env (not a repo\nfile), so a project `.env` cannot turn the toggle off (or back on) for\nitself.\n- Wired as a first-class manifest option (`startup.read_project_dotenv`,\nBOOL, default `True`) so `dcode config get startup.read_project_dotenv`\nreports the resolved value and source like any other option. Resolution\nis a thin `resolve_read_project_dotenv` over the standard ranked engine;\n`_load_dotenv` consults it before the project-file branch and skips to\nthe global file when false. The dry-run `_preview_dotenv_environ` is\nunchanged — it reports what a real reload would load, and a real reload\nnow loads nothing from the project file when the option is off.","verified_at":"2026-08-21T16:51:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/995cad67519af294851282133f8c40f643807c88/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/use