_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"328f9160e0f95a459be8ad57f76e7178b24a3ef8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/328f9160e0f95a459be8ad57f76e7178b24a3ef8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/328f9160e0f95a459be8ad57f76e7178b24a3ef8"}]},{"sha":"328f9160e0f95a459be8ad57f76e7178b24a3ef8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMyOGY5MTYwZTBmOTVhNDU5YmU4YWQ1N2Y3NmU3MTc4YjI0YTNlZjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T15:59:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T15:59:15Z"},"message":"fix(code): block dotenv git config injection keys (#5723)\n\nA project `.env` can no longer inject git configuration or git\nexec-helper environment variables into `dcode`'s process environment.\nPreviously, a cloned repository's `.env` could set\n`GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n`/`GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_n` (or\n`GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS`, `GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM`/`GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`) to\ninject config values such as\n`core.fsmonitor`/`core.pager`/`core.sshCommand`, which git executes —\nand `dcode` runs `git` during startup local-context detection, before\nany approval prompt. It could also set `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_WORK_TREE`,\n`GIT_EDITOR`, `GIT_PAGER`, `GIT_SSH`/`GIT_SSH_COMMAND`, and related keys\nto redirect git or hook its helper programs. These keys are now silently\nskipped during dotenv loading, matching the existing handling of shell\nstartup hooks (`BASH_ENV`, `ENV`) and dynamic-linker preload variables.\n\n---\n\nSame trust boundary as #4288 (T12 in `libs/code/THREAT_MODEL.md`): a\nproject `.env` is untrusted input that travels with a cloned repo, so it\nmust not be able to turn loading configuration into code execution in\nsubprocesses `dcode` spawns. The shell-hook denylist covered bash, the\ndynamic linker, and interpreter startup paths, but not git — and git is\na live consumer because `local_context.build_detect_script` runs `git\nrev-parse`/`git status`/`git for-each-ref` at startup.\n\nTwo shapes of git key are denied:\n\n- Exact keys added to `_DOTENV_DENIED_ENV_KEYS`: `GIT_DIR`,\n`GIT_WORK_TREE`, `GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY`, `GIT_EXEC_PATH`, `GIT_EDITOR`,\n`GIT_PAGER`, `GIT_SSH`, `GIT_SSH_COMMAND` (exec helpers / object-store\nredirects). `GIT_ASKPASS` was already covered.\n- A new `_DOTENV_DENIED_ENV_KEY_PREFIXES` family checked by prefix in\n`_is_dotenv_denied_env_key`, because\n`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n`/`GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_n` are numbered pairs that cannot\nbe enumerated in a static set. Also covers `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`,\n`GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS`, `GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM`, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`.\nMatching stays case-sensitive; benign keys like `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME` and\nnear-misses like `GIT_CONFIGKEY_0` are unaffected.\n\nBoth dotenv application paths (the mutating `_load_dotenv` and the\ndry-run `_preview_dotenv_environ`) route through the same predicate, so\nthe preview cannot report a value a real reload would reject.\n\nThis is defense-in-depth on a best-effort denylist: it closes the\nreported git vector without claiming the boundary is closed, and does\nnot change the documented residual that project files in the working\ndirectory can still influence execution.","tree":{"sha":"c0259955b1ad44c09ad84d4057fef8427730988d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c0259955b1ad44c09ad84d4057fef8427730988d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/328f9160e0f95a459be8ad57f76e7178b24a3ef8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiHXTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAknoQAF49jTLmrJVM0cgFFGJeBOX3\nb7ZhVGQ+H6xq/p9z6i4Ew+4lpiajAbbemyhR4VLgwbcUDMBvTEr7mbZEnWFT+y4o\nKR6Q8GjXtvDqjV1rDc63dbYyn0ykgf9RCjDOZEmwiCGcMhfBgCWR18rXAuaEP2jg\nbpCDGCTIzYH8xZdeFFjr9Up7UPhOtN6LG+xTfSjblq2kUzI3uqWlZk0g8a4V5xs9\nl4Y88A6Pk83upprkxWAzwRve/SJZLPDC/i2DGsS6hdS6nFBL3NwtnOP+b5+c1xIO\n6uiN6xP4fjyU0mGKeIWMhX//8p82MBI1906YWp3MxmJ80J5ePRjbvHCbTfBCuoRj\nze9AW7/CU9pYa0RG1rUODtKDpk6VW6+rf5QmYRY1qdxraugJNbKWZjVMm0127R74\nAVQepvtQZxx8H9uVTq6U6VTHIu4B0Biw21zJHKN7xq7ZscPObLbkYc0tV4+x7xGR\nCkuGqI8uVA8wnDmvbnL09EtjuSprBWWzdqqwFpU+3aphYAw/aILbujaNmMisltw0\nmBnPUqsfDUm7Jv5GFAOzNGlGP6JY0lAijz2nEDvdFsgSKf1xYZTHJgbyQgaXy/j8\n6j1ugWvmZJvneDPlAsmVrZR77xx+ltGu3fIWl4oS/p2T2ADITetH8vc6mXTX0Iz5\nLbGxYBHWToj88lCtFF+h\n=sGC8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c0259955b1ad44c09ad84d4057fef8427730988d\nparent 017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787327955 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787327955 -0400\n\nfix(code): block dotenv git config injection keys (#5723)\n\nA project `.env` can no longer inject git configuration or git\nexec-helper environment variables into `dcode`'s process environment.\nPreviously, a cloned repository's `.env` could set\n`GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n`/`GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_n` (or\n`GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS`, `GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM`/`GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`) to\ninject config values such as\n`core.fsmonitor`/`core.pager`/`core.sshCommand`, which git executes —\nand `dcode` runs `git` during startup local-context detection, before\nany approval prompt. It could also set `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_WORK_TREE`,\n`GIT_EDITOR`, `GIT_PAGER`, `GIT_SSH`/`GIT_SSH_COMMAND`, and related keys\nto redirect git or hook its helper programs. These keys are now silently\nskipped during dotenv loading, matching the existing handling of shell\nstartup hooks (`BASH_ENV`, `ENV`) and dynamic-linker preload variables.\n\n---\n\nSame trust boundary as #4288 (T12 in `libs/code/THREAT_MODEL.md`): a\nproject `.env` is untrusted input that travels with a cloned repo, so it\nmust not be able to turn loading configuration into code execution in\nsubprocesses `dcode` spawns. The shell-hook denylist covered bash, the\ndynamic linker, and interpreter startup paths, but not git — and git is\na live consumer because `local_context.build_detect_script` runs `git\nrev-parse`/`git status`/`git for-each-ref` at startup.\n\nTwo shapes of git key are denied:\n\n- Exact keys added to `_DOTENV_DENIED_ENV_KEYS`: `GIT_DIR`,\n`GIT_WORK_TREE`, `GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY`, `GIT_EXEC_PATH`, `GIT_EDITOR`,\n`GIT_PAGER`, `GIT_SSH`, `GIT_SSH_COMMAND` (exec helpers / object-store\nredirects). `GIT_ASKPASS` was already covered.\n- A new `_DOTENV_DENIED_ENV_KEY_PREFIXES` family checked by prefix in\n`_is_dotenv_denied_env_key`, because\n`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n`/`GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_n` are numbered pairs that cannot\nbe enumerated in a static set. Also covers `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`,\n`GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS`, `GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM`, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`.\nMatching stays case-sensitive; benign keys like `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME` and\nnear-misses like `GIT_CONFIGKEY_0` are unaffected.\n\nBoth dotenv application paths (the mutating `_load_dotenv` and the\ndry-run `_preview_dotenv_environ`) route through the same predicate, so\nthe preview cannot report a value a real reload would reject.\n\nThis is defense-in-depth on a best-effort denylist: it closes the\nreported git vector without claiming the boundary is closed, and does\nnot change the documented residual that project files in the working\ndirectory can still influence execution.","verified_at":"2026-08-21T15:59:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/328f9160e0f95a459be8ad57f76e7178b24a3ef8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/328f9160e0f95a459be8ad57f76e7178b24a3ef8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/328f9160e0f95a459be8ad57f76e7178b24a3ef8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c"}]},{"sha":"017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAxN2YwYmVkOTI5YzRkOGYzMTAwNjBlMjk0Njk5MjBiNzlkZWRmNWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-21T15:42:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-21T15:42:06Z"},"message":"docs(code): state dotenv denylist is best-effort in threat model (#5722)\n\nThe dotenv execution-hook denylist (`config._DOTENV_DENIED_ENV_KEYS`)\nwas added in #4288 to block shell startup hooks (`BASH_ENV`, `ENV`,\netc.), but the threat model never stated that the list is a best-effort\nenumeration of *known* code-execution consumers rather than a closed\nset. This wording change makes that explicit so future reports in the\nsame class are clearly residual risk under an existing mitigation, not a\nnew undocumented boundary.\n\nThree spots updated, plus a revision-history row:\n\n- **TB11 inside-detail (dotenv)**: states the denylist enumerates\nvariables known to reach a code-execution consumer (shell startup hook,\ndynamic linker, interpreter startup path) and cannot claim completeness\n— a not-yet-listed hook honored by a spawned tool (e.g. `GIT_CONFIG_*`\ninjecting `core.fsmonitor`) remains a live vector until added.\n- **T12 description**: closes with the same framing — the mitigation is\na key denylist of known consumers, a best-effort enumeration rather than\na closed set.\n- **Configuration input-coverage row**: the \"Gaps\" cell still claimed\n\"project `.env` can set shell startup-hook vars,\" which has been stale\nsince the denylist landed in #4288; reworded to the actual residual\n(execution-hook keys consumed by not-yet-enumerated tools still reach\nsubprocesses). The validation cell now also reflects the full denylist\nrather than only the Auto-classifier entry.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc33b599ba049b4c6c899a7f29645ee7825e85bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bc33b599ba049b4c6c899a7f29645ee7825e85bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiHHOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp48QAJBvQOyjbwHw1ZeMZhKPsUqW\nLG1KnDlI1gSeWf8RDy6nc6fyIkYoP64PAE/vg9aFD2DU2AHbz+7nwDAohppLw8f/\nB3QAyfEUN2pBCGt56A2vhS1X2RrwA5edloee6lJOVz+oodU34AetetUu3+8sf518\na+U2ohob1oYuJRDCaNczq5DSxjR3gzavI1fSFNGGD0pLOtFqJq1BBAMHSPX74KyB\n/edMWuAsljuoXXHbzOOo8FabknKl+RkGcxuTvOLA1FS0x+3R07ylVAdXmR1EcxE0\n+T+rJFZWPjZ4hgno+Jo/HOlSg/Y/4Y95X0bduPSoVXSOEEIj7MSvgjXMlSG1CH0z\nHjISQCyJi+c1pac9oxbh0Cd2kbyOyGlW5RV9OkPuF+SqMWa90E2zWarLpcqQl4MO\nKrGcnxDNL7C1Bu2OlujjjT2jO4+CkKzTcrmaG3edc7Lg1kwIx1yHNBccon497lm4\nUJi4Ws05qhhHTHddEHp0dgV2jsw+2tEdEX4RstvTxVoKoT3g82kd1c7BllC48Jfd\ns85QEBz+veAXuoLTY8EiBxDnRQlcbUwLbqtlRVSm+2N3w+LxHaEoA/KRiItHFygP\nB9zMs1U1iAUvZWB//yAPHSEx1EplTHMANYIXB7IFS8bYh5Y6/lNZxbQc/r67vkBs\ni4+1Oa5JMsbtsg9GBBUH\n=MOCH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bc33b599ba049b4c6c899a7f29645ee7825e85bc\nparent b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787326926 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787326926 -0400\n\ndocs(code): state dotenv denylist is best-effort in threat model (#5722)\n\nThe dotenv execution-hook denylist (`config._DOTENV_DENIED_ENV_KEYS`)\nwas added in #4288 to block shell startup hooks (`BASH_ENV`, `ENV`,\netc.), but the threat model never stated that the list is a best-effort\nenumeration of *known* code-execution consumers rather than a closed\nset. This wording change makes that explicit so future reports in the\nsame class are clearly residual risk under an existing mitigation, not a\nnew undocumented boundary.\n\nThree spots updated, plus a revision-history row:\n\n- **TB11 inside-detail (dotenv)**: states the denylist enumerates\nvariables known to reach a code-execution consumer (shell startup hook,\ndynamic linker, interpreter startup path) and cannot claim completeness\n— a not-yet-listed hook honored by a spawned tool (e.g. `GIT_CONFIG_*`\ninjecting `core.fsmonitor`) remains a live vector until added.\n- **T12 description**: closes with the same framing — the mitigation is\na key denylist of known consumers, a best-effort enumeration rather than\na closed set.\n- **Configuration input-coverage row**: the \"Gaps\" cell still claimed\n\"project `.env` can set shell startup-hook vars,\" which has been stale\nsince the denylist landed in #4288; reworded to the actual residual\n(execution-hook keys consumed by not-yet-enumerated tools still reach\nsubprocesses). The validation cell now also reflects the full denylist\nrather than only the Auto-classifier entry.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-21T15:42:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/017f0bed929c4d8f310060e29469920b79dedf5c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c"}]},{"sha":"b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI2NTBiNDEyOTg4YmE1M2M1OTgzMGI0MjA3ZmNkYjYzYzQ1YTlhM2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-20T23:01:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-20T23:01:20Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.59 (#5668)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.59](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.58...deepagents-code==0.1.59)\n(2026-08-20)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added support for `managed_config.toml` configuration\n([#5604](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5604))\n- Multi-select `ask_user` answers are now encoded as JSON arrays\n([#5660](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5660))\n- Made teardown usage stats configurable\n([#5696](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5696))\n- Footer pickers now open on click\n([#5674](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5674))\n- Replaced Gemini 3.6 Flash with Gemini 3.7 Flash\n([#5681](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5681))\n\n### Bug fixes\n\n- Made tool argument validation errors recoverable\n([#5659](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5659))\n- Improved streaming performance for tool-call arguments to run in\nlinear time\n([#5712](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5712))\n- Fixed durable-mask config resolution with ranked resolver behavior\n([#5672](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5672))\n- Skipped background sync in Apple Terminal\n([#5666](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5666))\n- Hid thread IDs when tracing is disabled\n([#5692](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5692))\n- Kept installed providers visible in `/auth`\n([#5689](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5689))\n- Preloaded the auth UI before notification handoff\n([#5697](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5697))\n- Updated and clarified UI copy across Auto mode, YOLO hints, classifier\nnotices, `/tokens`, line-number toggles, review failures, onboarding\nTavily cancellation, and OpenAI subscription login labels\n([#5685](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5685),\n[#5694](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5694),\n[#5684](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5684),\n[#5687](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5687),\n[#5680](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5680),\n[#5688](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5688),\n[#5686](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5686),\n[#5691](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5691),\n[#5693](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5693))\n- Removed the `Muse Spark 1.1` recommendation\n([#5683](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5683))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **community contributors** list and a **Special thanks** section\n(crediting the users who filed the issues this release's PRs closed) are\nappended to the GitHub release notes automatically at publish time (see\n[Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 3).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"302d42082d9c1ed96f608534d6acf1e38f02322e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/302d42082d9c1ed96f608534d6acf1e38f02322e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh4dBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhnwQAJ5IG7pN9MZxWTL7t6o1hoWn\n4SNl8zn0CKvr1yqW0oo67fe7Y9PI9sa+ReKBepRNXoWoX2CRlamatSmL7Xa8stJW\nSobLpIiYADFbQIGbECt/3dnIGBJ1pDh4mngRGzV5fa4Lh0VJLLHMxFoIJ1gvIv8f\nYnpwUlpmpAw6G2MKTw8IKUoOQ83KEz6mKJKIfR3417oFc/MJ4SBJAZd5fG6hMG4T\nmNckJdLAcgym43Zdbhy0iUHxQ6BNMTpFqJ9eDh9yTTF7NKykQkRXR9BQqa/cVnzr\nWFePzcAdQg6sW/sXc0O65FKU90oGBDGSpxq+NCQJXc9yfKoAu0xgSGGAkdNx2PyH\nNK4fz1ThwEFg9G4DSYWKv5geZGvXkk7RpSqWFTguJyibDLt+oWKXYcqtyREX1wwT\nVXYcutV6e5eQM8vhFvntAS92hJIjl4CfcD4HZnGbPO/AbHehBRDRr8O/Me/LsyAU\nEafyQkPzbDbMNT8E44mxKZnbj9xTfbm8uusNfEFyD6FH8StQn2Duehtj/tKWTWEF\n6/zizu2i1adLv20MU2egVDAfVlVC+7BvBhOq1EIXBZa5ssYajDJW+FVgfq68ITgW\nJ4QXnqBSP5hue9KvCiYWmOF8tFpfQren9oUKG8fbyxfp1aAddN31LX2x/eOOEc6B\nKKugXwGRmQCvgXoC970b\n=cyww\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 302d42082d9c1ed96f608534d6acf1e38f02322e\nparent 57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787266880 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787266880 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.59 (#5668)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.59](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.58...deepagents-code==0.1.59)\n(2026-08-20)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added support for `managed_config.toml` configuration\n([#5604](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5604))\n- Multi-select `ask_user` answers are now encoded as JSON arrays\n([#5660](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5660))\n- Made teardown usage stats configurable\n([#5696](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5696))\n- Footer pickers now open on click\n([#5674](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5674))\n- Replaced Gemini 3.6 Flash with Gemini 3.7 Flash\n([#5681](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5681))\n\n### Bug fixes\n\n- Made tool argument validation errors recoverable\n([#5659](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5659))\n- Improved streaming performance for tool-call arguments to run in\nlinear time\n([#5712](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5712))\n- Fixed durable-mask config resolution with ranked resolver behavior\n([#5672](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5672))\n- Skipped background sync in Apple Terminal\n([#5666](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5666))\n- Hid thread IDs when tracing is disabled\n([#5692](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5692))\n- Kept installed providers visible in `/auth`\n([#5689](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5689))\n- Preloaded the auth UI before notification handoff\n([#5697](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5697))\n- Updated and clarified UI copy across Auto mode, YOLO hints, classifier\nnotices, `/tokens`, line-number toggles, review failures, onboarding\nTavily cancellation, and OpenAI subscription login labels\n([#5685](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5685),\n[#5694](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5694),\n[#5684](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5684),\n[#5687](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5687),\n[#5680](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5680),\n[#5688](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5688),\n[#5686](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5686),\n[#5691](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5691),\n[#5693](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5693))\n- Removed the `Muse Spark 1.1` recommendation\n([#5683](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5683))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **community contributors** list and a **Special thanks** section\n(crediting the users who filed the issues this release's PRs closed) are\nappended to the GitHub release notes automatically at publish time (see\n[Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 3).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-20T23:01:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b650b412988ba53c59830b4207fcdb63c45a9a3c/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8"}]},{"sha":"57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU3YmZhNmJkYzU3MDU2MjY1MDQ3NzQ0ZGMzMmYzMzM3YTk2NGRkYzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-20T20:55:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-20T20:55:35Z"},"message":"fix(code): stream tool-call args in linear time (#5712)\n\nLarge streamed tool calls no longer repeatedly copy their full argument\npayload while rendering.\n\n`ToolCallBuffer` scanned the whole accumulated prefix on every chunk to\ndecide whether the payload was complete, so a long argument value cost\nO(n^2) over its stream. It now tracks JSON lexical state per fragment —\nfirst and last non-whitespace character, container depth and its running\nmaximum, string and escape state, over-closing — and defers the join and\nthe `json.loads` until that state says the value is structurally\ncomplete. The parsed result is memoized, and invalidated as soon as\nanother fragment arrives.\n\nEach fragment is scanned once, so the container and string-scalar paths\nare linear over a stream. A bare non-string scalar (a number or literal)\nhas no closing token to wait for and still re-joins per chunk; tool\narguments are never that shape.\n\nMeasured cost of `ingest` + `parse_args` per fragment:\n\n| fragments | container | bare scalar |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2000 | 0.68 ms | 5.98 ms |\n| 4000 | 1.36 ms | 19.22 ms |\n| 8000 | 2.58 ms | 68.34 ms |\n\n## Latch lifetime\n\n`parse_args` short-circuits on `warned`, since every condition that sets\nit is permanent: depth exceeded (the running maximum never falls),\nover-closed (a closer at depth 0 cannot be undone), or\nbalanced-but-unparseable (the top-level value has already closed, so any\nsuffix is trailing junk). That makes the latch gate data rather than\nonly logging, so `_reset_args_fragment_state` clears it with the rest of\nthe per-payload state. Otherwise a malformed payload strands the next\none in the same buffer:\n\n```\ningest '{bad json}'   -> None          warned=True\ningest {'whole': 1}   -> {'whole': 1}  (whole-value chunk resets fragment state)\ningest '{\"good\": 1}'  -> None          <- valid payload, tool.use dropped\n```\n\n## Warning text\n\nThe over-closed path skips the balance check, so a payload can be\nreported unparseable while it ends mid-string. The old wording described\nthat as complete:\n\n```\nbefore: Tool-call args look complete but failed to parse: '{\"a\":1}} {\"b\":\"x\\n}'\nafter:  Tool-call args are unparseable and cannot be completed: '{\"a\":1}} {\"b\":\"x\\n}'\n```\n\n`%r` keeps control characters in model output escaped, and the preview\nis capped by `INVALID_ARGS_PREVIEW_LIMIT`.\n\n## Behavior\n\nVerified unchanged against the previous implementation by differential\nfuzzing over randomized payloads and fragmentations, comparing the full\nper-fragment return sequence and the warning counts. Deliberate\ntrade-offs are preserved and now documented at the lines that implement\nthem: a bracketed value with trailing junk is treated as\nstill-streaming, and a bare scalar that is complete but malformed is not\nwarned about, being indistinguishable from a still-streaming fragment.\n\nCoverage was added for the state that crosses fragment boundaries, which\nthe previous single-pass helpers did not have: the escape flag\nstraddling a boundary, the parse memo invalidating, the open-string term\nin the completeness gate, the depth guard at its boundary (nesting that\n`json.loads` would accept, so only the guard can produce the skip),\nincremental over-closing, the preview cap, and the latch reset.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b51e9730ad24b2aa3b20d717bc762aa3e83203ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b51e9730ad24b2aa3b20d717bc762aa3e83203ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh2nHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1xwQACf244WwNll3uAHE9ezaCb5o\nCuQEr+2mowdAKEfZ8Wbs5dRPvPqNLUMufRHTSNVtaSyGHGa+Md5aL65omHvfxuxi\nQTYFduJXfudkhThGaffJvr60tTmcaLxfe/JfPVOmGF5J3t3nkOyP4FHxQA5xfdc9\nB5WD/eX20Kghs3ZheHDZzyQrxoXCwbYdhUAHYawMedKWnFQcD6aphHKBLuluNxO+\n3dtvL4wyXmkdXukfUL2hkSmfP72zi6FkkVxKmGdpdL/nWsdtKkqiTwdu6ZG7P2pb\njy89PgYboCrhHSKfSwxbDW9x/s+NPE1QWGLHkZZ6QJ77kysf55Q3Ca1Qw7ikyYde\nxr3ZRb0bicgQWRa3MrF89ZUBxMT7YgekxsK/D01UsUtq47cUVfWSSW9APtCbcYyQ\ndPfDzxDickzFJv8IEizKozfM4/R9IBC3hZKblOYyWhENXfHddgoiOr6P7KqDgK69\n9PPfPeRZEpYYg4mup4OZ2btZUvsiw5ZScuv/OQG+2Fey8EiwdvdjiZE5HH3P9BWJ\nnfQlgnhwXKuqNe0wJqnqyjVy8CMIryE3aZpN8Yv+Q88yIBOBkfGFrRlLvs59/NW8\nLW5l1nKVK+PkAQl7PvX7YwjNohPm1aD5uxftlDRq2VOVwbPgBAVCk00mYyOmMsGb\nfTso/OumBoMaNNSQgRqA\n=qV9x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b51e9730ad24b2aa3b20d717bc762aa3e83203ac\nparent c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787259335 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787259335 -0400\n\nfix(code): stream tool-call args in linear time (#5712)\n\nLarge streamed tool calls no longer repeatedly copy their full argument\npayload while rendering.\n\n`ToolCallBuffer` scanned the whole accumulated prefix on every chunk to\ndecide whether the payload was complete, so a long argument value cost\nO(n^2) over its stream. It now tracks JSON lexical state per fragment —\nfirst and last non-whitespace character, container depth and its running\nmaximum, string and escape state, over-closing — and defers the join and\nthe `json.loads` until that state says the value is structurally\ncomplete. The parsed result is memoized, and invalidated as soon as\nanother fragment arrives.\n\nEach fragment is scanned once, so the container and string-scalar paths\nare linear over a stream. A bare non-string scalar (a number or literal)\nhas no closing token to wait for and still re-joins per chunk; tool\narguments are never that shape.\n\nMeasured cost of `ingest` + `parse_args` per fragment:\n\n| fragments | container | bare scalar |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2000 | 0.68 ms | 5.98 ms |\n| 4000 | 1.36 ms | 19.22 ms |\n| 8000 | 2.58 ms | 68.34 ms |\n\n## Latch lifetime\n\n`parse_args` short-circuits on `warned`, since every condition that sets\nit is permanent: depth exceeded (the running maximum never falls),\nover-closed (a closer at depth 0 cannot be undone), or\nbalanced-but-unparseable (the top-level value has already closed, so any\nsuffix is trailing junk). That makes the latch gate data rather than\nonly logging, so `_reset_args_fragment_state` clears it with the rest of\nthe per-payload state. Otherwise a malformed payload strands the next\none in the same buffer:\n\n```\ningest '{bad json}'   -> None          warned=True\ningest {'whole': 1}   -> {'whole': 1}  (whole-value chunk resets fragment state)\ningest '{\"good\": 1}'  -> None          <- valid payload, tool.use dropped\n```\n\n## Warning text\n\nThe over-closed path skips the balance check, so a payload can be\nreported unparseable while it ends mid-string. The old wording described\nthat as complete:\n\n```\nbefore: Tool-call args look complete but failed to parse: '{\"a\":1}} {\"b\":\"x\\n}'\nafter:  Tool-call args are unparseable and cannot be completed: '{\"a\":1}} {\"b\":\"x\\n}'\n```\n\n`%r` keeps control characters in model output escaped, and the preview\nis capped by `INVALID_ARGS_PREVIEW_LIMIT`.\n\n## Behavior\n\nVerified unchanged against the previous implementation by differential\nfuzzing over randomized payloads and fragmentations, comparing the full\nper-fragment return sequence and the warning counts. Deliberate\ntrade-offs are preserved and now documented at the lines that implement\nthem: a bracketed value with trailing junk is treated as\nstill-streaming, and a bare scalar that is complete but malformed is not\nwarned about, being indistinguishable from a still-streaming fragment.\n\nCoverage was added for the state that crosses fragment boundaries, which\nthe previous single-pass helpers did not have: the escape flag\nstraddling a boundary, the parse memo invalidating, the open-string term\nin the completeness gate, the depth guard at its boundary (nesting that\n`json.loads` would accept, so only the guard can produce the skip),\nincremental over-closing, the preview cap, and the latch reset.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-20T20:55:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/57bfa6bdc57056265047744dc32f3337a964ddc8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141"}]},{"sha":"c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMxZDk2NWFhMGRiOTNmOTIzZWMxNzk0N2ZhYjM0YTUzMDBjMTkxNDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-20T20:23:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-20T20:23:08Z"},"message":"feat(code): make teardown usage stats configurable (#5696)\n\nSessions can now disable the teardown usage stats table with\n`[ui].show_usage_stats = false`. The default stays enabled.\n\nThe option is registered in the config manifest, so `dcode config`\nreports it and it resolves through the ranked provider tiers: managed\npolicy, then `~/.deepagents/config.toml`, then the declared default.\nThere is no env var for this option. Usage accounting is untouched —\nonly the final rendered table is gated.\n\nThe preference applies to both surfaces, the TUI and `dcode -x`, since\nthe key names the preference rather than the surface.\n\nBefore, with `show_usage_stats = false`:\n\n```\n✓ Task completed\n        Session usage\nModel        Input   Output\ntest-model     100       50\n```\n\nAfter:\n\n```\n✓ Task completed\n```\n\nResolution for boolean display options lives in one place,\n`config_manifest.load_bool_display_preference`, shared by `app.py` and\n`main.py`. That helper resolves through `resolve_scalar`, which since\nthe ranked-resolver refactor is a compatibility surface over the ranked\nengine — so this option gets managed-policy precedence and provenance\nwithout any dedicated wiring.\n`test_bool_display_preference_keys_match_the_manifest` pins every such\nkey to its manifest default so a hardcoded fallback cannot drift.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5252967019f4d512b649e6e9a8cb448a7df80117","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5252967019f4d512b649e6e9a8cb448a7df80117"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh2IsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoicQABxKfVhPMTGyob5QH5tNQ39c\n7dMHIAYxzqp2M+9pa0SomCt7+S4PyUmAa4xrc+L05mQKojj6NG+yHql4qKH9Pete\nD0AbeDsiccbwEt3NcWoPVPBNHxE0mPF8uSl15x02VshXxRnXVyvrIoorFXgfV2XT\ncsc4rh5eIdX/ztzmUMTvsKWaQukcF6UyvMT06vEbhGmjjFua1enYyVewu09uSJ/R\nPBXQfgc0tL4kJLDpy/0hQZe9igLd6bdDGe1evWCOYxy0/GBeb8tUP8vOINukoGLG\nPhvrQGa/a8vQ3P9q5X3VlT1TW0/Ikmiq0a1pGQRBOevCpnbW2c1rt9nTSB7hy1wR\ngBOiJEOzeTDrkihHCxMJFjfPYIYGeKQCvYkeGxv1ErYwW1fH+Qm4bnVmUfMZ5IUA\nZUcXZHi22DGRixCEHhZkx86eFGbcUK4Ar4pRtzq33sAKW/YQcMfgVdFHNAq/qpcF\naDRt91B7Zz+YOWxCC5rpS/3XlAEKonlqwh5cjfinetR5VWUlcul4Xjy5rT4t3DMn\nl/AAkorVEe9CxasTHjjYyZH/7Mw/fMZ6oflQR5vKpDjtNo0YBiyyeTXU4MNDEzMV\nVpewJTRIZqysM4m5zuUnfJO5Z5cVuw+z8DiQsBd//ImNpq/+45zsOCrOmuLNo/L1\nLoDHQDTs4kD8OXTsw+q9\n=vzcc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5252967019f4d512b649e6e9a8cb448a7df80117\nparent a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787257388 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787257388 -0400\n\nfeat(code): make teardown usage stats configurable (#5696)\n\nSessions can now disable the teardown usage stats table with\n`[ui].show_usage_stats = false`. The default stays enabled.\n\nThe option is registered in the config manifest, so `dcode config`\nreports it and it resolves through the ranked provider tiers: managed\npolicy, then `~/.deepagents/config.toml`, then the declared default.\nThere is no env var for this option. Usage accounting is untouched —\nonly the final rendered table is gated.\n\nThe preference applies to both surfaces, the TUI and `dcode -x`, since\nthe key names the preference rather than the surface.\n\nBefore, with `show_usage_stats = false`:\n\n```\n✓ Task completed\n        Session usage\nModel        Input   Output\ntest-model     100       50\n```\n\nAfter:\n\n```\n✓ Task completed\n```\n\nResolution for boolean display options lives in one place,\n`config_manifest.load_bool_display_preference`, shared by `app.py` and\n`main.py`. That helper resolves through `resolve_scalar`, which since\nthe ranked-resolver refactor is a compatibility surface over the ranked\nengine — so this option gets managed-policy precedence and provenance\nwithout any dedicated wiring.\n`test_bool_display_preference_keys_match_the_manifest` pins every such\nkey to its manifest default so a hardcoded fallback cannot drift.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-20T20:23:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c1d965aa0db93f923ec17947fab34a5300c19141/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b"}]},{"sha":"a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEyNzgyZmYzNmVmZDVlOWM5ZWJkOWFiYjE3YjZmYjUxYTJmMDFlOGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-20T19:59:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-20T19:59:15Z"},"message":"fix(code): skip background sync in Apple Terminal (#5666)\n\nApple Terminal no longer inherits dcode's theme background after exit.\n\n---\n\nApple Terminal accepts `OSC 11` background changes but does not reliably\nrestore them with `OSC 111`. Skip terminal background sync when\n`TERM_PROGRAM=Apple_Terminal`, while preserving behavior elsewhere.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4a32bb78-8b86-53ea-8205-d9c7f6450485)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d350408496a15d1519921867bb769f0e41bbe99a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d350408496a15d1519921867bb769f0e41bbe99a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh1yTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJEAQAJo0nxkGmtLjJRPfORa3bO+k\n75zWL8RX4yJTI8chcY86fi0iWow4CIVY1xm0oD8rHaL4KGWvODoPcCm3a7cPG0Uq\nO+ZiW+4TcwKDKo5ASk42k82kDlwjmKGVlUKf+8tIfFSlN1rrb6NV/ABmA5HfWD+I\nE6//QmjwCkXXZDq7oBFw91E6j+7IRIc1KwXnw3RNjVX1eCu/VgWnvBcyq9WYK2SF\nB8Flsg8oiIcbMDZhEyHfctM3UeaHD3hsSb+KpXvXTpG5jbKoLCwPnJlZbaqhixuK\nCkVDPbm0w6GmuiW/s8cpJSqgi38HlbxTKScUrQpdw8/KslNPbeiNLF3SeB6zJ0tf\nY7PvLdn1yn5gLFgB79j+LBgS19p4q3p4AfraIA24oFQzBrD5b6J+hdLVf6VLBeex\nRfpOw1Hh7Xcq67v67V+qZ6OIHfG6FCmZbYiuA3eUjJ7ttVL2FYMdSNX05Y0hw9rb\no6Tjw5LysE7Ey6dn9tleYnSH/fhf6jbKUlcFd1EsYkydglrSj37Xc9103yLos/fO\njD/hyMs4qPpoAOsOaftsHgVG3oroxhgc8yBTNG7Izt74FF+2SEftg2hrk8eOUIfO\nMvAdCmua/PvKaxadb9d0T30kCOmIgMKK8VeC0kkQl0mDe7nRCv0ZI/u5KqIoQEGI\nyovKNZYQ26p8J/cu1DOj\n=JtRr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d350408496a15d1519921867bb769f0e41bbe99a\nparent c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787255955 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787255955 -0400\n\nfix(code): skip background sync in Apple Terminal (#5666)\n\nApple Terminal no longer inherits dcode's theme background after exit.\n\n---\n\nApple Terminal accepts `OSC 11` background changes but does not reliably\nrestore them with `OSC 111`. Skip terminal background sync when\n`TERM_PROGRAM=Apple_Terminal`, while preserving behavior elsewhere.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4a32bb78-8b86-53ea-8205-d9c7f6450485)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-20T19:59:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2782ff36efd5e9c9ebd9abb17b6fb51a2f01e8b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2"}]},{"sha":"c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM5ODRmOGQ5ZTk0ZjNiZjFhYzhkMjhhYzkwNWRjYmFhNWUzYWI0YTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-20T18:31:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-20T18:31:58Z"},"message":"docs(repo): trim always-loaded agent guidance (#5706)\n\nThe root `AGENTS.md` is always loaded, so every line competes for agent\ncontext. It had grown to 467 lines by restating setup, architecture,\nrelease, and workflow detail that already lives elsewhere in the repo.\n\nThis trims it to 151 lines of repository-wide rules and routes the rest\nto the existing sources of truth. Guidance with no home elsewhere moves\nto the scoped guide nearest to it:\n\n- `libs/DEVELOPMENT.md` — repository layout, `uv` environment rules,\ntesting, warning-filter mechanics, benchmarks, and the worked examples\nfor ruff suppressions, docstrings, and PR titles.\n- `.github/RELEASING.md` — the CI guardrails that gate a release.\n- `libs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — SDK starting points.\n- `libs/evals/AGENTS.md` — rules for the vendored tau-bench data.\n- `libs/partners/AGENTS.md` (new) — the partner onboarding checklist.\n\nScoped files load only when an agent works in that directory, so this\nguidance costs nothing on unrelated tasks. Two couplings are now\ndocumented where an editor will see them: the `Warnings are errors`\nheading, cited by name in eleven `pyproject.toml` files, and the `Branch\nnaming` heading, cited by `.githooks/pre-push` and by the comment\n`branch_name_check.yml` posts on PRs. Both keep their names for that\nreason.\n\nMoving each claim meant checking it, which surfaced several that were\nalready wrong on `main`. They are corrected here rather than carried\nforward:\n\n- The CLI guide's `deploy` example used a `--config` flag that does not\nexist, with a `deepagents.toml` that the deploy pipeline now rejects\noutright. Three documents still advertised the removed `dev` subcommand.\n- The CLI integration-test directory is a scaffold holding only a\n`conftest.py`. It has no tests and no LangSmith Hub suite.\n- The partner checklist named `pr_lint.yml` but not the two mirrored\n`SCOPES_RE` copies that the `branch-scopes-sync` hook compares against\nit, so following the checklist produced a failing hook. Four further\nsurfaces that hardcode partner names were also absent.\n- The benchmark section misdescribed the `libs/cli` target, the\n`has-memory-benchmarks` input, and the nightly sweep's coverage.\n\nEvery cross-document link and heading anchor in the change resolves, and\n`pre-commit` passes on all touched files.\n\nInitial trim made by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0d59394d-290a-58bd-b666-98100d6d1628).\n\n## References\n\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0d59394d-290a-58bd-b666-98100d6d1628/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ab5ebded02a2d4b2e2b6fab579f22287ed9148e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4ab5ebded02a2d4b2e2b6fab579f22287ed9148e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh0geCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJxYQADWJdnrlxXoI2sInf0THg5Hi\nbChpYcepkHA6xSZtuEzVg2Jmh0PWHWv68VwqLEvWkYnzfPNsO7i7nlpsl38FcqMB\nNhMvc1mBhm7kzj7jYSHlwt1x6UHZ4XF1Ao9xP2xnyl4Y3UBLs2rBJ23E/4XLfApN\nXanhA/A8orSZx77xUi57GjRDw//jUu1B5t+0nvRrgUpBN52PMqiB0ujEbFVIRuYV\neXD5RYTz98dFVoyXpiyyVcVzhSvOHpP14v8AuRRG+ZSjjJvV4GrKEsJx39ZZoswA\n6EA3qmAlmx8ymPKMhWur831PT3ALxrW+YDcdvRmKBgWdqDUyzGGjmPJ/5ikwpiNd\nJgQnrPzIYsP5ulmO+ttpTnT5Rk3mgcVHUHM5Rl16185j26k5nUYxuvo8LC0g1DvY\n8ySp9gGhpOrwArhB7Hri2yG4p3a1MVD5NmawUeE6T2X4/opuJrHpet/pt0/Kjv2y\njQHIiBgmuKpsAkh3jap+De1kdbgP9MbMvNYFoW8Z0e+VJVorZYcYAd1FZ1mCBW88\nnOCc8Imb6KbIe8lGPCe23ksKlrm2XI3GwieS/C++PuhfBTrfF9j8QWjR0EXAHKIY\nlmCvGkDwnrg9XYz6cp3g2uydjybGogdc75nGVqWeqWjRvkGJbXmkJIfaVvmxeNwe\nWgbCCW+JISKsg/3rfOBr\n=JQZD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4ab5ebded02a2d4b2e2b6fab579f22287ed9148e\nparent 9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787250718 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787250718 -0400\n\ndocs(repo): trim always-loaded agent guidance (#5706)\n\nThe root `AGENTS.md` is always loaded, so every line competes for agent\ncontext. It had grown to 467 lines by restating setup, architecture,\nrelease, and workflow detail that already lives elsewhere in the repo.\n\nThis trims it to 151 lines of repository-wide rules and routes the rest\nto the existing sources of truth. Guidance with no home elsewhere moves\nto the scoped guide nearest to it:\n\n- `libs/DEVELOPMENT.md` — repository layout, `uv` environment rules,\ntesting, warning-filter mechanics, benchmarks, and the worked examples\nfor ruff suppressions, docstrings, and PR titles.\n- `.github/RELEASING.md` — the CI guardrails that gate a release.\n- `libs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — SDK starting points.\n- `libs/evals/AGENTS.md` — rules for the vendored tau-bench data.\n- `libs/partners/AGENTS.md` (new) — the partner onboarding checklist.\n\nScoped files load only when an agent works in that directory, so this\nguidance costs nothing on unrelated tasks. Two couplings are now\ndocumented where an editor will see them: the `Warnings are errors`\nheading, cited by name in eleven `pyproject.toml` files, and the `Branch\nnaming` heading, cited by `.githooks/pre-push` and by the comment\n`branch_name_check.yml` posts on PRs. Both keep their names for that\nreason.\n\nMoving each claim meant checking it, which surfaced several that were\nalready wrong on `main`. They are corrected here rather than carried\nforward:\n\n- The CLI guide's `deploy` example used a `--config` flag that does not\nexist, with a `deepagents.toml` that the deploy pipeline now rejects\noutright. Three documents still advertised the removed `dev` subcommand.\n- The CLI integration-test directory is a scaffold holding only a\n`conftest.py`. It has no tests and no LangSmith Hub suite.\n- The partner checklist named `pr_lint.yml` but not the two mirrored\n`SCOPES_RE` copies that the `branch-scopes-sync` hook compares against\nit, so following the checklist produced a failing hook. Four further\nsurfaces that hardcode partner names were also absent.\n- The benchmark section misdescribed the `libs/cli` target, the\n`has-memory-benchmarks` input, and the nightly sweep's coverage.\n\nEvery cross-document link and heading anchor in the change resolves, and\n`pre-commit` passes on all touched files.\n\nInitial trim made by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0d59394d-290a-58bd-b666-98100d6d1628).\n\n## References\n\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0d59394d-290a-58bd-b666-98100d6d1628/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-20T18:31:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c984f8d9e94f3bf1ac8d28ac905dcbaa5e3ab4a2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87"}]},{"sha":"9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlmMjRiOWZjYWY3ZWQzOTliNzg4OGIyZjBmOWQxMzM2MzkzOWVhODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-20T18:09:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-20T18:09:55Z"},"message":"fix(code): ranked durable-mask config resolver (#5672)\n\nManaged configuration now resolves through ranked providers and durable\nmasking.\n\n---\n\n## Problem\n\nManaged precedence was centralized in `merge_managed_over_user`, but\nscalar precedence still depended on explicit managed-before-env branches\nin `resolve_scalar`, while update, sandbox, theme, MCP, and model\nreaders each carried managed-aware composition at their callsite. That\nmade precedence a convention every reader had to reproduce and left\ncoercion, provenance, and provider health split across different\nabstractions.\n\n## Design\n\nEach provider now coerces its own input into `Found`, `Unset`, or\n`Invalid`, then the pure resolver orders provider values by numeric\nrank: managed 200, a reserved-but-unwired CLI seam at 300, environment\n400, user TOML 500, and default 1000. Lower ranks win; for replacement\noptions, a durable `Found` masks lower-priority ephemeral tiers. Options\ndeclare which tiers they participate in — most display/debug settings\nare env-only and omit the file tiers. Per-option `replace`, `union`, and\n`deep_merge` strategies preserve existing deny-list and structured-table\nbehavior. Provenance, provider results, and retained diagnostics are\nkeyed by rank, while `ProviderStatus` supplies human labels only when\ncompatibility and diagnostic surfaces render them.\n\n## Behavior changes\n\nTwo outputs change. Both are cases where one spelling of a setting was\nread by two different code paths that did not agree.\n\n**Deny lists declared as a string now display as a list.** `config get`\nrenders the parsed value instead of the raw string. The effective deny\nlist is the same in both versions.\n\n```\n# config.toml:  [mcp]  disabled_servers = \"alpha, beta\"\n\nbefore:  mcp.disabled_servers = alpha, beta        (config.toml)\nafter:   mcp.disabled_servers = ['alpha', 'beta']  (config.toml)\n```\n\n**A whitespace-only `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK` no longer disables\nupdate checks, and now says so.** The runtime reader took the raw\nstring's truthiness, so a variable that degraded to whitespace disabled\nchecks with no output. The display path already treated the same value\nas unset, so the two disagreed. Resolution is now unified on \"unset\",\nand the rejection is reported.\n\n```\n# export DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=\"$UNSET_VAR \"\n\nbefore:  checks disabled, no output\nafter:   checks enabled\n         WARNING Ignoring DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK='   '\n                 (whitespace-only; treated as unset)\n```\n\n## Per-callsite risk\n\n| Consumer | Resolution change | Main parity risk |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `update_check` | Ranked replacement for update settings | A present\nwrong-typed managed `update` value must remain fail-closed like an\nunreadable file. |\n| `sandbox_config` | Ranked replacement plus deep merge for provider\ntables | Managed default selection and user provider siblings must\nretain their existing split. |\n| `theme` | Ranked deep merge for custom theme definitions | Built-in\noverrides, user theme siblings, and terminal-theme diagnostics must not\ndrift. |\n| `mcp_disabled` | Ranked union for managed/user string-or-list denials\n| Managed malformed values must still disable all servers; user strings\nmust still fall back to legacy `[mcp_disabled]`. |\n| `ModelConfig.load` | Ranked file tiers | Persisted\n`auto_classifier_model` intentionally excludes env, and provider/effort\ntables must merge identically. |\n| `load_mcp_server_trust_lists` | Ranked union/deep merge after grant\nnormalization | Security-sensitive deny precedence and the composite\napproval representation above need the closest review. |\n| Startup policy | Reads managed `tier_health` and `ProviderStatus` |\nEvery enforced invalid key and an indeterminate managed path must still\nexit 78 before runtime policy applies. |\n| Config/doctor surfaces | One snapshot plus rank-rendered provenance |\nHealth, violations, rejections, and effective values must describe the\nsame provider generation. |","tree":{"sha":"4f077eba3e2d69b891066149cfef204b9e6b2a75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4f077eba3e2d69b891066149cfef204b9e6b2a75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh0LzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW1EQAHay6Q0OmoouVMtSHat1+6kA\n3G3fwktro/ekC77QblOGcq9LblkySAZBnv6jdaXmP7HIeio4jShZI4AqhXe6hSNc\nrQEOSb1whZ6yfyCpCKXEtyxsb2AFpWn6LgxTtQRykk16j35rOmyDQ9xw01EwNWx6\nQ8jOmbyH5TiZ3Jle888oFi/Hxg9s7Li+mKp95lQkd/7r6nCmaAqIQo1fFT0PR9Gw\nPltKID+iI6TWNb0PQq+ylSnHvUK8mCr3kK2wcfRgFk1+ju3YvWlLNctG8d45lXWY\nSfvNiS+KtPXQDgnJS+kO8qs1GvvqOnh6AUF/e49R0Pk3EwbpxF528CKcvCAo9VcB\n5UN/+GQfEyJ1+AKP0D4eL/muQNZk17Y5P5gRuN8xfz37RLSTOSXCw000iVATNNu8\nhH3pmLPkGlHVocSz2WeF2vUcK0gR00k+CFAo6Nzg4N8hdk7X92nnt61gp0Y3a5w/\n3O1QsVWNMh84Uhr+Mtphe6L7b+9SY6gREP30akS92OVpxTqd2HSOTqc2jHOxSUue\ngV1cVAG1cCbVlX3T/7qryYfrAt4M05qivM9jrxVfSaRqNQmi2mgRHDU8v8Z83FFG\nfqoJQjOa3J/+GOKXblkiah8YlPkRDw/UKOW+rQ57eMXITTJIpf9X8MwqBlCA2s8S\nY4tAtxN8oZ/iNRqLiuVb\n=P1gJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4f077eba3e2d69b891066149cfef204b9e6b2a75\nparent 32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787249395 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787249395 -0400\n\nfix(code): ranked durable-mask config resolver (#5672)\n\nManaged configuration now resolves through ranked providers and durable\nmasking.\n\n---\n\n## Problem\n\nManaged precedence was centralized in `merge_managed_over_user`, but\nscalar precedence still depended on explicit managed-before-env branches\nin `resolve_scalar`, while update, sandbox, theme, MCP, and model\nreaders each carried managed-aware composition at their callsite. That\nmade precedence a convention every reader had to reproduce and left\ncoercion, provenance, and provider health split across different\nabstractions.\n\n## Design\n\nEach provider now coerces its own input into `Found`, `Unset`, or\n`Invalid`, then the pure resolver orders provider values by numeric\nrank: managed 200, a reserved-but-unwired CLI seam at 300, environment\n400, user TOML 500, and default 1000. Lower ranks win; for replacement\noptions, a durable `Found` masks lower-priority ephemeral tiers. Options\ndeclare which tiers they participate in — most display/debug settings\nare env-only and omit the file tiers. Per-option `replace`, `union`, and\n`deep_merge` strategies preserve existing deny-list and structured-table\nbehavior. Provenance, provider results, and retained diagnostics are\nkeyed by rank, while `ProviderStatus` supplies human labels only when\ncompatibility and diagnostic surfaces render them.\n\n## Behavior changes\n\nTwo outputs change. Both are cases where one spelling of a setting was\nread by two different code paths that did not agree.\n\n**Deny lists declared as a string now display as a list.** `config get`\nrenders the parsed value instead of the raw string. The effective deny\nlist is the same in both versions.\n\n```\n# config.toml:  [mcp]  disabled_servers = \"alpha, beta\"\n\nbefore:  mcp.disabled_servers = alpha, beta        (config.toml)\nafter:   mcp.disabled_servers = ['alpha', 'beta']  (config.toml)\n```\n\n**A whitespace-only `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK` no longer disables\nupdate checks, and now says so.** The runtime reader took the raw\nstring's truthiness, so a variable that degraded to whitespace disabled\nchecks with no output. The display path already treated the same value\nas unset, so the two disagreed. Resolution is now unified on \"unset\",\nand the rejection is reported.\n\n```\n# export DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=\"$UNSET_VAR \"\n\nbefore:  checks disabled, no output\nafter:   checks enabled\n         WARNING Ignoring DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK='   '\n                 (whitespace-only; treated as unset)\n```\n\n## Per-callsite risk\n\n| Consumer | Resolution change | Main parity risk |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `update_check` | Ranked replacement for update settings | A present\nwrong-typed managed `update` value must remain fail-closed like an\nunreadable file. |\n| `sandbox_config` | Ranked replacement plus deep merge for provider\ntables | Managed default selection and user provider siblings must\nretain their existing split. |\n| `theme` | Ranked deep merge for custom theme definitions | Built-in\noverrides, user theme siblings, and terminal-theme diagnostics must not\ndrift. |\n| `mcp_disabled` | Ranked union for managed/user string-or-list denials\n| Managed malformed values must still disable all servers; user strings\nmust still fall back to legacy `[mcp_disabled]`. |\n| `ModelConfig.load` | Ranked file tiers | Persisted\n`auto_classifier_model` intentionally excludes env, and provider/effort\ntables must merge identically. |\n| `load_mcp_server_trust_lists` | Ranked union/deep merge after grant\nnormalization | Security-sensitive deny precedence and the composite\napproval representation above need the closest review. |\n| Startup policy | Reads managed `tier_health` and `ProviderStatus` |\nEvery enforced invalid key and an indeterminate managed path must still\nexit 78 before runtime policy applies. |\n| Config/doctor surfaces | One snapshot plus rank-rendered provenance |\nHealth, violations, rejections, and effective values must describe the\nsame provider generation. |","verified_at":"2026-08-20T18:09:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f24b9fcaf7ed399b7888b2f0f9d13363939ea87/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2"}]},{"sha":"32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMyZjU2NWY0NjUxOWQ5YzM1OTE5NjQwYmRmOTM3NDUwNmQwNTcyZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-20T16:38:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:38:49Z"},"message":"fix(code): show Auto first-enable notice as pre-confirmation (#5686)\n\nThe Auto first-enable notice is now a pre-confirmation dialog that\nappears before Auto activates, instead of a post-hoc acknowledgment\nshown after the switch already happened.\n\n---\n\nThe previous flow activated Auto first, then showed a modal saying \"You\nswitched to Auto\" with Enter to keep it and Esc to revert. This was\nconfusing — the user was asked to confirm a transition that had already\noccurred, and the key labels described states rather than actions.\n\nThe modal now gates the switch itself. It appears before Auto activates\nwith clear labels: **Enter** confirms the switch to Auto, **Esc**\ncancels and stays in the current mode. This matches the existing YOLO\nacknowledgement pattern.\n\nBoth entry points are covered:\n\n- **Shift+Tab toggle** — the modal appears before the mode changes.\nEnter proceeds with the switch; Esc leaves the mode untouched.\n- **Inline \"approve all\" escalation** — the modal appears before Auto\ncommits. Enter activates Auto; Esc returns `False` so the approval loop\ncontinues asking.\n\nThe startup restore path no longer shows the notice — if Auto was\npersisted from a prior session, the notice was already confirmed when\nthe user first switched.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f61e2534-22a6-5838-afe9-8c575122c784)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1393830716e6242621ceecdc8f445fddf090dfa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1393830716e6242621ceecdc8f445fddf090dfa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhy2ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvB0QAI4H2NMOfTxXAaJTfb3s2Ue+\nnZfRnW3uSc2ZIk1WRZl4nFBkOVfSIcASmVzTK/zRvhIIzoK/Gz3O+NFFIaTERWKe\nFX8vcG9pONCl6n+zmDp0OlwGxV7pFmVIL8zpu73gDYGV6pHhhiPsJUH91BsdU54q\nY9eSHTHURcjF9DdropK1GIMsapnAcHzKFjM8wA9CW1vvi3tbAql/Ivv0So0XNTSm\nAKtoQLLdPSQYEll4x1Fqd8NnQY1DMfSgkTlgg71Li2vE3c8/j9gvttr2xtLzG91g\n+a//zNATzkqs7iRq/x2ccqQ9MyylxJidWPV8EGzKhu9SAhDGaCBeh4VqRBFcS6Ly\nld0i2PEdRUjatwBcCD152KemD4GexGhr1CjTF13J5S4rgurG7YY065K7BYeuJMWU\n2vsHe6b6hSRIyVqOoZcLseBnjSeuBeZsN4fc+atA9XHqo9xsrPbvYvwIg5VFG/Zq\n1pCwONilOIe7RNb5sXzeRezbLN/5JaMV00gHcI9q72OQNmmafzhv76q6TiF9DnWT\nuEnbff2SlOzLdEL1E4WPv8Fsbg7Nxt5G49Wg1CuGidobbkwPzA0Lba2YDrGUzZhU\nY29rNwG/ob4O7mzZGFmkOvQOfCzLDs2twmMz6YvbY5Hg2IgWf3oWUa05hasg7F0N\nzTaWAA2PjDJUgCHWTnDQ\n=roHh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1393830716e6242621ceecdc8f445fddf090dfa7\nparent 1680237e69bf27740001df7a7f67de5a053536c1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787243929 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787243929 -0400\n\nfix(code): show Auto first-enable notice as pre-confirmation (#5686)\n\nThe Auto first-enable notice is now a pre-confirmation dialog that\nappears before Auto activates, instead of a post-hoc acknowledgment\nshown after the switch already happened.\n\n---\n\nThe previous flow activated Auto first, then showed a modal saying \"You\nswitched to Auto\" with Enter to keep it and Esc to revert. This was\nconfusing — the user was asked to confirm a transition that had already\noccurred, and the key labels described states rather than actions.\n\nThe modal now gates the switch itself. It appears before Auto activates\nwith clear labels: **Enter** confirms the switch to Auto, **Esc**\ncancels and stays in the current mode. This matches the existing YOLO\nacknowledgement pattern.\n\nBoth entry points are covered:\n\n- **Shift+Tab toggle** — the modal appears before the mode changes.\nEnter proceeds with the switch; Esc leaves the mode untouched.\n- **Inline \"approve all\" escalation** — the modal appears before Auto\ncommits. Enter activates Auto; Esc returns `False` so the approval loop\ncontinues asking.\n\nThe startup restore path no longer shows the notice — if Auto was\npersisted from a prior session, the notice was already confirmed when\nthe user first switched.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f61e2534-22a6-5838-afe9-8c575122c784)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-20T16:38:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/32f565f46519d9c35919640bdf9374506d0572d2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1680237e69bf27740001df7a7f67de5a053536c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1680237e69bf27740001df7a7f67de5a053536c1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1680237e69bf27740001df7a7f67de5a053536c1"}]},{"sha":"1680237e69bf27740001df7a7f67de5a053536c1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE2ODAyMzdlNjliZjI3NzQwMDAxZGY3YTdmNjdkZTVhMDUzNTM2YzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-20T16:34:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:34:43Z"},"message":"fix(code): hide thread IDs when tracing is disabled (#5692)\n\nThread transition notices now omit opaque IDs when LangSmith tracing is\nunavailable, while preserving clickable IDs when tracing is configured.\n\n---\n\nUnlinked IDs add noise without helping users navigate. The concise\nfallback retains the `/threads -r` recovery action and skips un