chain-openai>=1.5.2,<2.0.0` → `langchain-openai>=1.6.0,<2.0.0` |\n\nOpened automatically by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`. Review the\nraised bounds against any compatibility notes in the manifest comments\nbefore merging.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-19T21:53:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9bd088a69ed9b9510391daf247a9dbb9dfbea6bf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9bd088a69ed9b9510391daf247a9dbb9dfbea6bf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9bd088a69ed9b9510391daf247a9dbb9dfbea6bf/comments","author":{"login":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","id":248757908,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODtO-lA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2441712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/langchain-oss-automated-triage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ab359bab20175a960227203de482a1fbd6edffea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ab359bab20175a960227203de482a1fbd6edffea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ab359bab20175a960227203de482a1fbd6edffea"}]},{"sha":"ab359bab20175a960227203de482a1fbd6edffea","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFiMzU5YmFiMjAxNzVhOTYwMjI3MjAzZGU0ODJhMWZiZDZlZGZmZWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T21:50:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T21:50:22Z"},"message":"test(code): await the connection refresh task instead of polling `_state` (#5661)\n\n`test_connection_refresh_waits_for_initial_refresh` no longer spins on a\nfixed number of event-loop yields: it awaits the settled\nconnection-refresh task itself, so the test passes no matter how long a\nloaded CI runner takes to schedule the refresh task's continuation.\n\n---\n\nThe event-driven rewrite in #5636 removed the test's fixed 1-second\ntimeouts but left one scheduling-sensitive wait. After the stubbed state\nloader signaled the settled refresh from the `to_thread` worker, the\ntest polled `screen._state` across 100 `asyncio.sleep(0)` iterations,\nassuming that was enough yields for the connection task's `_state = ...`\ncontinuation (the resume after `await asyncio.to_thread(...)`) to run.\n\nIt usually is — but the thread-side signal fires strictly before that\ncontinuation, and the continuation needs a fresh default-executor thread\nspawn plus a loop iteration. Under `-n auto` xdist load on the 2-core CI\nrunner the test task can exhaust all 100 iterations while the connection\ntask is still suspended, failing with:\n\n```\nAssertionError: settled load ran but `_state` was not applied; snapshots: [True, False]\n```\n\neven though the ordering under test held (`snapshots == [True, False]`\nproves the settled load ran second) and the refresh would have applied\nthe settled snapshot moments later. Example failure:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32299324726/job/96218579664?pr=5591\n(Python 3.13 leg; 3.14 passed in the same run).\n\nThe fix awaits the connection refresh task directly:\n\n- `update_connection_state` already keeps each refresh task strongly\nreferenced in `screen._refresh_tasks` so it cannot vanish mid-flight, so\nthe test can unpack the single queued task and `await` it under the\nexisting 10-second descriptive timeout. Awaiting the task waits for the\nentire `_refresh_state` body — including the `_state` assignment —\ninstead of racing it.\n- The thread-side `settled_applied` event is no longer needed and is\nremoved; `snapshots` still asserts the load ordering.\n\nBehavior under test is unchanged; only the wait mechanism moves off the\nbounded spin loop.","tree":{"sha":"e72c1cc07021306ac6e6869d276e3bd1007f1729","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e72c1cc07021306ac6e6869d276e3bd1007f1729"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ab359bab20175a960227203de482a1fbd6edffea","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhiUeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2NYQACwD3Yx85wOREkuil4ZCz9de\n9KnV65I4uFM2tNiQh08CF0Y4zhIhvcR1NByID1LIn/NQSWBBbbuV4hg6p4Z1+lJT\nE6h0EQPZ880M5DA9As9rNWJdQhhqEiKuAy/ezK1UhaM5Kuo8NSPuG7HEnR6RbkFy\nB11Aks1pukHKrQHal1SM7Bzm2ZfbSc/R8oTW3eKdYGMX9rX5LmglCnLly7RBMZXW\nNYzhIhaGwUdoFX86pudJKuLl3ESPY3RNP8MuBlgaMRcCyhyB8lobYJUWodD8/ZYi\nFSgCAlvchip+E95aLEDfma5PN4HAo4TUCAs/YJYsmfnjA8vRBZGkeMfmo7BgWk24\nJnHL43gIXFQcvkre9dNUi2WySaEvMt6612fs27nfo3y+nsVm9Yr8pGRSo2YgMzCW\nT3MaVsIabityvzyzykvSPZyz7HqFiGrOgvr03uo57PwGZ/77aiv/32zsluaSxO4X\nw3nzoPGMEHZlC0fCTfIhb2t4tnaZN147Knk9nAxG5ANokVDege2GeNuf1D74CVA7\nYRZzMvHJf+Sf05q3ncfnb9CGT3bV2L3s+tvGdpYa1Khx4Q2vT8+Cx6ePvDa3OvKt\n5aiwBNo17IXxbM81p+xVBwIUJ4HSCPAvWsGmxgpkLg2T1uUtHuu4lyvaik++8OEL\nG2WH9GJdJtdiO/QHulZC\n=a/L1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e72c1cc07021306ac6e6869d276e3bd1007f1729\nparent 31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787176222 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787176222 -0400\n\ntest(code): await the connection refresh task instead of polling `_state` (#5661)\n\n`test_connection_refresh_waits_for_initial_refresh` no longer spins on a\nfixed number of event-loop yields: it awaits the settled\nconnection-refresh task itself, so the test passes no matter how long a\nloaded CI runner takes to schedule the refresh task's continuation.\n\n---\n\nThe event-driven rewrite in #5636 removed the test's fixed 1-second\ntimeouts but left one scheduling-sensitive wait. After the stubbed state\nloader signaled the settled refresh from the `to_thread` worker, the\ntest polled `screen._state` across 100 `asyncio.sleep(0)` iterations,\nassuming that was enough yields for the connection task's `_state = ...`\ncontinuation (the resume after `await asyncio.to_thread(...)`) to run.\n\nIt usually is — but the thread-side signal fires strictly before that\ncontinuation, and the continuation needs a fresh default-executor thread\nspawn plus a loop iteration. Under `-n auto` xdist load on the 2-core CI\nrunner the test task can exhaust all 100 iterations while the connection\ntask is still suspended, failing with:\n\n```\nAssertionError: settled load ran but `_state` was not applied; snapshots: [True, False]\n```\n\neven though the ordering under test held (`snapshots == [True, False]`\nproves the settled load ran second) and the refresh would have applied\nthe settled snapshot moments later. Example failure:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32299324726/job/96218579664?pr=5591\n(Python 3.13 leg; 3.14 passed in the same run).\n\nThe fix awaits the connection refresh task directly:\n\n- `update_connection_state` already keeps each refresh task strongly\nreferenced in `screen._refresh_tasks` so it cannot vanish mid-flight, so\nthe test can unpack the single queued task and `await` it under the\nexisting 10-second descriptive timeout. Awaiting the task waits for the\nentire `_refresh_state` body — including the `_state` assignment —\ninstead of racing it.\n- The thread-side `settled_applied` event is no longer needed and is\nremoved; `snapshots` still asserts the load ordering.\n\nBehavior under test is unchanged; only the wait mechanism moves off the\nbounded spin loop.","verified_at":"2026-08-19T21:50:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ab359bab20175a960227203de482a1fbd6edffea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ab359bab20175a960227203de482a1fbd6edffea","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ab359bab20175a960227203de482a1fbd6edffea/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5"}]},{"sha":"31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMxYWY4YzExMjE5YzNjNzdmNDUzMGJjMWU0YWRjM2MxNDBjZmE2ZDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","email":"248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-19T21:48:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T21:48:57Z"},"message":"chore(deps): raise dependency minimums for `deepagents` (#5662)\n\nRaises the LangChain-ecosystem dependency lower bounds (`langchain*`,\n`langgraph*`, `langsmith*`, `deepagents*`) for `deepagents` to the\nlatest compatible stable PyPI release, and regenerates every affected\n`uv.lock`. Upper bounds, extras, and markers are preserved; exact `==`\npins are left alone.\n\nRaised 1 minimum(s):\n\n| Manifest | Dependency | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| `libs/deepagents/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-anthropic` |\n`langchain-anthropic>=1.5.6,<2.0.0` →\n`langchain-anthropic>=1.6.0,<2.0.0` |\n\nOpened automatically by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`. Review the\nraised bounds against any compatibility notes in the manifest comments\nbefore merging.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9438188e886af9f7f766f62a59d9dc7a4651957e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9438188e886af9f7f766f62a59d9dc7a4651957e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhiTJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO1QQAJ/tUbop7gtF7BinKtdgnVOn\noCB1NlLPeOP93TtU1G5eMu4GMWS3ejwJQNNwUkvpLsVNs2Mqq1qyIIt50HGL+QVH\ny4OzVHbqv5XEmctk4igNWqHoK3VsSD64/xEKzfQ4/0NFQ6kKAgdEwRGFqF2wfstA\n1GKaefYGssbq3cIMeefg8BYzePz+zRZuKzxNEJDrR2fixivWrHyEHkU6s9ewtxzl\nPkSVscNpydRbgNVpZOk9Lebcjq7O/u+E7Dsc+tKCvmzXQ6ximVpjOkOnxxRMn3f9\nm35+2OjmHfI0wJnTa/iOp/JELdwBk8fonQu5ZzXOzD0vq9BO0QDpbtrBa7FOvtP5\nuXnpM8HB6SWqu7/1ar/7yeBUpqX26K3wtKXXfFSwdQUE84cVfSBnLBeYwWcxad5G\nEhNCwXWNy8PKm0JJ0yDGgCwAwD3LdAEnRzWtepa5u0Qpuk3pvrJ8DvSX5Ktn2DiJ\nbX7XwhQfeKjjPMJD/CB25xno7mhejve9NQjuRiUkBGWg0I8WLuQrX74Wi8KfGyuj\nC0yRkXN7nb1nlOpl9dvvmIqMhHDzuwcSI9zq46zBWNkI1iWfsvW6EqlLcGunB4kK\nmoAdtt7fyY1+u1MYx+8xg+w3Tl9gdoK39W07OzdqmvqDWlykKebitnEqiZUa5jK9\n/BgfHLShsP9/PTZRKLRX\n=3Va5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9438188e886af9f7f766f62a59d9dc7a4651957e\nparent a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d\nauthor langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787176137 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787176137 -0400\n\nchore(deps): raise dependency minimums for `deepagents` (#5662)\n\nRaises the LangChain-ecosystem dependency lower bounds (`langchain*`,\n`langgraph*`, `langsmith*`, `deepagents*`) for `deepagents` to the\nlatest compatible stable PyPI release, and regenerates every affected\n`uv.lock`. Upper bounds, extras, and markers are preserved; exact `==`\npins are left alone.\n\nRaised 1 minimum(s):\n\n| Manifest | Dependency | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| `libs/deepagents/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-anthropic` |\n`langchain-anthropic>=1.5.6,<2.0.0` →\n`langchain-anthropic>=1.6.0,<2.0.0` |\n\nOpened automatically by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`. Review the\nraised bounds against any compatibility notes in the manifest comments\nbefore merging.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-19T21:48:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/31af8c11219c3c77f4530bc1e4adc3c140cfa6d5/comments","author":{"login":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","id":248757908,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODtO-lA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2441712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/langchain-oss-automated-triage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d"}]},{"sha":"a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEwOTkwZmYwZDljNDAyNzZmYzU1ZTQ3YzhmZDQ0Yzc5OGU4Zjg1OGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T21:44:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T21:44:15Z"},"message":"feat(infra): `bypass-ripgrep-check` label for release PR strict install (#5657)\n\nA release PR whose strict ripgrep install hits a transient apt or mirror\nfailure currently fails CI with no recourse but a re-run. Maintainers\ncan now add the `bypass-ripgrep-check` label to the release PR to\ntolerate that failure: the affected legs skip the ripgrep-gated tests, a\nsticky comment on the PR records which legs ran without ripgrep, and\nwhen the PR merges the publish run is dispatched with\n`dangerous-skip-ripgrep-check=true` so its own ripgrep install tolerates\nthe same flake instead of re-failing.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\nThe strict install in `_test.yml` (and the matching `Install ripgrep`\nstep in `release.yml`) runs with no timeout on release-sensitive paths\non purpose: the rg-gated tests, including the symlink-containment check,\nmust exercise the real binary rather than the Python fallback, and a\nsilent skip at that gate is worse than a red job. The cost is that pure\ninfrastructure flake — an apt mirror timeout, a wedged dpkg — blocks an\notherwise-good release.\n\nThis mirrors the existing `bypass-warnings-check` and `release: skip sdk\npin check` patterns rather than inventing a new mechanism:\n\n- **`_test.yml`**: a new `🏷️ Resolve ripgrep bypass` step reads the live\nPR labels via `gh api` (not the event payload, so a label added before a\nre-run takes effect) and fails closed on an API error. The strict step\nkeeps trying to install, but on a labeled PR an apt failure exits 0\ninstead of failing. `DEEPAGENTS_RIPGREP_EXPECTED` is only set when `rg`\nis actually usable, so a genuinely missing binary lets\n`require_ripgrep()` skip the gated tests on that leg rather than fail\nthem.\n- **`ripgrep_timeout_comment.yml`**: the bypassed strict leg emits the\nsame `ripgrep-timeout-*` marker artifact as the soft path, so the\nexisting sticky-comment workflow reports it. The comment now reads the\nPR's labels (fail-closed) and branches its wording — a bypassed release\nPR says so explicitly and notes that the publish run was dispatched with\nthe override, instead of the old (now-inaccurate) \"release PRs fail if\nripgrep does not install\" line.\n- **`release-please.yml`**: after the SDK-pin block, it checks the\nmerged release PR for `bypass-ripgrep-check` via the existing\nfail-closed `release_pr_has_label` helper and, when present, passes `-f\ndangerous-skip-ripgrep-check=true` to every dispatched package. Unlike\nthe SDK-pin check this is not package-gated, because every package's\npublish run shares the same ripgrep step. The dispatch log, step\nsummary, and recovery commands all surface the override.\n- **`release.yml`**: a new `dangerous-skip-ripgrep-check` boolean input\nis logged in the dispatch-inputs summary and softens the `Install\nripgrep` step — a failure is tolerated and `DEEPAGENTS_RIPGREP_EXPECTED`\nleft unset only when the input is `true`.\n\nScope: the label is honored only on release PRs. `push`-to-`main` and\nmerge-queue runs have no PR label to read, so they always enforce the\nstrict install.\n\nThe label must be created in repo settings (`bypass-ripgrep-check`)\nbefore this can take effect; documented under \"Release Failed: Ripgrep\nInstall\" in `RELEASING.md`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Extended `test_ci_workflow.py` with an executable\n`test_strict_ripgrep_install_bypass` that runs the strict step's real\n`run:` body against stubbed `apt-get`/`rg`/`dpkg`: unlabeled apt\nfailures fail with the original exit code; labeled failures are\ntolerated; ripgrep is only promised to the tests when `rg` is actually\nusable; a bypassed leg with no usable `rg` emits the marker artifact.\n- Updated the strict-step and upload-step drift assertions to match the\nnew condition and artifact selection, and added comment-workflow\nassertions for the label read and bypass wording.\n- All 1108 workflow-helper tests pass; the touched YAML files parse; the\nnew bash bodies pass `bash -n`; the comment workflow's JS passes `node\n--check`; ruff check/format clean on the test file.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"7b5381fb2dd17f7e48b111b3e90f9cbf2e2cbca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7b5381fb2dd17f7e48b111b3e90f9cbf2e2cbca0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhiOvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1C0QAIzlo6eMXdRDHKRAQviWVjNa\nBCio43rgOqa3QlJTiRKpeCOVN0i9DIv9aT3eMfy/W8RbGT4ZmmrVn/p0c4HWKjAg\netXSnYROptuCUWtly8xZWBSqrByzyDGUa/yID57ckwCUgDFWQ4IiG9+rBiUaDWyp\ncCWKVo8cIH4E1ltHT4k5Dlql2O+Y95YApTBKddYEc7Cc0GmEWniP1uYQy/xjQYhg\nVpoi5ivE8k9aLMYIvRZAKuDG4+cPkxzCZPyeI7k+5OtXYPnzEe07gogskM5yPrYf\nY4TxbLVL8PEnvLAvdxKwj5o5yAcItRlCv7anHtxOPg8JGCcZ9yI4hUA+Z6/PNtp1\nU5PO755kdhTJxdgogofzNq+pFZ+en7hCH3Kkf4m5hBSb7dge+/mca8OnZYgcZNMG\njLm7tlNL0zYQ32aRjmJxRwtD1k0MZCJpB2LaptAclklC8eokfNt9tWnEbRoD/rZE\n6SalHZsBtSXKZg+DiKuNIwAmY/NVgfRXC/8yTRddyYilwCESaVEzUn5vsiLCjvxq\nrPcK4YrLC7u7OArCdCRCk2+jxXPRwNNWV26UzlZUgqPh84zZRPUMeZ8doHzT5qvF\nwdbuPiXhXyWN0SdceaF3BkdkbOTb6KTcyZUlZd0s8RzF/BL9VHVlIjxtQf7oohTt\ncVXHy3we4zdnZKODm8qI\n=fRpw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7b5381fb2dd17f7e48b111b3e90f9cbf2e2cbca0\nparent 81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787175855 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787175855 -0400\n\nfeat(infra): `bypass-ripgrep-check` label for release PR strict install (#5657)\n\nA release PR whose strict ripgrep install hits a transient apt or mirror\nfailure currently fails CI with no recourse but a re-run. Maintainers\ncan now add the `bypass-ripgrep-check` label to the release PR to\ntolerate that failure: the affected legs skip the ripgrep-gated tests, a\nsticky comment on the PR records which legs ran without ripgrep, and\nwhen the PR merges the publish run is dispatched with\n`dangerous-skip-ripgrep-check=true` so its own ripgrep install tolerates\nthe same flake instead of re-failing.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\nThe strict install in `_test.yml` (and the matching `Install ripgrep`\nstep in `release.yml`) runs with no timeout on release-sensitive paths\non purpose: the rg-gated tests, including the symlink-containment check,\nmust exercise the real binary rather than the Python fallback, and a\nsilent skip at that gate is worse than a red job. The cost is that pure\ninfrastructure flake — an apt mirror timeout, a wedged dpkg — blocks an\notherwise-good release.\n\nThis mirrors the existing `bypass-warnings-check` and `release: skip sdk\npin check` patterns rather than inventing a new mechanism:\n\n- **`_test.yml`**: a new `🏷️ Resolve ripgrep bypass` step reads the live\nPR labels via `gh api` (not the event payload, so a label added before a\nre-run takes effect) and fails closed on an API error. The strict step\nkeeps trying to install, but on a labeled PR an apt failure exits 0\ninstead of failing. `DEEPAGENTS_RIPGREP_EXPECTED` is only set when `rg`\nis actually usable, so a genuinely missing binary lets\n`require_ripgrep()` skip the gated tests on that leg rather than fail\nthem.\n- **`ripgrep_timeout_comment.yml`**: the bypassed strict leg emits the\nsame `ripgrep-timeout-*` marker artifact as the soft path, so the\nexisting sticky-comment workflow reports it. The comment now reads the\nPR's labels (fail-closed) and branches its wording — a bypassed release\nPR says so explicitly and notes that the publish run was dispatched with\nthe override, instead of the old (now-inaccurate) \"release PRs fail if\nripgrep does not install\" line.\n- **`release-please.yml`**: after the SDK-pin block, it checks the\nmerged release PR for `bypass-ripgrep-check` via the existing\nfail-closed `release_pr_has_label` helper and, when present, passes `-f\ndangerous-skip-ripgrep-check=true` to every dispatched package. Unlike\nthe SDK-pin check this is not package-gated, because every package's\npublish run shares the same ripgrep step. The dispatch log, step\nsummary, and recovery commands all surface the override.\n- **`release.yml`**: a new `dangerous-skip-ripgrep-check` boolean input\nis logged in the dispatch-inputs summary and softens the `Install\nripgrep` step — a failure is tolerated and `DEEPAGENTS_RIPGREP_EXPECTED`\nleft unset only when the input is `true`.\n\nScope: the label is honored only on release PRs. `push`-to-`main` and\nmerge-queue runs have no PR label to read, so they always enforce the\nstrict install.\n\nThe label must be created in repo settings (`bypass-ripgrep-check`)\nbefore this can take effect; documented under \"Release Failed: Ripgrep\nInstall\" in `RELEASING.md`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Extended `test_ci_workflow.py` with an executable\n`test_strict_ripgrep_install_bypass` that runs the strict step's real\n`run:` body against stubbed `apt-get`/`rg`/`dpkg`: unlabeled apt\nfailures fail with the original exit code; labeled failures are\ntolerated; ripgrep is only promised to the tests when `rg` is actually\nusable; a bypassed leg with no usable `rg` emits the marker artifact.\n- Updated the strict-step and upload-step drift assertions to match the\nnew condition and artifact selection, and added comment-workflow\nassertions for the label read and bypass wording.\n- All 1108 workflow-helper tests pass; the touched YAML files parse; the\nnew bash bodies pass `bash -n`; the comment workflow's JS passes `node\n--check`; ruff check/format clean on the test file.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-08-19T21:44:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a0990ff0d9c40276fc55e47c8fd44c798e8f858d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6"}]},{"sha":"81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgxYzZlMjk1Nzc1MjViZGM2MGNmMTM5MDk4NDMwYmU0YmFjMGVmZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T20:27:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:27:36Z"},"message":"fix(infra): unset `UV_PYTHON` when installing release wheels with `uv pip` (#5655)\n\nRelease dependency validation and release import steps no longer fail\nwith `No virtual environment found for Python 3.14` when the release\npackage targets a different Python than the one setup-uv installed.\n\n---\n\nThe `uv_setup` composite action installs Python 3.14 for running helper\nscripts, and `setup-uv` exports `UV_PYTHON=3.14` job-wide. `UV_PYTHON`\ntakes precedence over `VIRTUAL_ENV` for `uv pip install`, so when the\nfreshness gate (or release import test) created a venv from the release\npackage's own `python_version` (e.g. 3.12) and then ran `VIRTUAL_ENV=...\nuv pip install`, uv refused to use it:\n\n```\nerror: No virtual environment found for Python 3.14; run `uv venv` to create an environment, or pass `--system` to install into a non-virtual environment\n```\n\nSeen on the `deepagents-code` 0.1.58 release PR:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32297131672/job/96211155972\n\nThe fix prefixes each `uv pip install` in these steps with `env -u\nUV_PYTHON` so the install targets the venv the step just created. This\naffected three call sites: the \"Install wheel with dependencies from\nPyPI\" step in `check_dep_freshness.yml`, and the \"Import dist package\" /\n\"Import published package (again)\" steps in `release.yml` — the latter\ntwo haven't failed only because the package Python happened to match the\nsetup version recently. The workflow-mirror test asserting the shared\ninstall invocation is updated to match.","tree":{"sha":"0ad8d925d5525f57576b03c8bea59a409d10866d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0ad8d925d5525f57576b03c8bea59a409d10866d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhhG4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmCoQAFJI+8QlssLS3LIBhYCtuWv5\n2u/QkUY4Ijz7EaR25yOMwgdOyd7EjG+z4uNKsmryUXcu7IrPLlNTt3IXI2vpZ1UV\n6KwwHNVsIp4DfVCdK9emYuPMeuEuOo8tSdDiZumTIIw/BsT6+v4DqnTFjfqERbhA\ntTyk/qIKsQN6ezQGH8coaKODEVhhdp3tbQUyHUc1LZzD7PHO7D0zWdc1W/1YuKwu\nBYv86X6UglNq3vDSGSnjHq574jwHIzGAvjz6T4X+l4O5ZeUbddEyzzKKlapG7erX\nRoapjQU/yW8NgOPayFRGgKNgwhS6SGImr1rXaiEXAwL7/3XIvwC0xnrhN7k9o+ys\nosYhfmyH3JLyCNNc1vzr+O1w3kWxim5P8QqJUzXNJnY3J8b3gG7GyWw8rVn8sEIf\nx2uZEv4k+C3BA6p5Wg491prf+fqnEXJP30FxcXqVDzIl1oIX521/aSOqiqqqTPZh\nHXBPmJpnz/bao74nrLx4j6Xi43K5Oq2G2oAbzUodnOdYyzyWSTfuOjDFwXJcXG1X\n0NYI2eh2l80yE2tVsjzsyw+cwj0hFOFvspxDvpRNwN3mjkzsAl7wWJ1FVWhN3czy\nNykUHXXMF48jaPBBGhCTgN+0y1F+YnpQe2zeNSSEqF1K5pTplTtDOdiMakry6cS7\nExWar7GGyeDqcTmQmoB4\n=R5FB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0ad8d925d5525f57576b03c8bea59a409d10866d\nparent 28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787171256 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787171256 -0400\n\nfix(infra): unset `UV_PYTHON` when installing release wheels with `uv pip` (#5655)\n\nRelease dependency validation and release import steps no longer fail\nwith `No virtual environment found for Python 3.14` when the release\npackage targets a different Python than the one setup-uv installed.\n\n---\n\nThe `uv_setup` composite action installs Python 3.14 for running helper\nscripts, and `setup-uv` exports `UV_PYTHON=3.14` job-wide. `UV_PYTHON`\ntakes precedence over `VIRTUAL_ENV` for `uv pip install`, so when the\nfreshness gate (or release import test) created a venv from the release\npackage's own `python_version` (e.g. 3.12) and then ran `VIRTUAL_ENV=...\nuv pip install`, uv refused to use it:\n\n```\nerror: No virtual environment found for Python 3.14; run `uv venv` to create an environment, or pass `--system` to install into a non-virtual environment\n```\n\nSeen on the `deepagents-code` 0.1.58 release PR:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32297131672/job/96211155972\n\nThe fix prefixes each `uv pip install` in these steps with `env -u\nUV_PYTHON` so the install targets the venv the step just created. This\naffected three call sites: the \"Install wheel with dependencies from\nPyPI\" step in `check_dep_freshness.yml`, and the \"Import dist package\" /\n\"Import published package (again)\" steps in `release.yml` — the latter\ntwo haven't failed only because the package Python happened to match the\nsetup version recently. The workflow-mirror test asserting the shared\ninstall invocation is updated to match.","verified_at":"2026-08-19T20:27:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81c6e29577525bdc60cf139098430be4bac0efe6/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22"}]},{"sha":"28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI4ZDQ0ZDQ5Yzg3ODAwODhhODViZTU2ZGMzMDA5YjAyNmFmYWJhMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T20:24:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:24:37Z"},"message":"feat(infra): name the package in curated release-notes check output (#5656)\n\nThe curated release-notes refresh runs share one package-agnostic job\nname (\"Refresh curated release notes check\") across every open release\nPR, and neither the job output nor the refreshed check named the package\nor version being validated. A failure run surfaced only a bare list of\nstale-state reasons (\"applied metadata references an older override\ncomment; …\"), leaving no indication of which component was gated or\nwhether the failure was a real verdict versus a validator error.\n\n`checkCuratedState` now returns the resolved `component` and `version`\non every status it reaches after resolving them, and the workflow\nthreads them through the output:\n\n- The job log line reads `Curated release-note state for the <component>\n<version> release PR: <status>.`\n- The refreshed check's title and summary name the target, e.g. `Curated\nrelease notes are valid for the deepagents-code 0.1.58 release PR`.\n- The `setFailed` annotation behind a `failed` result is prefixed with\n`for <component> <version>:` so the annotation GitHub surfaces on the\nrun identifies the package on its own.\n\nThe failure conclusion itself is unchanged and is by design: dispatch\nruns execute from `main`, so the run's native job conclusion is how the\ngate reports the release PR's state — `setFailed` marks the run failed\nwhenever the curated notes are stale, which is distinct from a validator\nerror (that path gets its own \"hit an error talking to GitHub\" check\nsummary).","tree":{"sha":"23120418fd8fa42c013bbffb999a9a4722191347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/23120418fd8fa42c013bbffb999a9a4722191347"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhhEFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfEUQAHR5SQG/8XnbgNUgJWxt0wJg\ndgX6RKsEeRmYa8yAmlsj1u4qJ10s9cEIfpChewyLGF1UQQD2m7zPQjxsusTy3237\nzKa3imluoyZM8ABsdV0hLV7LHoYROIuAnm2UZhH63OfAVBysQQjNJvhGjWjuHFCR\nBol79tLW3YnEVCf07GSuGrqR4vO4jFLLu+3rbAXmuyrUu75S93HWrcZEY6KcR2Yr\nOt5cTKA8UnD8PEpO12sSlTXfmf+oskT/r6fEdiT07m/PDsncwd9Za83fYHWygcpr\n86ybc3AO1sVkZL37pWHLEruCtfSEPYW+r427leU/R4NoriNNmuq82p6EsQ7bW7+l\nVwJq1asMfFgoDZwKPEjV3XI8cqH2lhWG24AauJgSMsE1NtVHJGpqHe9IyWTUDp4H\nOqJ/FZg3NAEvS51a2mN7g5M2vOjdVXa3wCLelohb0bApCp+bHCcIXyQ+6bGgwemp\n+Rm7eA49wy8lxxDyUyHdMRELxJ6AvTeHCsEbWoDbwNhmMenYMOLKPLq7xweUsfWz\nN1ILt1LaGh0eYss/HWQOU7XIu1YAuWHP4F4e8zamZ2D6UEljHDLXj0r13Edwutvj\nDG4ikMT5RAg7+SOFsuZ2N0+Xw2j09krwRd8kg1QOgm+9wYzfKuPwH1nW8CTdmAC4\nG/yOq51/DSAxqngmfOa0\n=NBlg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 23120418fd8fa42c013bbffb999a9a4722191347\nparent 2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787171077 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787171077 -0400\n\nfeat(infra): name the package in curated release-notes check output (#5656)\n\nThe curated release-notes refresh runs share one package-agnostic job\nname (\"Refresh curated release notes check\") across every open release\nPR, and neither the job output nor the refreshed check named the package\nor version being validated. A failure run surfaced only a bare list of\nstale-state reasons (\"applied metadata references an older override\ncomment; …\"), leaving no indication of which component was gated or\nwhether the failure was a real verdict versus a validator error.\n\n`checkCuratedState` now returns the resolved `component` and `version`\non every status it reaches after resolving them, and the workflow\nthreads them through the output:\n\n- The job log line reads `Curated release-note state for the <component>\n<version> release PR: <status>.`\n- The refreshed check's title and summary name the target, e.g. `Curated\nrelease notes are valid for the deepagents-code 0.1.58 release PR`.\n- The `setFailed` annotation behind a `failed` result is prefixed with\n`for <component> <version>:` so the annotation GitHub surfaces on the\nrun identifies the package on its own.\n\nThe failure conclusion itself is unchanged and is by design: dispatch\nruns execute from `main`, so the run's native job conclusion is how the\ngate reports the release PR's state — `setFailed` marks the run failed\nwhenever the curated notes are stale, which is distinct from a validator\nerror (that path gets its own \"hit an error talking to GitHub\" check\nsummary).","verified_at":"2026-08-19T20:24:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28d44d49c8780088a85be56dc3009b026afaba22/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5"}]},{"sha":"2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJjNjUwMmZlMzAyNDE0ODQ5NmZkMzVjNzAwNDljOGE0ZTBiNDRlYzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T20:08:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:08:03Z"},"message":"fix(infra): retry the new-entries warning comment and grant `pull-requests: write` (#5654)\n\nThe curated release notes check no longer logs a `Resource not\naccessible by integration` warning when posting its courtesy comment\nabout newly generated changelog entries on a release PR.\n\n---\n\nThe check posts a best-effort comment when the generated changelog\ndrifts from the curated draft. On [this\nrun](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32293839088/job/96201984315)\non #5591, that `POST\n/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5591/comments` returned 403 even\nthough the job token had `issues: write` — while an identical run 30\nminutes earlier on the same PR posted comments fine. The release PR\nbranch is owned by the `release-bot` app installation\n(`langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]`), and the token posting here is\n`github-actions[bot]`; every other workflow in this repo that comments\non PRs grants `pull-requests: write`, while this one granted only\n`issues: write` + `pull-requests: read`.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n- Grant `pull-requests: write` in `release_notes_check.yml`, matching\nthe other PR-commenting workflows.\n- Retry the courtesy comment up to 2 times (2s apart) before degrading\nto a log warning. The comment is intentionally non-blocking — the gate\nstill fails closed with its specific, actionable reason — but a\ntransient 403 shouldn't surface as a confusing warning, and in\n`issue_comment`/`workflow_dispatch` refresh runs it would otherwise\nleave the refreshed required check red over a courtesy comment.\n\nThe gate failure on that run was itself real\n(changelog/body/applied-commit drift) and is unaffected by this change;\nthis only fixes the courtesy-comment path.","tree":{"sha":"da0cc98a3a999b6c730a15e7f12fb5598eee98cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/da0cc98a3a999b6c730a15e7f12fb5598eee98cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhg0jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9bAQAKtlywsrvPd0ag1fRTcITOGV\nyZ3QJ4pPegqUY5rMy1hV9wmonHmseAvqJh2vvxmDL+wvk+YCahkw5cn8JGSJOS0d\nMfJkY8lY5fe1kuAs+pjDhhWKbwaEfmDTy7Lrs9UKN4eLWb2gbpZrra7NExh5E4ns\nwUzNMQVwaZf3uUND+f8Dk0+qO5NTJOItZStO+ZZSCZk/qrdB6850jFdpUsdWK1ve\nQCetfmeh2XNqXhnYEzbggFiAtFFllNq4Fcq5t8Y0mclFv/UjZIKC4xfab10OSkoz\natbw6weoV6QFk7cWJFHyMdbsTrIWzkn9IR0ow2ZmuLL/6U2TQCylzXpEuM4nip07\n3IGWr50dOw1ef9Hees0WeKOH/mclx8MBGYfwaQLZTnER0RiPBokd9fUZRBoUWVal\nf2aNJ/OcvhRTwyXODI2iK4Aits0hei8l7c+Ce2sYce3VhrjjvpXyU5WuWlNsvVMr\nQB6psA+SfnVqBV3njUhw99l5aJ7avZITMd/6XqdCmmrI8C56hgt1bSF4A1PtWj1U\nbPaNCUOsKmdVlxqzSjXcU9/kXdob+bjxiE5ToZVese+yZ75ZXfhHIxxRxFhpBWG1\njfzBcWoXX/LIhIUl4sd2+acMMgbe9uMaIjeE7DuHLQfT8fqgKhKBhQXLqua7d7MS\n5jalDKYykBY7u9yH4kLT\n=H5a9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree da0cc98a3a999b6c730a15e7f12fb5598eee98cd\nparent d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787170083 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787170083 -0400\n\nfix(infra): retry the new-entries warning comment and grant `pull-requests: write` (#5654)\n\nThe curated release notes check no longer logs a `Resource not\naccessible by integration` warning when posting its courtesy comment\nabout newly generated changelog entries on a release PR.\n\n---\n\nThe check posts a best-effort comment when the generated changelog\ndrifts from the curated draft. On [this\nrun](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32293839088/job/96201984315)\non #5591, that `POST\n/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5591/comments` returned 403 even\nthough the job token had `issues: write` — while an identical run 30\nminutes earlier on the same PR posted comments fine. The release PR\nbranch is owned by the `release-bot` app installation\n(`langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]`), and the token posting here is\n`github-actions[bot]`; every other workflow in this repo that comments\non PRs grants `pull-requests: write`, while this one granted only\n`issues: write` + `pull-requests: read`.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n- Grant `pull-requests: write` in `release_notes_check.yml`, matching\nthe other PR-commenting workflows.\n- Retry the courtesy comment up to 2 times (2s apart) before degrading\nto a log warning. The comment is intentionally non-blocking — the gate\nstill fails closed with its specific, actionable reason — but a\ntransient 403 shouldn't surface as a confusing warning, and in\n`issue_comment`/`workflow_dispatch` refresh runs it would otherwise\nleave the refreshed required check red over a courtesy comment.\n\nThe gate failure on that run was itself real\n(changelog/body/applied-commit drift) and is unaffected by this change;\nthis only fixes the courtesy-comment path.","verified_at":"2026-08-19T20:08:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c6502fe3024148496fd35c70049c8a4e0b44ec5/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab"}]},{"sha":"d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQwMDkyNmU5ZTAyNzhkNmU3NGY5MTYyMmIwMGQxMzc1YzdhZjE5YWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T20:04:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:04:54Z"},"message":"fix(code): let MCP footer wrap on narrow windows (#5651)\n\nThe `/mcp` viewer footer now wraps onto additional rows in narrow\nterminals instead of clipping its hints.\n\n---\n\nThe footer previously forced a single-row height even when the help text\nneeded more space. Content-driven height preserves every action hint,\nwith a focused Textual regression test covering the narrow layout.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/57acc062-3c83-5ae4-8e6a-193e3d42fce2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7e962ce6c2cf4a09086feab35b5aa91e549fc35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c7e962ce6c2cf4a09086feab35b5aa91e549fc35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgxmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ/MQABHycX+l9WHaTkIdSrEm4GWE\nAzGvMsDhp9RbauxW7pKZWn6KqSlokQtt0BgWL84AvdLTqXLFGQfB/lR01LAjsVeD\nEhFLR91HIR8lIaoPH+ZYhmq/PJKkJCa1E4ZplmAbLCrkwdOdfM9leuK9/8nByCIX\n3g6WC9KtEapFPjutEnQ5zRSbFM6vwEiJFSkxVt8DiKqx+Q8b5gCFDYMwi2MVGHk4\nEJV6EG1JAjMHcn+GzRlwMCY9/ifhnvZ9uipMLIS8x9+c+ICFoJSzYc+4mqhg+oEo\naYwhna7Sl331y5bZLr8+tlcdZ6VHgQT8+oUSxLZRn2Iv0xn4R6SBOapIsuwlrBrz\nb07+zRq2TS3vUnAGZ2Q1pHq7X6yN3ogX+MGSvqfmsf0nHudzMrDGxwFv2dmWh/lv\nl797D1eb/QZQMK9iIo8z7XLVxGBXkuTNhhPbPXveuEgMgcLJnIP0pdS6xW0HwFnN\nRCnCgEWlEVeL6PPj+9qBh3j6lVHl0YeiI7PeFYi8CaWkA/twewTCqBkQyzDKINuX\ntrN45SttxtGJ3ua2OrhRzW5+P5qLFVLvorTWdOEwb47/CbfLmfZgmyEpxbY7DpQL\noyf8x6+bL0hdR0I66YSfvTsgEUQwt7Mia+e88JhOEFBlAshfsub7xgSBt5vWxch4\ng+/0DBDN2NG62TGFGbRg\n=qo6G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c7e962ce6c2cf4a09086feab35b5aa91e549fc35\nparent 0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787169894 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787169894 -0400\n\nfix(code): let MCP footer wrap on narrow windows (#5651)\n\nThe `/mcp` viewer footer now wraps onto additional rows in narrow\nterminals instead of clipping its hints.\n\n---\n\nThe footer previously forced a single-row height even when the help text\nneeded more space. Content-driven height preserves every action hint,\nwith a focused Textual regression test covering the narrow layout.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/57acc062-3c83-5ae4-8e6a-193e3d42fce2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-19T20:04:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d00926e9e0278d6e74f91622b00d1375c7af19ab/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd"}]},{"sha":"0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAzOTlkZWE3ZDk5MDgyYjYzNDY4MjRmYzJlMjRjMTdjYTY2ZDhhZmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T19:53:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:53:21Z"},"message":"ci(infra): warn instead of fail on unreleased-Python caps in third-party deps (#5653)\n\nThe release dependency gate (`check_dep_freshness.yml` →\n`check_wheel_dep_freshness.py`) currently hard-fails a release PR when a\nthird-party dependency's newest published release declares a\n`requires-python` upper bound that excludes a CPython minor the wheel\nclaims but that has not shipped yet. This is blocking the\n`deepagents-code` 0.1.58 release PR (#5591): the wheel claims\n`>=3.12,<4.0`, and the optional `ibm` extra's\n`langchain-ibm>=1.1.0,<2.0.0` only publishes `<3.15,>=3.10`. pip already\nrefuses that extra on the unreleased interpreter and installs it fine on\n3.12–3.14, so the release is blocked purely on another project widening\nits bound.\n\nThis change downgrades that specific case from a hard `::error::` to a\n`::warning::` plus a step-summary note. The warning applies only when\nall of these hold:\n\n- the dependency is **third-party** — repo-managed siblings keep the\nstrict freshest-metadata assertion that caught the coordinated\nCode/Talon Python-floor bump;\n- a published release **satisfies the version constraint** (a missing\nrelease still fails);\n- the Python coverage gap is **exactly the next unreleased CPython minor\nthrough the wheel's ceiling** (e.g. `<3.15` while 3.14 is current).\n\nGaps at real installation targets still fail: the wheel's minimum\n(dependency rejects the install floor, e.g. dep requires `>=3.13`\nagainst the wheel's `>=3.12`), any middle minor (e.g. dep ships only\n`>=3.13,<3.14`), and patch-level exclusions on released lines.\n\nThe gate's \"latest existing minor\" anchor is the interpreter running the\ncheck; `check_dep_freshness.yml` pins that job to Python 3.14, so the\nverdict is deterministic per workflow, and the new unit tests pin\n`sys.version_info` to stay runner-independent.","tree":{"sha":"0f2fb53cb06ed883571747259e57dc8474d9c9af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0f2fb53cb06ed883571747259e57dc8474d9c9af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgmxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASMQQAISVXSlHx/guFlH8F+BSCFv4\n9NkOsq89bd/l4aK8xnvgCmuuZKVUiXHcvqJmN+xD+fXnYR1rr5p9cyy60sH5HQbv\nag+QSOu6VLpshpPlndbqwpm0ylBQ2It9938Wdgj6FsLsoW4SAVlbbQRL4KO5jZRz\nD+Od0Xd24fnZsVLmzik3m49E+Jj/6rR4ZSiYHWtszvum3vy4HrhxGEExVVl2zzVY\nMuHUtlwTBYpJnVBTVbCZzOBL4ug4I+OQUwujMmmHsCzNJsxkQXKwWI5dytoS90Et\nhihcjQTgfrPC+R3T+0zpBQmXzxBhdQlTCu6hE9GusuamzWy4fuYvFcxY2tHYFd/O\nz8fFK0TsR18s+pto68WaLKVe06M1yiTx1FAv8lia1EMTHMWkpPhivEb6Mu7hQo6m\nVPDRnZ66RXF+g7v/JumZBNBBwNfM9iOOtUQK0LnEjdaLEwuOQCVYsOokZbaKnZ+V\nKI0sBzyN80zfFqeRsUrUdh1hk/zZb0FAv15SX3FbSIL8BnrCGGnHISraCGjQE0XJ\nE8nBwG7f/0HQVVAV/1+c6X2rO5kyjXZpXXHehdvznWWp5cRhvFcA7L8pHER6u1fY\nxXSlWvsRMhDOIRwSlE1TYCZ3cetR7JuUXXB/S+wO+ZImHjCHjtVp3q5Barycs521\nIpgyIZyDJ54I/thbmFc1\n=CMKh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0f2fb53cb06ed883571747259e57dc8474d9c9af\nparent 240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787169201 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787169201 -0400\n\nci(infra): warn instead of fail on unreleased-Python caps in third-party deps (#5653)\n\nThe release dependency gate (`check_dep_freshness.yml` →\n`check_wheel_dep_freshness.py`) currently hard-fails a release PR when a\nthird-party dependency's newest published release declares a\n`requires-python` upper bound that excludes a CPython minor the wheel\nclaims but that has not shipped yet. This is blocking the\n`deepagents-code` 0.1.58 release PR (#5591): the wheel claims\n`>=3.12,<4.0`, and the optional `ibm` extra's\n`langchain-ibm>=1.1.0,<2.0.0` only publishes `<3.15,>=3.10`. pip already\nrefuses that extra on the unreleased interpreter and installs it fine on\n3.12–3.14, so the release is blocked purely on another project widening\nits bound.\n\nThis change downgrades that specific case from a hard `::error::` to a\n`::warning::` plus a step-summary note. The warning applies only when\nall of these hold:\n\n- the dependency is **third-party** — repo-managed siblings keep the\nstrict freshest-metadata assertion that caught the coordinated\nCode/Talon Python-floor bump;\n- a published release **satisfies the version constraint** (a missing\nrelease still fails);\n- the Python coverage gap is **exactly the next unreleased CPython minor\nthrough the wheel's ceiling** (e.g. `<3.15` while 3.14 is current).\n\nGaps at real installation targets still fail: the wheel's minimum\n(dependency rejects the install floor, e.g. dep requires `>=3.13`\nagainst the wheel's `>=3.12`), any middle minor (e.g. dep ships only\n`>=3.13,<3.14`), and patch-level exclusions on released lines.\n\nThe gate's \"latest existing minor\" anchor is the interpreter running the\ncheck; `check_dep_freshness.yml` pins that job to Python 3.14, so the\nverdict is deterministic per workflow, and the new unit tests pin\n`sys.version_info` to stay runner-independent.","verified_at":"2026-08-19T19:53:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0399dea7d99082b6346824fc2e24c17ca66d8afd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867"}]},{"sha":"240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI0MGZkYmYzNjQ2MDQ1MGI4NmRlYWM0ZWE1MzAwNDAxNjU0Nzg4Njc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T19:31:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:31:54Z"},"message":"ci(ci): bound ripgrep install on ordinary PRs (#5642)\n\nSlow apt metadata refreshes should not block ordinary pull-request\nvalidation, so non-release PR jobs now continue after a two-minute\nripgrep install timeout and publish a sticky warning after CI. Release\nPRs, merge-queue/main runs, and release artifact tests keep the strict\ninstall path.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- 90 workflow contract tests pass; changed workflows also parse as valid\nYAML.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1a61b60c-cf77-5b18-83d9-3a2028f55fb6)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d8516073bdf20a50d06b2beaad1f1eccd9e2e177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d8516073bdf20a50d06b2beaad1f1eccd9e2e177"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgSqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsrUQADXfukEYqg78bx2seQShWqhP\nsWk6TzMG55mDIIMaJ6sMLZzJ1pgmJOJ9dLbRuBs3ErtwLoCtEj7IUW2dSvG6GHIi\n1no4gHV2lVt/K5ev0W+9QnWYsEwk7qMAI16FvS8e9QbdEMISOFkDVrYT+wGhixS8\nG1FtMnvPeo6jnwCQ30oLLqJdUdJ0suyPmkF0O66hknTsrB7roV4rbKSNVSOqZVXi\nMdiRyaQwu+3pDZDuHxzK22T7O1FuBcFCJzMG2teBtPvBEw26jn1PWLmMu0GLbYTr\nK03nXgDQ3OeiD/mCr1NcRn08g+y6l/hRiK2BMICovP2mkZmB2isdSLIfcyr52cVl\nQPxjLXTa9wnTCE+yTXuvwG7dHgUVeBvJgOq/FlDfXu+I4doAo+N+fhCEgTURwfqL\nnyBTc14v6lkDXdY5SN+JmQKTLzoMouB0FYJpMRzdcsfUAy02/PY3nmEAMTIjfSoz\npkoBBmnVqQVHqj0kIzxSurvcdyZoVXxzxRr4xUy2eKXc6/GbWc8kQmAuetc5qVgk\n3UbkB2ekXkj92cMPb7mGI4OMorGvHA2kj6/BCoYvZ/jVqyDqyZyB+XpQjQXp9x49\nCImyxfkuKzpVr/mSRFdS8D5Ng9fKU9x0jsAqcB+iYs8r2I++QjGDcgw/0dPcwanO\nDi7f3cIDhlF6kqIbKeYf\n=W9+S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d8516073bdf20a50d06b2beaad1f1eccd9e2e177\nparent a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787167914 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787167914 -0400\n\nci(ci): bound ripgrep install on ordinary PRs (#5642)\n\nSlow apt metadata refreshes should not block ordinary pull-request\nvalidation, so non-release PR jobs now continue after a two-minute\nripgrep install timeout and publish a sticky warning after CI. Release\nPRs, merge-queue/main runs, and release artifact tests keep the strict\ninstall path.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- 90 workflow contract tests pass; changed workflows also parse as valid\nYAML.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1a61b60c-cf77-5b18-83d9-3a2028f55fb6)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-19T19:31:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/240fdbf36460450b86deac4ea530040165478867/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151"}]},{"sha":"a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE2MWJjNmZlZWI2YWVmZDc4MGFkODQzNWFjYzljZTIwNTdmZTkxNTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T19:18:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:18:58Z"},"message":"fix(code): capture stdio MCP server stderr into the logger (#5610)\n\nStdio MCP server diagnostics are now captured in DEBUG logs during tool\ndiscovery and runtime sessions. Debug log files are restricted to\nuser-only permissions; captured output is sanitized and bounded, but can\nstill contain sensitive server-provided values.\n\n---\n\nThe MCP adapter discarded stdio server stderr, leaving subprocess\nfailures invisible. This routes the SDK stderr pipe through a dedicated\ndrain thread without blocking the event loop while preserving remote\ntransports and stdio environment behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a67e65dd-990f-502c-8aa9-ed8dcaf08060)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a67e65dd-990f-502c-8aa9-ed8dcaf08060/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ccd5cd8f1f75e53c84b23ab7d0ef5ca11a9e075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9ccd5cd8f1f75e53c84b23ab7d0ef5ca11a9e075"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgGiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5BAQAGRl53SHWYWCgWhuXiFsSl3W\nQrT7FLDjHfzkZc1QvY64xwMyfCm6QjlyUyXRy6CXdYVSPd75bXdhl9VL/o016/4J\n544WpcT9+r4hJ9W9/fCZzhpwFaLDi1kRPNaHiPEj19AU4OE3TP2wW2nUPbEQefFC\npF2Li5YM5coGVLIK3CTJcJnjKudjoZWHPz+OufAauvqKuZP382G8FzYPM/Vz1Y+y\n3Tg6L5KEcizZSe99/31gfsvd5ZH3IKCJt3P6hOfhkfIMeWJhc93VzMKUrDB+ziYZ\nc37/rz+wNKDkni7UzMOHq64CRzDgGGBwCC3elUjSFYEmvLCOMxmfN2Nvf8dITH3R\nlocHZ3fXIxPBz/iJzA6wV5LlRHd1RCoZjcgY1Kt7QpcJ5XFezwF6ROJqyhZXLymS\nP7/hhbv6LEsO2dgNrMs8SU7on1mQVjOf+xwtrvAhbWzVaNi9jixtXvgRvHZMoFr5\nMPq/OLhiDrl908X+sjr0Kbr495Bmfa8RT/I1Hz1EA70lemf1xmCvTV5D4ybjnRtv\nrR37W3jTLtS3Zt1dJJT/44bdTthcwX+15gIxLV2Fr8uhCnSAAv15V71HOB9sCJ2V\n9E0qv2Fh3dnoQPuy05mAujqlKHEQL4L9aWg7w9l7yFkwPVWclGhONiTZk9eswo8R\njDPSlbez8O9JSAikh71v\n=caTS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9ccd5cd8f1f75e53c84b23ab7d0ef5ca11a9e075\nparent d7c24d85f7b4d478116f022e1e969ddac89aeb2f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787167138 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787167138 -0400\n\nfix(code): capture stdio MCP server stderr into the logger (#5610)\n\nStdio MCP server diagnostics are now captured in DEBUG logs during tool\ndiscovery and runtime sessions. Debug log files are restricted to\nuser-only permissions; captured output is sanitized and bounded, but can\nstill contain sensitive server-provided values.\n\n---\n\nThe MCP adapter discarded stdio server stderr, leaving subprocess\nfailures invisible. This routes the SDK stderr pipe through a dedicated\ndrain thread without blocking the event loop while preserving remote\ntransports and stdio environment behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a67e65dd-990f-502c-8aa9-ed8dcaf08060)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a67e65dd-990f-502c-8aa9-ed8dcaf08060/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-19T19:18:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a61bc6feeb6aefd780ad8435acc9ce2057fe9151/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d7c24d85f7b4d478116f022e1e969ddac89aeb2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d7c24d85f7b4d478116f022e1e969ddac89aeb2f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d7c24d85f7b4d478116f022e1e969ddac89aeb2f"}]},{"sha":"d7c24d85f7b4d478116f022e1e969ddac89aeb2f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ3YzI0ZDg1ZjdiNGQ0NzgxMTZmMDIyZTFlOTY5ZGRhYzg5YWViMmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-19T18:49:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-19T18:49:13Z"},"message":"feat(code): re-auth MCP servers from viewer (#5637)\n\nUsers can sign in again to an OAuth-backed MCP server by selecting it in\n`/mcp` and pressing Enter.\n\n## Re-auth from the viewer\n\nA healthy OAuth-backed remote server can be re-authenticated in place:\nactivating its header (Enter, or a second click on the selected header)\ndismisses the viewer with the server name, and the app drives the\nexisting in-TUI OAuth flow and reconnect prompt. The action is\nadvertised in the footer, which shows `Enter re-auth` only when the\ncursor is on a row where Enter actually does that.\n\nThe affordance appears only where it means something. `_can_start_login`\nrequires the new `MCPServerInfo.uses_oauth`, which mirrors the condition\n`mcp_tools` already uses to attach an OAuth provider to a connection:\n\n```python\nexplicit_oauth or (stored_tokens is not None and not has_authorization_header)\n```\n\nSo a server behind a static `Authorization` header does not offer\nre-auth — that header takes precedence over stored OAuth tokens, and\nre-authorizing would change nothing. Neither does a public server with\nno OAuth flow to run. Healthy stdio, `awaiting_reconnect`, and\n`disabled` headers stay no-ops, and `error` headers still open the\ndetail modal.\n\n## Explicit login now forces a fresh grant\n\n`mcp_auth.login()` did not invalidate the stored token before the\nhandshake. For a healthy server that token is still valid, so the SDK\nattached it, the handshake succeeded with no authorization prompt, and\nthe user saw success for a sign-in that never happened:\n\n```\nLogged in to MCP server 'notion'. Tokens saved to ~/.deepagents/.state/mcp-tokens/notion-1cbd18bf.json\n```\n\n...followed by a reconnect prompt they did not need.\n\nThe provider is now built over `_FreshLoginTokenStorage`, a\n`FileTokenStorage` subclass whose token getters return `None`. The SDK\ncannot see an existing token, so an explicit login always runs the full\nauthorization flow.\n\nTwo details worth review:\n\n- **The token is hidden, not deleted.** Clearing it up front would log\nthe user out of a working server if they cancelled the browser prompt.\nHiding it means an aborted or failed flow leaves the credential on disk\nuntouched; a successful flow overwrites it through `set_tokens`.\n- **This applies to every explicit login, including `/mcp login\n<server>`.** An explicit login should re-authorize whatever the entry\npoint, so there is no re-auth intent flag to keep in sync. An\n`unauthenticated` server has no token to hide, so its behavior is\nunchanged. GitHub was already correct — its provider `run_login` runs\nthe device flow unconditionally and never reaches this handshake.\n\nClient registration and OAuth metadata still resolve from disk, so the\nhandshake reuses the existing DCR rather than re-registering against a\nnew redirect URI.\n\n## Footer follows the selected row\n\nThe footer previously advertised a static `Enter expand/login/details`\non every row. It now describes what Enter does on the row the cursor is\non, and omits the hint entirely when Enter does nothing:\n\n| Selected row | Footer |\n| --- | --- |\n| Tool | `Enter expand/collapse` |\n| Unauthenticated server | `Enter log in` |\n| OAuth-backed remote server | `Enter re-auth` |\n| Error server | `Enter details` |\n| Healthy stdio / non-OAuth / disabled | *(no Enter hint)* |\n\n`_update_help_text` refreshes it on cursor moves, filter changes, and\nthe F2 disable/enable toggle. With the footer carrying the action hint,\nserver headers no longer repeat it inline — the header shows only the\nstatus summary (transport, tool count), keeping one line per server.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ad87cb83-8fd6-545c-a021-866734144ff0)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4915f9e231d4837bf06ca8af7e19acc726444f75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4915f9e231d4837bf06ca8af7e19acc726444f75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d7c24d85f7b4d478116f022e1e969ddac89aeb2f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhfqpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGOEQAIBPv8KSoPYPCOBUCj+2bTrL\nI+F4IFVr+Ip2NCfce3Ib+SBbAXUUYnCb4FBbqd6iy6KTnXmMp7HtZ8q218YFgve2\ns1tfM+gy3Q1e348i5ieqiVqU+o3uLCmzVtPYKzxwzwdvQKJcYH+YrPbAnf8jgTG6\nLv6JlzxlnsbDUbdknjX5Exz3tGjyMvLSMCbShTqkzX8+ztK1bNLWocdN3iIP4UKp\nuDYo5oM7Ib9Q7d2J9BGrrt89kX6mA38Yk5LYBRZciFgifLIgf0Zizj+3eDESsWfx\n6/FJ5BvH7G+sXR8REbOH59R9vT2OP2NPIx5vphGe3wB/SzC/ATF45wG/td4pAcYO\nUlsf4/jKonviCyQahFRRpRlF1GSi17hwcmgvRzgT+R2j9s/aQ0F79iXkNzE1ePE1\nxhq2K1z2oLDJZXYa+cTUFY6ZXAdWgYEG6VRL4mu8olxY0sav6nFOH+amyZTB2Hzo\nwapbwD8SzoOS160mvCs3amS9IewKLffHkTZlTjZ50VUAIk5N6BNR1vbEGcNp7WEl\npnLGEdjrMBEPcgL6ErJH+mRqRB0xJ7TSrXgifgrf2b9d/gyx4OM5RuU6qgs8ZO4F\nfQnzvCCQY6QU0yHY2MTqC8zVuYLW8cqh1x1tNDRhMxNbUbFI4QiiW7XRNSzHVEbd\nZZ3PkwUeIvnySzR4bmJK\n=QPJ9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4915f9e231d4837bf06ca8af7e19acc726444f75\nparent 80e3d4738e0464cc3a6c5f9dfc27efc0128a9a00\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787165353 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787165353 -0400\n\nfeat(code): re-auth MCP servers from viewer (#5637)\n\nUsers can sign in again to an OAuth-backed MCP server by selecting it in\n`/mcp` and pressing Enter.\n\n## Re-auth from the viewer\n\nA healthy OAuth-backed remote server can be re-authenticated in place:\nactivating its header (Enter, or a second click on the selected header)\ndismisses the viewer with the server name, and the app drives the\nexisting in-TUI OAuth flow and reconnect prompt. The action is\nadvertised in the footer, which shows `Enter re-auth` only when the\ncursor is on a row where Enter actually does that.\n\nThe affordance appears only where it means something. `_can_start_login`\nrequires the new `MCPServerInfo.uses_oauth`, which mirrors the condition\n`mcp_tools` already uses to attach an OAuth provider to a connection:\n\n```python\nexplicit_oauth or (stored_tokens is not None and not has_authorization_header)\n```\n\nSo a server behind a static `Authorization` header does not offer\nre-auth — that header takes precedence over stored OAuth tokens, and\nre-authorizing would change nothing. Neither does a public server with\nno OAuth flow to run. Healthy stdio, `awaiting_reconnect`, and\n`disabled` headers stay no-ops, and `error` headers still open the\ndetail modal.\n\n## Explicit login now forces a fresh grant\n\n`mcp_auth.login()` did not invalidate the stored token before the\nhandshake. For a healthy server that token is still valid, so the SDK\nattached it, the handshake succeeded with no authorization prompt, and\nthe user saw success for a sign-in that never happened:\n\n```\nLogged in to MCP server 'notion'. Tokens saved to ~/.deepagents/.state/mcp-tokens/notion-1cbd18bf.json\n```\n\n...followed by a reconnect prompt they did not need.\n\nThe provider is now built over `_FreshLoginTokenStorage`, a\n`FileTokenStorage` subclass whose token getters return `None`. The SDK\ncannot see an existing token, so an explicit login always runs the full\nauthorization flow.\n\nTwo details worth review:\n\n- **The token is hidden, not deleted.** Clearing it up front would log\nthe user out of a working server if they cancelled the browser prompt.\nHiding it means an aborted or failed flow leaves the credential on disk\nuntouched; a successful flow overwrites it through `set_tokens`.\n- **This applies to every explicit login, including `/mcp login\n<server>`.** An explicit login should re-authorize whatever the entry\npoint, so there is no re-auth intent flag to keep in sync. An\n`unauthenticated` server has no token to hide, so its behavior is\nunchanged. GitHub was already correct — its provider `run_login` runs\nthe device flow unconditionally and never reaches this handshake.\n\nClient registration and OAuth metadata still resolve from disk, so the\nhandshake reuses the existing DCR rather than re-registering against a\nnew redirect URI.\n\n## Footer follows the selected row\n\nThe footer previously advertised a static `Enter expand/login/details`\non every row. It now describes what Enter does on the row the cursor is\non, and omits the hint entirely when Enter does nothing:\n\n| Selected row | Footer |\n| --- | --- |\n| Tool | `Enter expand/collapse` |\n| Unauthenticated server | `Enter log in` |\n| OAuth-backed remote server | `Enter re-auth` |\n| Error server | `Enter details` |\n| Healthy stdio / non-OAuth / disabled | *(no Enter hint)* |\n\n`_update_help_text` refreshes it on cursor moves, filter changes, and\nthe F2 disable/enable toggle. With the footer carrying the action hint,\nserver headers no longer repeat it inline — the header shows only the\nstatus summary (transport, tool count), keeping one line per server.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ad87cb83-8fd6-545c-a021-866734144ff0)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-19T18:49:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d7c24d85f7b4d478116f022e1e969ddac89aeb2f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commi