rihM8xKp68UU+aLkQATcDlfo7WM9ojaWDElHwhzRkFtHcOU92kYiQUklZvYeMA3z\n48Z77EYCdRlU9Sd55yuSkwai8zufAvVhr6PRj3i6Wtbqx4fjPdCKWV5wlYvsv7qN\n+ol8bA0nqsbIC9X7XEEme7vilBIuq53UtKc/Qqs6+ZK3nfrkOlMLL9ZTTSgyMQqP\npZX7Kz+dI+Q5pIB/sdj855SL7Vbg/qe+lMk95v2clbNMF6myVnY2cRsFdfzZewzm\nV97VPFfZE8RSX7pciqS/\n=6BXP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d951c224cfe49497562cf83ea042c001b8aa9928\nparent 84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787074489 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787074489 -0400\n\nfix(code): omit unavailable web-search prompt guidance (#5602)\n\nWeb-search guidance is now omitted from dcode's system prompt when\nTavily is not configured.\n\n---\n\nThe `web_search` tool binding already uses `settings.has_tavily`;\napplying the same gate during prompt construction keeps model-facing\nguidance aligned with the available tool set and avoids unnecessary\ntokens.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4a40ddc0-5348-5793-8fd3-eda1881a1abb)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T17:34:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9feaf51030a30203f43231b7fb9420293be9fedc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9feaf51030a30203f43231b7fb9420293be9fedc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9feaf51030a30203f43231b7fb9420293be9fedc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130"}]},{"sha":"84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg0ZWIwOWQ4ZWRhYTUyMjk3Y2EzZTJhZDc2YTJjODVhOWFkZjQxMzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T16:34:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T16:34:43Z"},"message":"fix(code): complete the `dcode config` surface (#5581)\n\nSupersedes #5219, #5225\n\n`dcode config` had four ways it could mislead you about your own\nsettings. This PR fixes all of them: it could report a value the running\napp ignores, it could print tables that contain credentials, several\n`config.toml` sections the app reads were invisible to it, and two kinds\nof bad input failed silently. The command and the app now share one\nresolver, so they can't disagree.\n\n---\n\n## The specific gaps\n\n**1. `dcode config` could show a classifier model the app isn't using.**\nA blank `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_AUTO_CLASSIFIER_MODEL` means \"inherit the main\nagent model\" and deliberately outranks `config.toml`. The CLI resolved\noptions through the generic scalar path, which treats a blank env var as\nunset — so with a blank env var and a `config.toml` value set, the app\nuses your main model while `dcode config get models.auto_classifier`\nreported the config-file model. This option picks which model reviews\ngated actions, so the two surfaces disagreeing here is the worst case.\nBoth now call the same resolver\n(`resolve_auto_classifier_model_with_source`), and the source line\ncredits the blank env var that forced the inherit.\n\n**2. Tables that can hold credentials were printed raw, or rejected as\nunknown.**\n`[async_subagents]` headers, `[models.providers]`, and\n`[sandboxes.providers]` can carry `Authorization` tokens and constructor\nparams. They weren't in the manifest at all, so `dcode config` either\nsaid \"unknown option\" or printed the full table. They're now flagged\n`redacted`: presence and source are reported, the values never are.\n\n```\n$ dcode config get agents.async_subagents\nagents.async_subagents = configured  (config.toml)\n```\n\nRedaction is enforced in all three output paths (table display, `config\n--json` rows, and single-key JSON), so a new output path can't\naccidentally leak them.\n\n**3. Whole sections the app reads were missing from the manifest.**\n`[models.providers]`, `[sandboxes]`, `[agents]`, `[retries]`, and\n`[themes]` now show up in `dcode config list`. Three display settings\nthat were previously hardcoded one-off readers — cursor blink, terminal\nprogress, and message timestamps — are now manifest options with their\nown env vars (`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_CURSOR_BLINK`,\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_TERMINAL_PROGRESS`,\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SHOW_MESSAGE_TIMESTAMPS`), so they follow the same env\n→ config → default precedence as everything else. The four copy-pasted\nTOML readers in `app.py` collapsed into one shared\n`_load_bool_display_preference`, and a test pins each caller's fallback\nto the manifest default so they can't drift.\n\n**4. Two silent failure modes now log.**\n- A whitespace-only env var (`export DEEPAGENTS_CODE_THEME=\"$UNSET \"`)\nwas discarded with no trace — and for `empty_env_is_false` options it\nactually forced `False` over your `config.toml`. Both cases now log.\n- A scalar shadowing a table (`ui = \"dark\"` at the top level of\n`config.toml`) silently defaulted every option under `[ui]`. This now\nlogs once per path, since the manifest resolves ~100 options in one pass\nand per-option logging would print the same line ~100 times.\n\n**5. `dcode config` credited values the app refuses.**\nTwo new option kinds enforce the runtime's validation at read time:\n`NON_NEGATIVE_INT` rejects a negative retry count, `NON_EMPTY_STR`\nrejects a blank agent name. Both now correctly read `(unset)`.\n\n## Why one resolver\n\nThe root cause of gaps 1 and 5 was the CLI maintaining its own\nresolution logic that didn't know the runtime's override rules. Every\nfix above routes both surfaces through the manifest, so the CLI reports\nwhat the app does by construction rather than by convention. A\nmanifest-drift test rejects new hand-written readers (like the old\n`[ui]` loaders) so the manifest stays the single source.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f7c2602aa15a1ed505ebf4287ce586b395e940e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5f7c2602aa15a1ed505ebf4287ce586b395e940e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhImjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjxIQADkLxMtnt9C8JZooC7X4qOTD\no7BldkZbfeFfhL4NNzBc1uZmCvDeQYWbi+fa/r5sgPEbaGnXH1+d891YZmlbURsK\nvXUAf1HSkf/r1rqw0agop6kLfXEO2Wv4RoBHAnTZt/K88zEA2RZ2cX3QtK+0ToKG\nGIBnmV+/DiWGXmgn94pkap5rLG44GWzcU91JYBzquLfCAEKmPU3ORFE5y9NKfUAZ\nyvGxJiyG0yy97fBZFW7PHD0Hh4cDN2VHNRxkdcaObPBu1jOccQS5//ebLxbDaZK6\nsR42uGJDecG7lo20kgwITmIfyTPALPKzrNTEleHVlEsc7kcgIIJDy8yDtydU01d8\nHxMHjh07ijkxFWvuNufvaQtmFPQaAkJsbKPn7mKwu6geR7k3jyFnexWuOg2tAnPc\nsGmgwU2VnTsY1mykMkXIsBOEmt2She3mmF0WkTnubAZOoQx39j+mHUuVkA4sUDo7\n94fvESJBfIvu9M7cYxPCLhu7hdUrfZOaxgRUzRb7h/nz07L9R8eTbdtfH1RrIVoC\nBmYAr6jJnooqf8tNHHvoL2EwaE9t87HRQwv0FjP3IGwuqYsZGmZbWygrgK7WsToH\nMquDAGGEdeOzekYdWQtBALEXTjvco9Z09FxjzaGNcWGcv6BjDTl5BwyNoiuz8hDD\nB9khgtQ/wdtAYRn9sZ1n\n=lbb4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5f7c2602aa15a1ed505ebf4287ce586b395e940e\nparent 345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787070883 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787070883 -0400\n\nfix(code): complete the `dcode config` surface (#5581)\n\nSupersedes #5219, #5225\n\n`dcode config` had four ways it could mislead you about your own\nsettings. This PR fixes all of them: it could report a value the running\napp ignores, it could print tables that contain credentials, several\n`config.toml` sections the app reads were invisible to it, and two kinds\nof bad input failed silently. The command and the app now share one\nresolver, so they can't disagree.\n\n---\n\n## The specific gaps\n\n**1. `dcode config` could show a classifier model the app isn't using.**\nA blank `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_AUTO_CLASSIFIER_MODEL` means \"inherit the main\nagent model\" and deliberately outranks `config.toml`. The CLI resolved\noptions through the generic scalar path, which treats a blank env var as\nunset — so with a blank env var and a `config.toml` value set, the app\nuses your main model while `dcode config get models.auto_classifier`\nreported the config-file model. This option picks which model reviews\ngated actions, so the two surfaces disagreeing here is the worst case.\nBoth now call the same resolver\n(`resolve_auto_classifier_model_with_source`), and the source line\ncredits the blank env var that forced the inherit.\n\n**2. Tables that can hold credentials were printed raw, or rejected as\nunknown.**\n`[async_subagents]` headers, `[models.providers]`, and\n`[sandboxes.providers]` can carry `Authorization` tokens and constructor\nparams. They weren't in the manifest at all, so `dcode config` either\nsaid \"unknown option\" or printed the full table. They're now flagged\n`redacted`: presence and source are reported, the values never are.\n\n```\n$ dcode config get agents.async_subagents\nagents.async_subagents = configured  (config.toml)\n```\n\nRedaction is enforced in all three output paths (table display, `config\n--json` rows, and single-key JSON), so a new output path can't\naccidentally leak them.\n\n**3. Whole sections the app reads were missing from the manifest.**\n`[models.providers]`, `[sandboxes]`, `[agents]`, `[retries]`, and\n`[themes]` now show up in `dcode config list`. Three display settings\nthat were previously hardcoded one-off readers — cursor blink, terminal\nprogress, and message timestamps — are now manifest options with their\nown env vars (`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_CURSOR_BLINK`,\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_TERMINAL_PROGRESS`,\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SHOW_MESSAGE_TIMESTAMPS`), so they follow the same env\n→ config → default precedence as everything else. The four copy-pasted\nTOML readers in `app.py` collapsed into one shared\n`_load_bool_display_preference`, and a test pins each caller's fallback\nto the manifest default so they can't drift.\n\n**4. Two silent failure modes now log.**\n- A whitespace-only env var (`export DEEPAGENTS_CODE_THEME=\"$UNSET \"`)\nwas discarded with no trace — and for `empty_env_is_false` options it\nactually forced `False` over your `config.toml`. Both cases now log.\n- A scalar shadowing a table (`ui = \"dark\"` at the top level of\n`config.toml`) silently defaulted every option under `[ui]`. This now\nlogs once per path, since the manifest resolves ~100 options in one pass\nand per-option logging would print the same line ~100 times.\n\n**5. `dcode config` credited values the app refuses.**\nTwo new option kinds enforce the runtime's validation at read time:\n`NON_NEGATIVE_INT` rejects a negative retry count, `NON_EMPTY_STR`\nrejects a blank agent name. Both now correctly read `(unset)`.\n\n## Why one resolver\n\nThe root cause of gaps 1 and 5 was the CLI maintaining its own\nresolution logic that didn't know the runtime's override rules. Every\nfix above routes both surfaces through the manifest, so the CLI reports\nwhat the app does by construction rather than by convention. A\nmanifest-drift test rejects new hand-written readers (like the old\n`[ui]` loaders) so the manifest stays the single source.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T16:34:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/84eb09d8edaa52297ca3e2ad76a2c85a9adf4130/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132"}]},{"sha":"345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM0NTg1OWU4ZTEzZDViNDgzNDhlZmViZDBhNDhiZmI0ZDNmYmYxMzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T16:33:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T16:33:37Z"},"message":"fix(code): group resume trace rounds (#5593)\n\nDeep Agents Code now marks every approval-interrupt continuation as part\nof the same user turn, making long auto-approval sessions readable and\ngroupable in LangSmith.\n\n---\n\n### Before\n\nA single user prompt can pause many times while tools pass through\napproval checks. After each approval, dcode resumes the LangGraph\ncheckpoint with a new Agent Server request. LangSmith recorded every\nresume request as a separate root trace, so one turn with 30 approval\nchecks looked like 30 independent traces with nearly identical\nconversation inputs—even though the graph was advancing normally by one\nstep each time.\n\n### After\n\nThe initial run of a turn is unchanged and stays untagged. Every later\n`Command(resume=...)` request is tagged `dcode:resume` and reuses the\nturn's config, so it keeps the same `thread_id`, `turn_id`, and\n`turn_number` as the original run. LangSmith views and cost reports can\ntherefore filter and group those sibling roots as one logical user turn.\n\n`stream_trace_config(config, stream_input)` makes that decision in one\nplace; each call site passes its stream input and the helper tags only\n`Command` inputs.\n\nThis applies to interactive TUI runs, headless runs, and internal\n`/offload` resumes. It does not change approval or classifier decisions,\nmodel inputs, prompt caching, checkpoint frequency, or graph execution\nsemantics.\n\n### Scope and caveats\n\n- **`/offload` groups by `thread_id` only.** It builds a thread-only\nconfig instead of going through `build_stream_config`, so its rounds\ncarry no `turn_id`/`turn_number`. The tag is its only resume marker.\n- **The tag is inheritable.** LangGraph unions `tags` onto child\nconfigs, so pair it with an `is_root` filter to select resume roots\nalone.\n- **ACP is out of scope.** `deepagents_acp` resumes untagged; tagging\nbelongs in that package.\n- **Nothing in this repository reads `dcode:resume`.** The consumer is\nLangSmith, so the literal string is an external contract — renaming it\nbreaks saved views and filters. This is recorded next to the constant.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ed3785b9-7a7d-6eca-5293-24b8e524ca4d)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ed3785b9-7a7d-6eca-5293-24b8e524ca4d/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f30dc337ff97e44e50b731eebf0e064cfa64e1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2f30dc337ff97e44e50b731eebf0e064cfa64e1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhIlhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4rkQAImCzTvSbK27J0BOu4bz0mXM\ndTRLMMKcdxWulWLcVXsVlV3fHYTfaRh2/bJXda04+a2Sy17p4wRV6N0AIs8BTv7b\ngGgK/SX0DB2aW0H9U1y4ECshfUhWYez8KYtXLxFc0PPheyhvSDjxQTNHA9OmXOuR\nCGU2DjX2LVq3oCAjd6dXLsLpNTyic9+cxPP7u7IiJSViH86LYP2UQiKNxI6Ib+pr\n6JMHl8kF5zc/UogoI4QQQHHH92F8hicBcKlDeny/vZ3eZq//C46YFP2xp4iFlBFF\n7UQXwP7IopHzMg9qictQILuAUOEcctCEuZ1+AjWTZ9IFMG9wWzfCs4ndx4q88OgB\nP2hzk6m6Mh7ROMnNJa/eESGUdXYE5iikBcIx7L5LeypjiN05PbWj4qVv/jbcq2bM\n+83EEiZ1FDKfJlOq4vsYQgb/m8DqmlzmK7ucpsffgKiE58JyeoWvzPQe5/vDK7fJ\nle5P9bDREznbwE6a57VWgj13kLQNI+DY4uYgibFyiYzhSs12DFMbAvN9RrycnwT2\nlqmMk4qvx6GDhwvozeG7vrT7RfWo7kVtl5xwOS2oteoal7imndlslZ0JOsX4R0n6\njpp3h4pP1EBDRdAaWb4HiBFD37/hs7xxcEZSEJh02xpzE42/Rl6d0u0lXFeLzlqx\nUKY+paDJER4coMKHfLVP\n=bFlh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2f30dc337ff97e44e50b731eebf0e064cfa64e1c\nparent 7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787070817 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787070817 -0400\n\nfix(code): group resume trace rounds (#5593)\n\nDeep Agents Code now marks every approval-interrupt continuation as part\nof the same user turn, making long auto-approval sessions readable and\ngroupable in LangSmith.\n\n---\n\n### Before\n\nA single user prompt can pause many times while tools pass through\napproval checks. After each approval, dcode resumes the LangGraph\ncheckpoint with a new Agent Server request. LangSmith recorded every\nresume request as a separate root trace, so one turn with 30 approval\nchecks looked like 30 independent traces with nearly identical\nconversation inputs—even though the graph was advancing normally by one\nstep each time.\n\n### After\n\nThe initial run of a turn is unchanged and stays untagged. Every later\n`Command(resume=...)` request is tagged `dcode:resume` and reuses the\nturn's config, so it keeps the same `thread_id`, `turn_id`, and\n`turn_number` as the original run. LangSmith views and cost reports can\ntherefore filter and group those sibling roots as one logical user turn.\n\n`stream_trace_config(config, stream_input)` makes that decision in one\nplace; each call site passes its stream input and the helper tags only\n`Command` inputs.\n\nThis applies to interactive TUI runs, headless runs, and internal\n`/offload` resumes. It does not change approval or classifier decisions,\nmodel inputs, prompt caching, checkpoint frequency, or graph execution\nsemantics.\n\n### Scope and caveats\n\n- **`/offload` groups by `thread_id` only.** It builds a thread-only\nconfig instead of going through `build_stream_config`, so its rounds\ncarry no `turn_id`/`turn_number`. The tag is its only resume marker.\n- **The tag is inheritable.** LangGraph unions `tags` onto child\nconfigs, so pair it with an `is_root` filter to select resume roots\nalone.\n- **ACP is out of scope.** `deepagents_acp` resumes untagged; tagging\nbelongs in that package.\n- **Nothing in this repository reads `dcode:resume`.** The consumer is\nLangSmith, so the literal string is an external contract — renaming it\nbreaks saved views and filters. This is recorded next to the constant.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ed3785b9-7a7d-6eca-5293-24b8e524ca4d)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ed3785b9-7a7d-6eca-5293-24b8e524ca4d/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T16:33:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/345859e8e13d5b48348efebd0a48bfb4d3fbf132/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08"}]},{"sha":"7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdlNjQ1YzYxZjliYjhkMDU4Zjk4Yjk2Yjg1MzMxMzc2MGE5NmZjMDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","email":"248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-18T16:32:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T16:32:48Z"},"message":"chore(deps): raise dependency minimums for `deepagents-code` (#5600)\n\nRaises the LangChain-ecosystem dependency lower bounds (`langchain*`,\n`langgraph*`, `langsmith*`, `deepagents*`) for `deepagents-code` to the\nlatest compatible stable PyPI release, and regenerates every affected\n`uv.lock`. Upper bounds, extras, and markers are preserved; exact `==`\npins are left alone.\n\nRaised 6 minimum(s):\n\n| Manifest | Dependency | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langgraph-runtime-inmem` |\n`langgraph-runtime-inmem>=0.32.4,<1.0.0` →\n`langgraph-runtime-inmem>=0.32.5,<1.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-google-genai` |\n`langchain-google-genai>=4.3.3,<5.0.0` →\n`langchain-google-genai>=4.3.4,<5.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-openai` |\n`langchain-openai>=1.5.0,<2.0.0` → `langchain-openai>=1.5.1,<2.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langsmith` |\n`langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.18` → `langsmith[sandbox]>=0.11.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-aws` |\n`langchain-aws>=1.7.0,<2.0.0` → `langchain-aws>=1.7.2,<2.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-openrouter` |\n`langchain-openrouter>=0.2.7,<2.0.0` →\n`langchain-openrouter>=0.2.8,<2.0.0` |\n\nOpened automatically by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`. Review the\nraised bounds against any compatibility notes in the manifest comments\nbefore merging.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5daa96942aeff85397322aa75e00896cc46f5843","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5daa96942aeff85397322aa75e00896cc46f5843"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhIkwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnSIQACobYN2RXs0vxzBjY8EBgBrs\ne90bj6oPnRrwakqF1J6ODpu9fhgfDAXuis8mAjpdeKyLMsA41wxc8LHTYjg16EDk\nJPL2pFEAim2pkI3ciSn88c1+kTxUE4Tt+CfzoEvsQl5CpSUek11MpEGToBIdLMqt\nzF+m5CKQ0570MHlZSIhtMw1BqMxJk9zxRBQN02b8Og8/SXP8dBXHilwNNvyMVNHy\nEgfkWUmdM1/XleH3Q5pjDgYQjq1iCFPV8oYlCqIQlbUuqguCrLhZe5SmEZr2H9Kh\n/cedcyOUT+qkTjeJ3+GkjhsQq3B+Nwp7jjGSfFYf0vPZ539GmxuDG30T+A9UFBGF\nBJ6ixk1O2ODSl1D6hIHNj8nM9WoB4ZJGzRo866zZlOYGdr3IJlimocfot9O7H7iq\nciJcWMzSUUKVjrjwYJy6oNuFLaJ3Z418Gbpj09L2HBrAdd1Pt7guwsiMl5p30KH4\nm7xqiiGVXvnW97MM2kRD1KRcH4VAukppZVbJU2EKoo7xXxWtM8XYS5hXna73fxJE\ntWEn42GbV+ldgya1WIE9Y7pPDmPAQGM55aT2Cq0ZFkEGSljVgWEzUClln7zUZmSa\nAH7G6rbEbK3HxPWGyTUvDcgpsSWZ9uWHiblcEBgXQ99pkhMCJEkBFjF9ZGVlQKGT\ncQaCSERiMafIgdRPTIbc\n=D9du\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5daa96942aeff85397322aa75e00896cc46f5843\nparent 9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66\nauthor langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787070768 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787070768 -0400\n\nchore(deps): raise dependency minimums for `deepagents-code` (#5600)\n\nRaises the LangChain-ecosystem dependency lower bounds (`langchain*`,\n`langgraph*`, `langsmith*`, `deepagents*`) for `deepagents-code` to the\nlatest compatible stable PyPI release, and regenerates every affected\n`uv.lock`. Upper bounds, extras, and markers are preserved; exact `==`\npins are left alone.\n\nRaised 6 minimum(s):\n\n| Manifest | Dependency | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langgraph-runtime-inmem` |\n`langgraph-runtime-inmem>=0.32.4,<1.0.0` →\n`langgraph-runtime-inmem>=0.32.5,<1.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-google-genai` |\n`langchain-google-genai>=4.3.3,<5.0.0` →\n`langchain-google-genai>=4.3.4,<5.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-openai` |\n`langchain-openai>=1.5.0,<2.0.0` → `langchain-openai>=1.5.1,<2.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langsmith` |\n`langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.18` → `langsmith[sandbox]>=0.11.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-aws` |\n`langchain-aws>=1.7.0,<2.0.0` → `langchain-aws>=1.7.2,<2.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain-openrouter` |\n`langchain-openrouter>=0.2.7,<2.0.0` →\n`langchain-openrouter>=0.2.8,<2.0.0` |\n\nOpened automatically by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`. Review the\nraised bounds against any compatibility notes in the manifest comments\nbefore merging.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T16:32:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7e645c61f9bb8d058f98b96b853313760a96fc08/comments","author":{"login":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","id":248757908,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODtO-lA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2441712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/langchain-oss-automated-triage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66"}]},{"sha":"9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlhMWUwZWM0Mjk5NGJhMTVmMGVmZjZhNjFmYWE4ZjM3MDRmY2JjNjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T16:00:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T16:00:36Z"},"message":"chore(evals): drop langsmith upper-bound cap (#5598)\n\nCloses #5545\n\nThe evals package no longer caps langsmith below 0.11.0, which unblocks\nthe automated dependency-minimums workflow that was failing to\nregenerate the evals lockfile after deepagents-code raised its langsmith\nfloor to 0.11.0 (failed run:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32156544008).\n\n---\n\nThe evals package path-depends on `deepagents-code`, whose\n`langsmith[sandbox]>=0.11.0` floor made the evals `<0.11.0` cap\nunsatisfiable, so `uv lock` for `libs/evals` failed in the\ndependency-minimums workflow. Dropping the cap lets the lockfile resolve\nlangsmith 0.11.0. Verified with `uv lock --directory libs/evals --python\n3.12` (matching the lockfile-check invocation) and the evals unit test\nsuite passes against langsmith 0.11.0.","tree":{"sha":"13e034a23b6806bee5c2621cd2a761e7f019c3c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/13e034a23b6806bee5c2621cd2a761e7f019c3c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhIGkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ74QAAYi6PlvQ/R2tLh21ZM/r02T\nI0gH0Z0kwNr5jk1iW/7VV7mqRszI6qUuX5bRUy2TUCqVVgKK0rOcKkuS0IDjI8JR\ndV6nC9jgI/0tcVTNfA0306dZm+7UAErWPH4oUAigAgEj6hzdnB9n+hKIp+FD7MEw\nubZPay5GH5GEALnmsA9/Kn0CiU48jjXzIvkUryIZnR/DsnZMDNO5ly52/MER6Qhi\ngbpwlrrklDfefBc5cQN6icfo4X2g7PU+gCtuk77JvNN95wOlp98DdUxm2sM7kdA7\nUHzI9+SYOJqWO7KA9JmD/4c1AH6pUTPmILtBegX3OjLj61CUP+XP6Cd3j9g6JXCX\n5T7qWtadjR4Z09sl7s2wNLfVzqjb5d2GX1UUv9nt8xq2eIt1ZjPRXSi22WGrMIWj\nfOvIrKDRjpf4gftFdjfVbQlFwIbstTzx4gwhin2di5wGCSNm4EIGcZ0R6sD1LbAg\n0JneHJ59LgpQs6Mf4kpoX0aEn7852BRsZ8YmV4oThCvtsPxZBgYXy3/PKCgMKGoH\naOXqPFSN9C6I+j0YC754ANJl1LJgTkRHQLI20qei7OBvF0fFDulrWRGu9LHEdrHc\ndxkQrn1vSBdt+j0aNA+Jb8PvvW5rn/9ShBaHAlPHg8NLtrHYQUlLwbr8XAYLt4V0\nzSdRMQOFKkUrDsQDqsyl\n=eqI1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 13e034a23b6806bee5c2621cd2a761e7f019c3c9\nparent cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787068836 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787068836 -0400\n\nchore(evals): drop langsmith upper-bound cap (#5598)\n\nCloses #5545\n\nThe evals package no longer caps langsmith below 0.11.0, which unblocks\nthe automated dependency-minimums workflow that was failing to\nregenerate the evals lockfile after deepagents-code raised its langsmith\nfloor to 0.11.0 (failed run:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32156544008).\n\n---\n\nThe evals package path-depends on `deepagents-code`, whose\n`langsmith[sandbox]>=0.11.0` floor made the evals `<0.11.0` cap\nunsatisfiable, so `uv lock` for `libs/evals` failed in the\ndependency-minimums workflow. Dropping the cap lets the lockfile resolve\nlangsmith 0.11.0. Verified with `uv lock --directory libs/evals --python\n3.12` (matching the lockfile-check invocation) and the evals unit test\nsuite passes against langsmith 0.11.0.","verified_at":"2026-08-18T16:00:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a1e0ec42994ba15f0eff6a61faa8f3704fcbc66/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106"}]},{"sha":"cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNkNGMzOTkzZmFmOWFhYmZjNmJiNmMyMmJiNTZhNTdjMzM1NjMxMDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T15:45:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T15:45:37Z"},"message":"fix(code): resolve message pointer shapes per cell (#5592)\n\nTextual applies the pointer of a widget to all of the widget area. The\nmessage widgets set `pointer: text` in CSS. Therefore a short line\nshowed a text cursor across the empty part of its row.\n\nEach message widget now selects the shape from the cell below the mouse:\n\n- `pointer` on a link\n- `text` on rendered text\n- `default` on blank space\n\nThis changes seven widgets: `UserMessage`, `QueuedUserMessage`,\n`AssistantMessage`, `DiffMessage`, `ErrorMessage`, `AppMessage` and\n`SummarizationMessage`.\n\n---\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7d248a88-53b8-4a78-3271-a805cbf68cdb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"180653cb171c22042edbcc4fada6d23d6a5dfb04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/180653cb171c22042edbcc4fada6d23d6a5dfb04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhH4hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAqMQAIi2XLjkIO2XbjAky1JNc5ZH\nW2e1htpMr7MpwCUIAmW4cHZ4H6c1/LWB4q9z86PFXOdrziWbMY3oog6JBymONZn2\nzGNbnEa7l6pe8rM0uhUGaTgfhw8Bv3zIUn6zuStkWYrzQILeH9jhVkxL9QpICglX\nWzMrTPW+MLqOGQnF3iWx0rD1BGh2Z0sArMA0SXK7uaSJxqB4sl5lVr5EOOkl3EO9\nvvEOp8D4TmfdJe+7jnK5lJ7AUNSmYqLreB7M/hBUTOC6BwQhzP4BAZZBk3r/iOij\nyrYSTBfXS5DWdY8H3Mjp9LqWgEAKIG8udprZRL2zd+8VAVTq63qGei+jlqIiwMrB\nbQRCVUsf1iJX1E8WCoieYT0E0ORhZYDaj4bNXGXFHcmK8FivZzl8/88Vqr3/E2GA\nVSwg95Lou3lDkqFHKyfOFyArbi0hx/SAD+6vJClQ5P0yEx3d724Iaxaybp1f9SfE\nYH2RErcn2n67z0LC7W0dQXGX8AZXCraM8DuWHzjLBuh9LlpaW4xgcxhHJqelMYGh\n4RJAbZTabNDXlzozssxhhlq1/v+0ybetEDuTNqzNqCHhxiZVSa3RsqbnkuRtxl8O\nbU0OG8QFtoEQbiExqe5DFVNqtifQX1L9cv/wk9mIsmd8ode4iyj5AXXprnIiBCDi\nWNxYjZqxoHRP319mzjwu\n=KDHY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 180653cb171c22042edbcc4fada6d23d6a5dfb04\nparent b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787067937 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787067937 -0400\n\nfix(code): resolve message pointer shapes per cell (#5592)\n\nTextual applies the pointer of a widget to all of the widget area. The\nmessage widgets set `pointer: text` in CSS. Therefore a short line\nshowed a text cursor across the empty part of its row.\n\nEach message widget now selects the shape from the cell below the mouse:\n\n- `pointer` on a link\n- `text` on rendered text\n- `default` on blank space\n\nThis changes seven widgets: `UserMessage`, `QueuedUserMessage`,\n`AssistantMessage`, `DiffMessage`, `ErrorMessage`, `AppMessage` and\n`SummarizationMessage`.\n\n---\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7d248a88-53b8-4a78-3271-a805cbf68cdb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T15:45:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cd4c3993faf9aabfc6bb6c22bb56a57c33563106/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b"}]},{"sha":"b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIzMjA5N2JkOTBmZGIxYmM2ZTY3Yjc0MzQ2MzEzYmExODk5MTUyMGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T15:31:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T15:31:56Z"},"message":"ci(infra): include run URL in SDK pin bump dispatch notice (#5595)\n\nWhen `release.yml` publishes `deepagents` to PyPI, its\n`bump-code-sdk-pin` job dispatches `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` and prints a\nnotice. The notice now includes a link to the dispatched run.\n\nBefore:\n\n::notice::Dispatched bump_code_sdk_pin.yml after publishing\ndeepagents==0.7.7.\n\nAfter:\n\n::notice::Dispatched bump_code_sdk_pin.yml after publishing\ndeepagents==0.7.7:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32152501551\n\n---\n\n`gh workflow run` prints no run ID and returns before the run exists. So\nthere is no URL to print at dispatch time.\n\nThe step now records the time, dispatches the workflow, then polls `gh\nrun list` for the newest `workflow_dispatch` run of\n`bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`. It tries six times, five seconds apart. A\n`--created \">=<dispatch time>\"` filter makes the poll ignore older runs\nof the same workflow. Without the filter, the poll would match the\nprevious run at once while the new run is still starting.\n\nIf the poll finds no run after about 30 seconds, the notice falls back\nto the workflow page URL\n(`.../actions/workflows/bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`). That page lists the\nnewest run at the top, so the link stays useful.\n\nThe lookup uses the Org Membership App token, whose `actions: write`\ngrant also covers reading runs. The step keeps `continue-on-error: true`\nand `|| true` on the list call, so a lookup failure still cannot fail\nthe release run.","tree":{"sha":"a76196e50fa9b686fa5804d1495e2964d6f9eb78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a76196e50fa9b686fa5804d1495e2964d6f9eb78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhHrsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATVUQAGC40aWm+ePEvLgTDClxyVrr\nzp0JVbe2j9pmI7DAP5+7P/V/FMoE35qQxkCVgM1k9qVq80x5YxWzSLVQ+XJBKSR4\n3dmHwX8cgnUqKAar/VcarjKu2SPTBv3ANJklojr5VUW1Ou9usVqiN89mF+MSsKgS\nunWAD5SSctWo67QgKV8v7egHiDUGIlK2fh/Q9fWAcK+3i19Xk6aSuqAeVtuHqVUL\n63qMH1H+5mlwKdh5e9PbAkxuKGwYI8PUhdt9w10kJbaFoHygDgb9a4CI2E++554C\nqn3KNjDcT4IP8NIgdpLrkEjbCo2vWX3LB1AO/UGDSS2L4niwUPG0tu5aYIYCVHX6\nb40BfVZT4G4nK6BYpkzKgMArcdBHr/W1VMoPxS9aRjv6drwKbNwGjr461kAIzFZ6\npO3dCh4y0H+gQ6bxiE7cOjXZzqNDTwlJFCMCbEH4rKS19waeyxcSvK6/J7yuXG90\nY8pXl1byDuYSEVdgAzqj8Oy+og/r/eZmbZKjtPRExok/gTioryFT644QRzNekc79\niE5z9Qxnsc27ZTMBxr4/PNSsQv+iuP9+rHufKIyGunUZNh1xUckASuM/mVhhFNHd\nuRdMp2t7D7FprPnHCuen+/HaCq+tuEOh0rWJ3a/QO1n9qvnD0h21U6855u4rJTdF\nZ8aFbcnpomteU/kwa+wU\n=mjQ6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a76196e50fa9b686fa5804d1495e2964d6f9eb78\nparent 1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787067116 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787067116 -0400\n\nci(infra): include run URL in SDK pin bump dispatch notice (#5595)\n\nWhen `release.yml` publishes `deepagents` to PyPI, its\n`bump-code-sdk-pin` job dispatches `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` and prints a\nnotice. The notice now includes a link to the dispatched run.\n\nBefore:\n\n::notice::Dispatched bump_code_sdk_pin.yml after publishing\ndeepagents==0.7.7.\n\nAfter:\n\n::notice::Dispatched bump_code_sdk_pin.yml after publishing\ndeepagents==0.7.7:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32152501551\n\n---\n\n`gh workflow run` prints no run ID and returns before the run exists. So\nthere is no URL to print at dispatch time.\n\nThe step now records the time, dispatches the workflow, then polls `gh\nrun list` for the newest `workflow_dispatch` run of\n`bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`. It tries six times, five seconds apart. A\n`--created \">=<dispatch time>\"` filter makes the poll ignore older runs\nof the same workflow. Without the filter, the poll would match the\nprevious run at once while the new run is still starting.\n\nIf the poll finds no run after about 30 seconds, the notice falls back\nto the workflow page URL\n(`.../actions/workflows/bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`). That page lists the\nnewest run at the top, so the link stays useful.\n\nThe lookup uses the Org Membership App token, whose `actions: write`\ngrant also covers reading runs. The step keeps `continue-on-error: true`\nand `|| true` on the list call, so a lookup failure still cannot fail\nthe release run.","verified_at":"2026-08-18T15:31:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b32097bd90fdb1bc6e67b74346313ba18991520b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77"}]},{"sha":"1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFlMjBmNTkyYjU0Yzg5ZWZlZjZiMGE5OGM3ZWJjM2U5MGZlZmJmNzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T15:31:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T15:31:14Z"},"message":"fix(infra): fall back to head commit subject when release-please run `display_title` is the workflow name (#5596)\n\nWhen a release finishes, an automated workflow posts a comment on the\nrelease pull request with the result. That comment did not post for a\nrecent release. This change fixes the cause.\n\n---\n\n**Background**\n\nEach release runs in two steps:\n\n1. The release-please workflow merges the release pull request and\nstarts the publish jobs.\n2. The release-comment workflow then posts the publish result as a\ncomment on the merged pull request.\n\nThe second workflow must find the release pull request that caused the\nrun. To do this, it reads the run's title. A release run has a title\nlike `release(deepagents): 0.7.7 (#5498)`. Runs that are not releases\nhave different titles and are skipped.\n\n**Problem**\n\nGitHub sometimes returns the workflow's name (`⚠️ (Automated) Release\nPlease`) as the run title instead of the title shown above. This\nhappened for the `deepagents 0.7.7` release ([run\n32152816232](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32152816232)).\nThe title check did not match, so the workflow stopped and no result\ncomment was posted.\n\n**Fix**\n\nThe run title normally comes from the message of the commit that started\nthe run. When the title check fails and the returned title is exactly\nthe workflow's name, the workflow now reads that commit message and\nchecks it instead. Non-release runs are still skipped, because their\ncommit messages do not have the release format.\n\nThe fix also applies to manually started runs, which read the same title\nfield.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Checked that the workflow file parses and the shell script has valid\nsyntax.\n- Tested the title check with four cases: a normal release run\n(matched), a non-release run (skipped), the broken title with a release\ncommit message (matched through the fallback), and the broken title with\na non-release commit message (still skipped).\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"cdcdc6ccae0fd7fba5a43552607acf97795ccedc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cdcdc6ccae0fd7fba5a43552607acf97795ccedc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhHrCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkHUQAJQFC8dco/Lje+DDXvbJH1VI\ni3/ErBs8+5TZxe2mfjCQKCtVnTD6YJcI8s5KQ2GKJ7F3arJuRC5I6Xlv1GQ5Ta2N\nBEyArPxTbi90Bd4ckBskgD+qLfOeBnWYHdEV5PITMf4VU6attumpPGyCPgIDgI13\nluVeZSsw9gdLIf9J/xa9nUy0s8yXYG1RRLdvr16/E3JD1y35Js6BhR1pMnfG9F0U\nqPPqFR3m+X/8Sq0dYGE0u81ARzOY21fOPCxIdbUbLmaFCGIqzCDJsOJrL4Aos0KE\nnIdFQlDGZdB2YdjjtI59jE277MGd8n5vfZvSF3aNk8pHTHMxvPOJUX2+Ngy38igY\nS1IW6w7Pc5eVuWS9bfH3IT8Y582sE4HZhYRHWMy1ZpPzw+7Y++pwO5sMjLfXvclY\njKBa+MhgKi2RWCJrmWetljEoKuqN5fUpJtn78d7kAzzoMUrdMykG5Skaokg9hHUk\nrHzuhYUc3wKa9gvJznyB32DltViVCiMYj5BhedMF6tP0xa2GulA03/xPjm1AIixS\n3GkTnfrKhM5lVF+hXaSKyXW4ARjg/aC8kaio35KXVMSZ7fscGDJMnDNfOxmIGOPA\nRsrg7QCkuktM8NDI9ORo0MI6rr9FemWjXOVcf2VinE6NKYRf3n2VxEvpHycXocRt\nZsnoWcs3/RXGkP5pqvHl\n=jTPZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cdcdc6ccae0fd7fba5a43552607acf97795ccedc\nparent 8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787067074 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787067074 -0400\n\nfix(infra): fall back to head commit subject when release-please run `display_title` is the workflow name (#5596)\n\nWhen a release finishes, an automated workflow posts a comment on the\nrelease pull request with the result. That comment did not post for a\nrecent release. This change fixes the cause.\n\n---\n\n**Background**\n\nEach release runs in two steps:\n\n1. The release-please workflow merges the release pull request and\nstarts the publish jobs.\n2. The release-comment workflow then posts the publish result as a\ncomment on the merged pull request.\n\nThe second workflow must find the release pull request that caused the\nrun. To do this, it reads the run's title. A release run has a title\nlike `release(deepagents): 0.7.7 (#5498)`. Runs that are not releases\nhave different titles and are skipped.\n\n**Problem**\n\nGitHub sometimes returns the workflow's name (`⚠️ (Automated) Release\nPlease`) as the run title instead of the title shown above. This\nhappened for the `deepagents 0.7.7` release ([run\n32152816232](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/32152816232)).\nThe title check did not match, so the workflow stopped and no result\ncomment was posted.\n\n**Fix**\n\nThe run title normally comes from the message of the commit that started\nthe run. When the title check fails and the returned title is exactly\nthe workflow's name, the workflow now reads that commit message and\nchecks it instead. Non-release runs are still skipped, because their\ncommit messages do not have the release format.\n\nThe fix also applies to manually started runs, which read the same title\nfield.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Checked that the workflow file parses and the shell script has valid\nsyntax.\n- Tested the title check with four cases: a normal release run\n(matched), a non-release run (skipped), the broken title with a release\ncommit message (matched through the fallback), and the broken title with\na non-release commit message (still skipped).\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T15:31:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1e20f592b54c89efef6b0a98c7ebc3e90fefbf77/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f"}]},{"sha":"8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhiZTlhZDAyZWQzYzVkZGQ5MDhjMjM3ZWFkMDk5NDk2YTIxY2I4N2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","email":"248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-18T15:14:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T15:14:35Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump `deepagents` pin in `deepagents-code` to `0.7.7` (#5594)\n\nBumps the exact `deepagents` pin in `libs/code/pyproject.toml` from\n`0.7.6` to `0.7.7` (current workspace SDK version) and regenerates\n`libs/code/uv.lock`.\n\nOpened automatically by `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` after a commit on `main`\nchanged the SDK version. Merge this before the next `deepagents-code`\nrelease so the SDK pin check goes green.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"25d15d3ec2d25200753f2a0b62a27a5327afecd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/25d15d3ec2d25200753f2a0b62a27a5327afecd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhHbbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADJ8QAAULyk8U18fWSGmY4gjMfnWz\n6GLkuqYAeUCesCj2mTz/i1bjcKDVlNUmXhD5WwAgGLFOcCTt9Xsm1977YixJ0xeZ\nq1UWmpUxiMZzJCSZt9VszkzO6BLoRxzymSLgtUuDYQ0cXurHsTLkcfIqWpXshLLG\nv7To71s2Th880sJycOmuTzsvItjnq5XVkd+szAmy/NdwSvPN5tQ8eqy1Tgb7tUqn\nwurgaNgHmhFxBHN7kp2Vz39Wnx94bMM2Jori0+UCFKxNWQqW2zZ6DdwxT/tN4i+O\nS9kZcVpb1hBBpFp0Kp8WdBzRoftbuplnHy4iEcR7E/5PBmulyZktBHjuNqnxd0xG\nQJlHjiwFnZGPCWQkWPCdbI1tZY1Grt7+1t5qPWB9lJy147OE3huXdH0LdzdB7JCp\na7bgfJTAxn6xOUBtx4xmvLvQEhf/LUYMOvvTekjcZBaduOue0iX+LLKD7BvTOAOu\nxxDKRmsWBj/CHN0ooHnWVg73crUTdWQyBpDuiHxuf+hUEIhKz2H/ICQlol/legkI\nEsQZIhFSb1ZbkJvhUiKBYFV9bXcDr9CvT7H5dKHhrhc/Wz85H8Ac9NB3ufpjYKr9\nHjMcqvuFtLT3jKD+ywe5Y7XRn3/vIawnc2Wv6TZ4kgwrCKLpg1FJJSW62sqxPpqX\n8e/eSZUL3iQJL+fJP/7I\n=Pv6L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 25d15d3ec2d25200753f2a0b62a27a5327afecd6\nparent 42ed9406f08dfec11369631011405c1dc650293a\nauthor langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787066075 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787066075 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump `deepagents` pin in `deepagents-code` to `0.7.7` (#5594)\n\nBumps the exact `deepagents` pin in `libs/code/pyproject.toml` from\n`0.7.6` to `0.7.7` (current workspace SDK version) and regenerates\n`libs/code/uv.lock`.\n\nOpened automatically by `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` after a commit on `main`\nchanged the SDK version. Merge this before the next `deepagents-code`\nrelease so the SDK pin check goes green.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T15:14:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8be9ad02ed3c5ddd908c237ead099496a21cb87f/comments","author":{"login":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","id":248757908,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODtO-lA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2441712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/langchain-oss-automated-triage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-os